(```) Tj
T*
(Before we answer the questions listed above, let’s look at how we create layers of abstractions) Tj
T*
(for the user to hide the internal complexity of a blob store. These abstraction layers help us) Tj
T*
(make design-related decisions as well.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(There are three layers of abstractions:) Tj
T*
(1. User account: Users uniquely get identified on this layer through their account_ID. Blobs) Tj
T*
(uploaded by users are maintained in their containers.) Tj
T*
(2. Container: Each user has a set of containers that are all uniquely identified by a) Tj
T*
(container_ID. These containers contain blobs.) Tj
T*
(3. Blob: This layer contains information about blobs that are uniquely identified by their) Tj
T*
(blob_ID. This layer maintains information about the metadata of blobs that’s vital for) Tj
T*
(achieving the availability and reliability of the system.) Tj
T*
(We can take routing, storage, and sharding decisions on the basis of these layers. The table) Tj
T*
(below summarizes these layers.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
