T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(Here, we utilize indexing to sort and categorize the blobs. We should do this beforehand, while) Tj
T*
(we store the blobs. Otherwise, it becomes challenging at the time of returning the list to the) Tj
T*
(user. There could be millions or billions of blobs and we can’t sort them quickly when the list) Tj
T*
(request is received.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For pagination, we need a continuation token as a starting point for the part of the list) Tj
T*
(that’s returned next. A continuation token is a string token that’s included in the response of) Tj
T*
(a query if the total number of queried results exceeds the maximum number of results that we) Tj
T*
(can return at once. As a result, it serves as a pointer, allowing the re-query to pick up where) Tj
T*
(we left off.) Tj
T*
(## Replication) Tj
T*
(Replication is carried out on two levels to support availability and strong consistency. To) Tj
T*
(keep the data strongly consistent, we synchronously replicate data among the nodes that are) Tj
T*
(used to serve the read requests, right after performing the write operation. To achieve) Tj
T*
(availability, we can replicate data to different regions or data centers after performing the) Tj
T*
(write operation. We don’t serve the read request from the other data center or regions until we) Tj
T*
(have not replicated data there.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(These are the two levels of replication:) Tj
T*
(- Synchronous replication within a storage cluster.) Tj
T*
(- Asynchronous replication across data centers and regions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Synchronous replication within a storage cluster) Tj
T*
(A storage cluster is made up of N racks of storage nodes, each of which is configured as a) Tj
T*
(fault domain with redundant networking and power.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We ensure that every data written into a storage cluster is kept durable within that storage) Tj
T*
(cluster. The master node maintains enough data replicas across the nodes in distinct fault) Tj
T*
(domains to ensure data durability inside the cluster in the event of a disk, node, or rack) Tj
T*
(failure.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: This intra-cluster replication is done on the critical path of the client’s write) Tj
T*
(requests.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Success can be returned to the client once a write has been synchronously replicated inside) Tj
T*
(that storage cluster. This allows for quick writes because:) Tj
T*
(- We replicate data within a storage cluster where all the nodes are nearby, thus reducing the) Tj
T*
(latency.) Tj
T*
(- We use in-lined data copying where we use redundant network paths to copy data to all the) Tj
T*
(replicas in parallel.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This replication technique helps maintain data consistency and availability inside the storage) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
