T*
(To stream a file, we need to define how many Bytes are allowed to be read at one time. Let’s) Tj
T*
(say we read X number of Bytes each time. The first time we read the first X Bytes starting from) Tj
T*
(the 0th Byte \(0 to X-1\) and the next time, we read the next X Bytes \(X to 2X−1\).) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question) Tj
T*
(How do we know which Bytes we have read first and which Bytes we have to read next?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(We can use an offset value to keep track of the Byte from which we need to start reading again.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
