(## Detailed design) Tj
T*
(We start this section by identifying the key components that we need to complete our blob store) Tj
T*
(design. Then, we look at how these components connect to fulfill our functional requirements.) Tj
T*
(### Components) Tj
T*
(Here is a list of components that we use in the blob store design:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Client: This is a user or program that performs any of the API functions that are specified.) Tj
T*
(- Rate limiter: A rate limiter limits the number of requests based on the user’s subscription) Tj
T*
(or limits the number of requests from the same IP address at the same time. It doesn’t allow) Tj
T*
(users to exceed the predefined limit.) Tj
T*
(- Load balancer: A load balancer distributes incoming network traffic among a group of servers.) Tj
T*
(It’s also used to reroute requests to different regions depending on the location of the user,) Tj
T*
(different data centers within the same region, or different servers within the same data) Tj
T*
(center. DNS load balancing can be used to reroute the requests among different regions based on) Tj
T*
(the location of the user.) Tj
T*
(- Front-end servers: Front-end servers forward the users’ requests for adding or deleting data) Tj
T*
(to the appropriate storage servers.) Tj
T*
(- Data nodes: Data nodes hold the actual blob data. It’s also possible that they contain a part) Tj
T*
(of the blob’s data. Blobs are split into small, fixed-size pieces called chunks. A data node) Tj
T*
(can accommodate all of the chunks of a blob or at least some of them.) Tj
T*
(- Master node: A master node is the core component that manages all data nodes. It stores) Tj
T*
(information about storage paths and the access privileges of blobs. There are two types of) Tj
T*
(access privileges: private and public. A private access privilege means that the blob is only) Tj
T*
(accessible by the account containing that blob. A public access privilege means that anyone can) Tj
T*
(access that blob.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: Each of the data nodes in the cluster send the master node a heartbeat and a chunk report) Tj
T*
(regularly. The presence of a heartbeat indicates that the data node is operational. A chunk) Tj
T*
(report lists all the chunks on a data node. If a data node fails to send a heartbeat, the) Tj
T*
(master node considers that node dead and then processes the user requests on the replica nodes.) Tj
T*
(The master node maintains a log of pending operations that should be replayed on the dead data) Tj
T*
(node when it recovers.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(- Metadata storage: Metadata storage is a distributed database that’s used by the master node) Tj
T*
(to store all the metadata. Metadata consists of account metadata, container metadata, and blob) Tj
T*
(metadata.) Tj
T*
( - Account metadata contains the account information for each user and the containers held by) Tj
T*
ET
