(### Workflow) Tj
T*
(We describe the workflow based on the basic operations we can perform on a blob store. We) Tj
T*
(assume that the user has successfully logged in and a container has already been created. A) Tj
T*
(unique ID is assigned to each user and container. The user performs the following operations in) Tj
T*
(a specific container.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(**Write a blob**) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. The client generates the upload blob request. If the client’s request successfully passes) Tj
T*
(through the rate limiter, the load balancer forwards the client’s request to one of the front-) Tj
T*
(end servers. The front-end server then requests the master node for the data nodes it should) Tj
T*
(contact to store the blob.) Tj
T*
(2. The master node assigns the blob a unique ID using a unique ID generator system. It then) Tj
T*
(splits the large-size blob into smaller, fixed-size chunks and assigns each chunk a data node) Tj
T*
(where that chunk is eventually stored. The master node determines the amount of storage space) Tj
T*
(that’s available on the data nodes using a free-space management system.) Tj
T*
(3. After determining the mapping of chunks to data nodes, the front-end servers write the) Tj
T*
(chunks to the assigned data nodes.) Tj
T*
(4. We replicate each chunk for redundancy purposes. All choices regarding chunk replication are) Tj
T*
(made at the master node. Hence, the master node also allocates the storage and data nodes for) Tj
T*
(storing replicas.) Tj
T*
(5. The master node stores the blob metadata in the metadata storage. We discuss the blob’s) Tj
T*
(metadata schema in detail in the next lesson.) Tj
T*
(6. After writing the blob, a fully qualified path of the blob is returned to the client. The) Tj
T*
(path consists of the user ID, container ID where the user has added the blob, the blob ID, and) Tj
T*
(the access level of the blob.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question) Tj
T*
(What does the master node do if a user concurrently writes two blobs with the same name inside) Tj
T*
(the same container?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(The master node serializes such operations and assigns a version number to the blob that’s) Tj
T*
(uploaded later.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(**Reading a blob**) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. When a read request for a blob reaches the front-end server, it asks the master node for) Tj
T*
(that blob’s metadata.) Tj
T*
(2. The master node first checks whether that blob is private or public, based on the path of) Tj
T*
(the blob and whether we’re authorized to transfer that blob or not.) Tj
T*
(3. After authorizing the blob, the master node looks for the chunks for that blob in the) Tj
T*
(metadata and looks at their mappings to data nodes. The master node returns the chunks and) Tj
T*
ET
