(failure, we start a new instance of the master node, initializing it from the saved state.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Natural disasters include floods, earthquakes, wildfires, tornadoes, nuclear reactor meltdowns,) Tj
T*
(and so on.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(## Durability) Tj
T*
(The replication and monitoring services ensure the durability of the data. The data, once) Tj
T*
(uploaded, is synchronously replicated within a storage cluster. If data loss occurs at one) Tj
T*
(node, we can recover the data from the other nodes. The monitoring service monitors the storage) Tj
T*
(disks. If any disk fails, the monitoring service alerts the administrators to change the disk) Tj
T*
(and sends messages to the master node to copy the content on that disk on to the other) Tj
T*
(available disk or the newly added disk. The master node then updates the mapping accordingly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Guarantees provided by the blob store]\(./blob.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Scalability) Tj
T*
(The partitioning and splitting of blobs into small-sized chunks helps us scale for billions of) Tj
T*
(blob requests. Blobs are partitioned into separate ranges and served by different partition) Tj
T*
(servers. The partition mappings specify which partition server will serve which particular blob) Tj
T*
(range requests. Partitioning also provides automatic load balancing between partition servers) Tj
T*
(to fulfill the blobs’ traffic needs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Our system is horizontally scalable for storage. As need for storage arises, we add more data) Tj
T*
(nodes. At some point, though, our master node can become a bottleneck. A single master node can) Tj
T*
(handle 10,000 queries per second \(QPS\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question) Tj
T*
(How can we further scale when our master server hits its limits and we can’t improve its) Tj
T*
(computational abilities by vertical scaling?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(We can make two independent instances of our system. Each instance will have its own master) Tj
T*
(node and a set of data nodes. Deployment of a system similar to ours has been shown to scale up) Tj
T*
(to a few petabytes. Therefore, making additional instances can help us scale further.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For further scaling inside a single instance, we need a new, more complicated design.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Windows Azure Storage: A Highly Available Cloud Storage Service with Strong Consistency.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Throughput) Tj
T*
(We save chunks of a blob on different data nodes that distribute the requests for a blob to) Tj
T*
(multiple machines. Parallel fetching of chunks from multiple data nodes helps us achieve high) Tj
T*
(throughput.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Additionally, caching at different layers— the client side, front-end servers, and the master) Tj
T*
(node—improves our throughput and reduces latency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Reliability) Tj
T*
(We achieve reliability through our monitoring techniques. For example, the heartbeat protocol) Tj
T*
(keeps the master node updated on the status of data nodes. This enables the master node to) Tj
T*
(request data from reliable nodes only. Furthermore, it takes necessary precautions to ensure) Tj
T*
(reliable service. For example, the failure of a node triggers the master node to request an) Tj
T*
(additional replica node.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
