(## Blob Store/Requirements of a Blob Store's Design/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Requirements of a Blob Store's Design) Tj
T*
(## Requirements) Tj
T*
(Let’s understand the functional and non-functional requirements below:) Tj
T*
(### Functional requirements) Tj
T*
(Here are the functional requirements of the design of a blob store:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Create a container: The users should be able to create containers in order to group blobs.) Tj
T*
(For example, if an application wants to store user-specific data, it should be able to store) Tj
T*
(blobs for different user accounts in different containers. Additionally, a user may want to) Tj
T*
(group video blobs and separate them from a group of image blobs. A single blob store user can) Tj
T*
(create many containers, and each container can have many blobs, as shown in the following) Tj
T*
(illustration. For the sake of simplicity, we assume that we can’t create a container inside a) Tj
T*
(container.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(A container is like a folder in a file system used to group blobs. Don’t mix up this container) Tj
T*
(with a Docker container.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Multiple containers associated with a single storage account, and multiple blobs inside a) Tj
T*
(single container]\(./blob.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Put data: The blob store should allow users to upload blobs to the created containers.) Tj
T*
(- Get data: The system should generate a URL for the uploaded blob, so that the user can access) Tj
T*
(that blob later through this URL.) Tj
T*
(- Delete data: The users should be able to delete a blob. If the user wants to keep the data) Tj
T*
(for a specified period of time \(retention time\), our system should support this functionality.) Tj
T*
(- List blobs: The user should be able to get a list of blobs inside a specific container.) Tj
T*
(- Delete a container: The users should be able to delete a container and all the blobs inside) Tj
T*
(it.) Tj
T*
(- List containers: The system should allow the users to list all the containers under a) Tj
T*
(specific account.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Functional requirements of a blob store]\(./f.jpg\)) Tj
T*
(### Non-functional requirements) Tj
T*
(Here are the non-functional requirements of a blob store system:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Availability: Our system should be highly available.) Tj
T*
(- Durability: The data, once uploaded, shouldn’t be lost unless users explicitly delete that) Tj
T*
(data.) Tj
T*
(- Scalability: The system should be capable of handling billions of blobs.) Tj
T*
(- Throughput: For transferring gigabytes of data, we should ensure a high data throughput.) Tj
T*
(- Reliability: Since failures are a norm in distributed systems, our design should detect and) Tj
T*
(recover from failures promptly.) Tj
T*
(- Consistency: The system should be strongly consistent. Different users should see the same) Tj
T*
(view of a blob.) Tj
T*
([The non-functional requirements of a blob store]\(./nf.jpg\)) Tj
T*
ET
