(## Blob Store/System Design A Blob Store/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# System Design: A Blob Store) Tj
T*
(## What is a blob store?) Tj
T*
(Blob store is a storage solution for unstructured data. We can store photos, audio, videos,) Tj
T*
(binary executable codes, or other multimedia items in a blob store. Every type of data is) Tj
T*
(stored as a blob. It follows a flat data organization pattern where there are no hierarchies,) Tj
T*
(that is, directories, sub-directories, and so on.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Mostly, it’s used by applications with a particular business requirement called write once,) Tj
T*
(read many \(WORM\), which states that data can only be written once and that no one can change) Tj
T*
(it. Just like in Microsoft Azure, the blobs are created once and read many times. Additionally,) Tj
T*
(these blobs can’t be deleted until a specified interval, and they also can’t be modified to) Tj
T*
(protect critical data.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(A blob \(binary large object\) consists of a collection of binary data stored as a single unit.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: It isn’t necessary for all applications to have this WORM requirement. However, we are) Tj
T*
(assuming that the blobs that are written can’t be modified. Instead of modifying, we can upload) Tj
T*
(a new version of a blob if needed.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(## Why do we use a blob store?) Tj
T*
(Blob store is an important component of many data-intensive applications, such as YouTube,) Tj
T*
(Netflix, Facebook, and so on. The table below displays the blob storage used by some of the) Tj
T*
(most well-known applications. These applications generate a huge amount of unstructured data) Tj
T*
(every day. They require a storage solution that is easily scalable, reliable, and highly) Tj
T*
(available, so that they can store large media files. Since the amount of data continuously) Tj
T*
(increases, these applications need to store an unlimited number of blobs. According to some) Tj
T*
(estimates, YouTube requires more than a petabyte of additional storage per day. In a system) Tj
T*
(like YouTube, a video is stored in multiple resolutions. Additionally, the video in all) Tj
T*
(resolutions is replicated many times across different data centers and regions for availability) Tj
T*
ET
