(## The bottom-up approach for modern system design) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(System design problems usually have some similarities, though specific details are often) Tj
T*
(unique. We have extracted these similarities across design problems as the basic building) Tj
T*
(blocks we’ll be covering. One example of a building block is a load-balancing component, which) Tj
T*
(we’ll probably use in every design problem in one way or the other.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The purpose of separating the building blocks is to thoroughly discuss their design just once.) Tj
