(the second phase, we’ll explore the workflow by explaining how each component interacts with) Tj
T*
(others to develop a fully functional CDN. Let’s dive in.) Tj
T*
(### CDN components) Tj
T*
(The following components comprise a CDN:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Clients: End users use various clients, like browsers, smartphones, and other devices, to) Tj
T*
(request content from the CDN.) Tj
T*
(- Routing system: The routing system directs clients to the nearest CDN facility. To do that) Tj
T*
(effectively, this component receives input from various systems to understand where content is) Tj
T*
(placed, how many requests are made for particular content, the load a particular set of servers) Tj
T*
(is handling, and the URI \(Uniform Resource Identifier\) namespace of various contents. In the) Tj
T*
