(next lesson, we’ll discuss different routing mechanisms to forward users to the nearest CDN) Tj
T*
(facility.) Tj
T*
(- Scrubber servers: Scrubber servers are used to separate the good traffic from malicious) Tj
T*
(traffic and protect against well-known attacks, like DDoS. Scrubber servers are generally used) Tj
T*
(only when an attack is detected. In that case, the traffic is scrubbed or cleaned and then) Tj
T*
(routed to the target destination.) Tj
T*
(- Proxy servers: The proxy or edge proxy servers serve the content from RAM to the users. Proxy) Tj
T*
(servers store hot data in RAM, though they can store cold data in SSD or hard drive as well.) Tj
T*
(These servers also provide accounting information and receive content from the distribution) Tj
T*
(system.) Tj
T*
(- Distribution system: The distribution system is responsible for distributing content to all) Tj
T*
(the edge proxy servers to different CDN facilities. This system uses the Internet and) Tj
T*
(intelligent broadcast-like approaches to distribute content across the active edge proxy) Tj
T*
(servers.) Tj
T*
(- Origin servers: The CDN infrastructure facilitates users with data received from the origin) Tj
T*
(servers. The origin servers serve any unavailable data at the CDN to clients. Origin servers) Tj
T*
(will use appropriate stores to keep content and other mapping metadata. Though, we won’t) Tj
T*
(discuss the internal architecture of origin infrastructure here.) Tj
T*
(- Management system: The management systems are important in CDNs from a business and) Tj
T*
(managerial aspect where resource usage and statistics are constantly observed. This component) Tj
T*
(measures important metrics, like latency, downtime, packet loss, server load, and so on. For) Tj
T*
(third-party CDNs, accounting information can also be used for billing purposes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([CDN components]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Workflow) Tj
T*
(The workflow for the abstract design is given below:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. The origin servers provide the URI namespace delegation of all objects cached in the CDN to) Tj
T*
(the request routing system.) Tj
T*
(2. The origin server publishes the content to the distribution system responsible for data) Tj
T*
(distribution across the active edge proxy servers.) Tj
T*
(3. The distribution system distributes the content among the proxy servers and provides) Tj
T*
(feedback to the request routing system. This feedback is helpful in optimizing the selection of) Tj
T*
(the nearest proxy server for a requesting client. This feedback contains information about) Tj
T*
(which content is cached on which proxy server to route traffic to relevant proxy servers.) Tj
T*
(4. The client requests the routing system for a suitable proxy server from the request routing) Tj
T*
(system.) Tj
T*
(5. The request routing system returns the IP address of an appropriate proxy server.) Tj
T*
(6. The client request routes through the scrubber servers for security reasons.) Tj
T*
(7. The scrubber server forwards good traffic to the edge proxy server.) Tj
T*
(8. The edge proxy server serves the client request and periodically forwards accounting) Tj
T*
(information to the management system. The management system updates the origin servers and) Tj
T*
(sends feedback to the routing system about the statistics and detail of the content. However,) Tj
T*
(the request is routed to the origin servers if the content isn’t available in the proxy) Tj
T*
(servers. It’s also possible to have a hierarchy of proxy servers if the content isn’t found in) Tj
T*
(the edge proxy servers. For such cases, the request gets forwarded to the parent proxy servers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
