(- Requests load refers to the load a proxy server handles at any point in time. If a set of) Tj
T*
(proxy servers are overloaded, the request routing system should forward the request to a) Tj
T*
(location with a lesser load. This action balances out the proxy server load and, consequently,) Tj
T*
(reduces the response latency.) Tj
T*
(Let’s look at the techniques that can be used to route users to the nearest proxy server.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### DNS redirection) Tj
T*
(In a typical DNS resolution, we use a DNS system to get an IP against a human-readable name.) Tj
T*
(However, the DNS can also return another URI \(instead of an IP\) to the client. Such a mechanism) Tj
T*
(is called DNS redirect.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Content providers can use DNS redirect to send a client to a specific CDN. As an example, if) Tj
T*
(the client tries to resolve a name that has the word “video” in it, the authoritative DNS) Tj
T*
(server provides another URL \(for example, cdn.xyz.com\). The client does another DNS resolution,) Tj
T*
(and the CDN’s authoritative DNS provides an IP address of an appropriate CDN proxy server to) Tj
T*
(fetch the required content.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Depending on the location of the user, the response of the DNS can be different. Let’s see the) Tj
T*
(slides below to understand how DNS redirection works:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([DNS redistribution]\(./redistribution\)) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: The nearest proxy server doesn’t necessarily mean the one that’s geographically the) Tj
T*
(closest. It could be, but it’s not only the geography that matters. Other factors like network) Tj
T*
(distance, bandwidth, and traffic load already on that route also matter.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(There are two steps in the DNS redirection approach:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. In the first step, it maps the clients to the appropriate network location.) Tj
T*
(2. In the second step, it distributes the load over the proxy servers in that location to) Tj
T*
(balance the load among the proxy servers \(see DNS and Load Balancers building blocks for more) Tj
T*
(details on this\).) Tj
T*
(DNS redirection takes both of these important factors—network distance and requests load—into) Tj
T*
(consideration, and that reduces the latency towards a proxy server.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(To shift a client from one machine in a cluster to another, the DNS replies at the second step) Tj
T*
(are given with short TTLs so that the client repeats the resolution after a short while. DNS) Tj
T*
(keeps delivering the content by routing requests to other active servers in case of hardware) Tj
T*
(failures and network congestion. It does so by load balancing the traffic, using intelligent) Tj
T*
(failover, and maintaining servers across many data centers, which achieves good reliability and) Tj
T*
(performance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Since the load at proxy servers changes over time, the content provider needs to make) Tj
T*
(appropriate changes in the DNS to make the DNS redirection effective. Many CDN providers like) Tj
T*
(Akamai use DNS redirection in their routing system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Anycast) Tj
T*
(Anycast is a routing methodology in which all the edge servers located in multiple locations) Tj
T*
(share the same single IP address. It employs the Border Gateway Protocol \(BGP\) to route clients) Tj
T*
(based on the Internet’s natural network flow. A CDN provider can use the anycast mechanism so) Tj
T*
(that clients are directed to the nearest proxy servers for content.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(BGP is a network-level protocol used by Internet edge routers to share routing and reachability) Tj
T*
(information so that every node on the network, even if independent, is aware of the status of) Tj
T*
(their closest network neighbors.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(### Client multiplexing) Tj
T*
(Client multiplexing involves sending a client a list of candidate servers. The client then) Tj
T*
(chooses one server from the list to send the request to. This approach is inefficient because) Tj
T*
(the client lacks the overall information to choose the most suitable server for their request.) Tj
T*
