(## Content Delivery Network \(CDN\)/In-depth Investigation of CDN Part 2/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# In-depth Investigation of CDN: Part 2) Tj
T*
(In this lesson, we learn how content consistency can be achieved using different consistency) Tj
T*
(mechanisms. We also learn about where we should deploy the proxy servers and the difference) Tj
T*
(between CDN as a service and specialized CDN.) Tj
T*
(## Content consistency in CDN) Tj
T*
(Data in the proxy servers should be consistent with data in the origin servers. There’s always) Tj
T*
(a risk of users accessing stale data if the proxy servers don’t remain consistent with the) Tj
T*
(origin servers. Different consistency mechanisms can be used to ensure consistency of data,) Tj
T*
(depending on the push or pull model.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Periodic polling) Tj
T*
(Using the pull model, proxy servers request the origin server periodically for updated data and) Tj
T*
(change the content in the cache accordingly. When content changes infrequently, the polling) Tj
T*
(approach consumes unnecessary bandwidth. Periodic polling uses time-to-refresh \(TTR\) to adjust) Tj
T*
(the time period for requesting updated data from the origin servers.) Tj
T*
(### Time-to-live \(TTL\)) Tj
T*
(Because of the TTR, the proxy servers may uselessly request the origin servers for updated) Tj
T*
(data. A better approach that could be employed to reduce the frequency of refresh messages is) Tj
T*
(the time-to-live \(TTL\) approach. In this approach, each object has a TTL attribute assigned to) Tj
T*
(it by the origin server. The TTL defines the expiration time of the content. The proxy servers) Tj
T*
(serve the same data version to the users until that content expires. Upon expiration, the proxy) Tj
T*
(server checks for an update with the origin server. If the data is changed, it gets the updated) Tj
T*
(data from the origin server and then responds to the user’s requests with the updated data.) Tj
T*
(Otherwise, it keeps the same data with an updated expiration time from the origin servers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
