(### Leases) Tj
T*
(The origin server grants a lease to the data sent to a proxy server using this technique. The) Tj
T*
(lease denotes the time interval for which the origin server agrees to notify the proxy server) Tj
T*
(if there’s any change in the data. The proxy server must send a message requesting a lease) Tj
T*
(renewal after the expiration of the lease. The lease method helps to reduce the number of) Tj
T*
(messages exchanged between the proxy and origin server. Additionally, the lease duration can be) Tj
T*
(optimized dynamically according to the observed load on the proxy servers. This technique is) Tj
T*
(referred to as an adaptive lease.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In the following section, we discuss where to place the CDN proxy server to transmit data) Tj
T*
(effectively.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Deployment) Tj
T*
(We have to be clear with the answers to the following questions before we instal the CDN) Tj
T*
(facility:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- What are the best locations to install proxy servers to maximally utilize CDN technology?) Tj
T*
(- How many CDN proxy servers should we install?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Placement of CDN proxy servers) Tj
T*
(The CDN proxy servers must be placed at network locations with good connectivity. See the) Tj
T*
(options below:) Tj
T*
(- On-premises represents a smaller data center that could be placed near major IXPs.) Tj
T*
(- Off-premises represents placing CDN proxy servers in ISP’s networks.) Tj
T*
(Today, it might be feasible to keep a large portion of a movie’s data in a CDN infrastructure) Tj
T*
(that’s housed inside an ISP. Still, for services like YouTube, data is so large and ever-) Tj
T*
(expanding that it’s challenging to decide what we should put near a user. Google uses split TCP) Tj
T*
(to reduce user-perceived delays by keeping persistent connections with huge TCP windows from) Tj
T*
(the IXP-level infrastructure to their primary data centers. The client’s TCP requests terminate) Tj
T*
(at the IXP-level infrastructure and are then forwarded on already established, low latency TCP) Tj
T*
(connections.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Doing this substantially reduces client-perceived latency, which is due to the avoidance of the) Tj
T*
(initial three-way handshake of TCP connection and slow-start stages to a host far away \(had the) Tj
T*
(client wanted to go to the primary data centers of Google\). A round-trip delay to IXP is often) Tj
T*
(very low. Therefore, three-way handshakes and slow starts at that level are negligible.) Tj
T*
(Predictive push is a significant research field to decide what to push near the customers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We can use measurements to facilitate the decision of proxy server placement. One such tool is) Tj
T*
(ProxyTeller to decide where to place the proxy server and how many proxy servers are required) Tj
T*
(to achieve high performance. ProxyTeller uses hit ratio, network bandwidth, and client-response) Tj
T*
(time \(latency\) as performance parameters to decide the placement of proxy servers. Other) Tj
T*
(greedy, random, and hotspot algorithms are also used for proxy server placements.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(A proxy placement tool for content delivery under performance constraints. Source: Trianfillou,) Tj
T*
(P. and Aekaterinidis, I., 2003, December. Proceedings of the Fourth International Conference on) Tj
T*
(Web Information Systems Engineering, 2003. WISE 2003. \(pp. 62-71\). IEEE.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: Akamai and Netflix popularized the idea of keeping their CDN proxy servers inside the) Tj
T*
(client’s ISPs. For many clients of Akamai, content is just one network hop away. On the other) Tj
T*
(hand, Google also has its private CDN infrastructure but relies more on its servers near IXPs.) Tj
T*
(One reason for this could be the sheer amount of data and the change patterns.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
