(## CDN as a service) Tj
T*
(Most companies don’t build their own CDN. Instead, they use the services of a CDN provider,) Tj
T*
(such as Akamai, Cloudflare, Fastly, and so on, to deliver their content. Similarly, players) Tj
T*
(like AWS make it possible for anyone to use a global CDN facility.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The companies sign a contract with the CDN service provider and deliver their content to the) Tj
T*
(CDN, thereby allowing the CDN to distribute the content to the end users. A public CDN raises) Tj
T*
(the following concerns for content providers:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- The content provider can’t do anything if the public CDN is down.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- If a public CDN doesn’t have any proxy servers located in the region or country where some) Tj
T*
(website traffic comes from, then those specific customers are out of luck. In such cases, the) Tj
T*
(content providers have to buy CDN services from other CDN providers or deploy and use their own) Tj
T*
(private CDN.) Tj
