() Tj
T*
(- It’s possible that some domains or IP addresses of CDN providers are blocked or restricted in) Tj
T*
(some countries because they might be delivering content that’s banned in those countries.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: Some companies make their own CDN instead of using the services of CDN providers. For) Tj
T*
(example, Netflix has its own purpose-built CDN called Open Connect.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(## Specialized CDN) Tj
T*
(We’ve discussed that many companies use CDN as a service, but there are cases where companies) Tj
T*
(build their own CDN. A number of reasons factor into this decision. One is the cost of a) Tj
T*
(commercial CDN service. A specialized CDN consists of points of presence \(PoPs\) that only serve) Tj
T*
(content for their own company. These PoPs can be caching servers, reverse proxies, or) Tj
T*
(application delivery controllers. Although a specialized CDN has high costs at its first setup,) Tj
T*
(the costs eventually decrease with time. In essence, it’s a buy versus build decision.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The specialized CDN’s PoPs consist of many proxy servers to serve petabytes of content. A) Tj
T*
(private CDN can be used in coexistence with a public CDN. In case the capacity of a private CDN) Tj
T*
(isn’t enough or there’s a failure that leads to capacity reduction, the public CDN is used as a) Tj
T*
(backup. Netflix’s Open Connect Appliance \(OCA\) is an example of a CDN that’s specialized in) Tj
T*
(video delivery.) Tj
T*
() Tj
