(## Content Delivery Network \(CDN\)/Introduction to a CDN/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Introduction to a CDN) Tj
T*
(## Proposed solution) Tj
T*
(The solution to all the problems discussed in the previous lesson is the content delivery) Tj
T*
(network \(CDN\). A CDN is a group of geographically distributed proxy servers. A proxy server is) Tj
T*
(an intermediate server between a client and the origin server. The proxy servers are placed on) Tj
T*
(the network edge. As the network edge is close to the end users, the placement of proxy servers) Tj
T*
(helps quickly deliver the content to the end users by reducing latency and saving bandwidth. A) Tj
T*
(CDN has added intelligence on top of being a simple proxy server.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(The network edge is the zone where a device or local network interfaces with the Internet.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We can bring data close to the user by placing a small data center near the user and storing) Tj
T*
(copies of the data there. CDN mainly stores two types of data: static and dynamic. A CDN) Tj
T*
(primarily targets propagation delay by bringing the data closer to its users. CDN providers) Tj
T*
(make the extra effort to have sufficient bandwidth available through the path and bring data) Tj
T*
(closer to the users \(possibly within their ISP\). They also try to reduce transmission and) Tj
T*
(queuing delays because the ISP presumably has more bandwidth available within the autonomous) Tj
T*
(system.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(static data: This type of data doesn’t change frequently and remains on the servers for a long) Tj
T*
(period.) Tj
T*
(dynamic data: This type of data changes most frequently—for example, newsletters, ads, live) Tj
T*
(videos, and so on.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Let’s look at the different ways CDN solves the discussed problems:) Tj
T*
(- High latency: CDN brings the content closer to end users. Therefore, it reduces the physical) Tj
T*
(distance and latency.) Tj
T*
(- Data-intensive applications: Since the path to the data includes only the ISP and the nearby) Tj
T*
(CDN components, there’s no issue in serving a large number of users through a few CDN) Tj
T*
(components in a specific area. As shown below, the origin data center will have to provide the) Tj
T*
ET
