(### ZooKeeper) Tj
T*
(To track changes in the cluster, many distributed data systems need a separate management) Tj
T*
(server like ZooKeeper. Zookeeper keeps track of all the mappings in the network, and each node) Tj
T*
(connects to ZooKeeper for the information. Whenever there’s a change in the partitioning, or a) Tj
T*
(node is added or removed, ZooKeeper gets updated and notifies the routing tier about the) Tj
T*
(change. HBase, Kafka and SolrCloud use ZooKeeper.) Tj
T*
(## Conclusion) Tj
T*
(For all current distributed systems, partitioning has become the standard protocol. Because) Tj
T*
(systems contain increasing amounts of data, partitioning the data makes sense since it speeds) Tj
T*
(up both writes and reads. It increases the system’s availability, scalability, and performance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
