(#### Multi-leader replication topologies) Tj
T*
(There are many topologies through which multi-leader replication is implemented, such as) Tj
T*
(circular topology, star topology, and all-to-all topology. The most common is the all-to-all) Tj
T*
(topology. In star and circular topology, there’s again a similar drawback that if one of the) Tj
T*
(nodes fails, it can affect the whole system. That’s why all-to-all is the most used topology.) Tj
T*
(### Peer-to-peer/leaderless replication) Tj
T*
(In primary-secondary replication, the primary node is a bottleneck and a single point of) Tj
T*
(failure. Moreover, it helps to achieve read scalability but fails in providing write) Tj
T*
(scalability. The peer-to-peer replication model resolves these problems by not having a single) Tj
T*
(primary node. All the nodes have equal weightage and can accept reads and writes requests.) Tj
T*
(Amazon popularized such a scheme in their DynamoDB data store.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Peer-to-peer data replication model where all nodes apply reads and writes to all the) Tj
T*
(data]\(./p2p.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Like primary-secondary replication, this replication can also yield inconsistency. This is) Tj
T*
(because when several nodes accept write requests, it may lead to concurrent writes. A helpful) Tj
T*
(approach used for solving write-write inconsistency is called quorums.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(#### Quorums) Tj
T*
(Let’s suppose we have three nodes. If at least two out of three nodes are guaranteed to return) Tj
T*
(successful updates, it means only one node has failed. This means that if we read from two) Tj
T*
(nodes, at least one of them will have the updated version, and our system can continue working.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If we have n nodes, then every write must be updated in at least w nodes to be considered a) Tj
T*
(success, and we must read from r nodes. We’ll get an updated value from reading as long as w +) Tj
T*
(r > n because at least one of the nodes must have an updated write from which we can read.) Tj
T*
(Quorum reads and writes adhere to these r and w values. These n, w and r are configurable in) Tj
T*
(Dynamo-style databases.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Reader getting an updated value from replica 2]\(./dynamo.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
