(### Advantages and disadvantages of a centralized database) Tj
T*
(#### Advantages) Tj
T*
(- Data maintenance, such as updating and taking backups of a centralized database, is easy.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Centralized databases provide stronger consistency and ACID transactions than distributed) Tj
T*
(databases.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Centralized databases provide a much simpler programming model for the end programmers as) Tj
T*
(compared to distributed databases.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- It’s more efficient for businesses to have a small amount of data to store that can reside on) Tj
T*
(a single node.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(#### Disadvantages) Tj
T*
(- A centralized database can slow down, causing high latency for end users, when the number of) Tj
T*
(queries per second accessing the centralized database is approaching single-node limits.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- A centralized database has a single point of failure. Because of this, its probability of not) Tj
T*
(being accessible is much higher.) Tj
T*
() Tj
