(## Databases/Types of Databases/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Types of Databases) Tj
T*
(As we discussed earlier, databases are divided into two types: relational and non-relational.) Tj
T*
(Let’s discuss these types in detail.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Relational databases) Tj
T*
(Relational databases adhere to particular schemas before storing the data. The data stored in) Tj
T*
(relational databases has prior structure. Mostly, this model organizes data into one or more) Tj
T*
(relations \(also called tables\), with a unique key for each tuple \(instance\). Each entity of the) Tj
T*
(data consists of instances and attributes, where instances are stored in rows, and the) Tj
T*
(attributes of each instance are stored in columns. Since each tuple has a unique key, a tuple) Tj
T*
(in one table can be linked to a tuple in other tables by storing the primary keys in other) Tj
T*
(tables, generally known as foreign keys.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A Structure Query Language \(SQL\) is used for manipulating the database. This includes) Tj
T*
(insertion, deletion, and retrieval of data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(There are various reasons for the popularity and dominance of relational databases, which) Tj
T*
(include simplicity, robustness, flexibility, performance, scalability, and compatibility in) Tj
T*
(managing generic data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Relational databases provide the atomicity, consistency, isolation, and durability \(ACID\)) Tj
T*
(properties to maintain the integrity of the database. ACID is a powerful abstraction that) Tj
T*
(simplifies complex interactions with the data and hides many anomalies \(like dirty reads, dirty) Tj
T*
(writes, read skew, lost updates, write skew, and phantom reads\) behind a simple transaction) Tj
T*
(abort.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(But ACID is like a big hammer by design so that it’s generic enough for all the problems. If) Tj
T*
(some specific application only needs to deal with a few anomalies, there’s a window of) Tj
T*
(opportunity to use a custom solution for higher performance, though there is added complexity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Let’s discuss ACID in detail:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Atomicity: A transaction is considered an atomic unit. Therefore, either all the statements) Tj
T*
