(Various database management systems \(DBMS\) are used to define relational database schema along) Tj
T*
(with other operations, such as to store, retrieve, and run SQL queries on data. Some of the) Tj
T*
(popular DBMS are as follows:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(MySQL) Tj
T*
(Oracle Database) Tj
T*
(Microsoft SQL Server) Tj
T*
(IBM DB2) Tj
T*
(Postgres) Tj
T*
(SQLite) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Why relational databases?) Tj
T*
(Relational databases are the default choices of software professionals for structured data) Tj
T*
(storage. There are a number of advantages to these databases. One of the greatest powers of the) Tj
T*
(relational database is its abstractions of ACID transactions and related programming semantics.) Tj
T*
(This make it very convenient for the end-programmer to use a relational database. Let’s revisit) Tj
T*
(some important features of relational databases:) Tj
T*
(#### Flexibility) Tj
T*
(In the context of SQL, data definition language \(DDL\) provides us the flexibility to modify the) Tj
T*
(database, including tables, columns, renaming the tables, and other changes. DDL even allows us) Tj
T*
(to modify schema while other queries are happening and the database server is running.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(DDL is a computer language used to create and modify the structure of database objects in a) Tj
T*
(database.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(#### Reduced redundancy) Tj
T*
(One of the biggest advantages of the relational database is that it eliminates data redundancy.) Tj
T*
(The information related to a specific entity appears in one table while the relevant data to) Tj
T*
(that specific entity appears in the other tables linked through foreign keys. This process is) Tj
T*
(called normalization and has the additional benefit of removing an inconsistent dependency.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Inconsistent dependencies arise when a user searches for some data in the irrelevant table or) Tj
T*
(the data is missing in the relevant table. For example, to find the customer’s address it) Tj
T*
(should be searched in the customer table instead of the product table.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(#### Concurrency) Tj
T*
(Concurrency is an important factor while designing an enterprise database. In such a case, the) Tj
T*
(data is read and written by many users at the same time. We need to coordinate such) Tj
T*
(interactions to avoid inconsistency in data—for example, the double booking of hotel rooms.) Tj
T*
(Concurrency in a relational database is handled through transactional access to the data. As) Tj
T*
(explained earlier, a transaction is considered an atomic operation, so it also works in error) Tj
T*
(handling to either roll back or commit a transaction on successful execution.) Tj
T*
ET
