(#### Key-value database) Tj
T*
(Key-value databases use key-value methods like hash tables to store data in key-value pairs. We) Tj
T*
(can see this depicted in the figure a couple of paragraphs below. Here, the key serves as a) Tj
T*
(unique or primary key, and the values can be anything ranging from simple scalar values to) Tj
T*
(complex objects. These databases allow easy partitioning and horizontal scaling of the data.) Tj
T*
(Some popular key-value databases include Amazon DynamoDB, Redis, and Memcached DB.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Use case: Key-value databases are efficient for session-oriented applications. Session) Tj
T*
(oriented-applications, such as web applications, store users’ data in the main memory or in a) Tj
T*
(database during a session. This data may include user profile information, recommendations,) Tj
T*
(targeted promotions, discounts, and more. A unique ID \(a key\) is assigned to each user’s) Tj
T*
(session for easy access and storage. Therefore, a better choice to store such data is the key-) Tj
T*
(value database.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The following figure shows an example of a key-value database. The Product ID and Type of the) Tj
T*
(item are collectively considered as the primary key. This is considered as a key for this key-) Tj
T*
(value database. Moreover, the schema for storing the item attributes is defined based on the) Tj
T*
(nature of the item and the number of attributes it possesses.) Tj
T*
([Data stored in the form of key-value pair in DynamoDB, where the key is the combination of two) Tj
T*
(attributes \(Product ID and Type\)]\(./dynamo.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(#### Document database) Tj
T*
(A document database is designed to store and retrieve documents in formats like XML, JSON,) Tj
T*
(BSON, and so on. These documents are composed of a hierarchical tree data structure that can) Tj
T*
(include maps, collections, and scalar values. Documents in this type of database may have) Tj
T*
(varying structures and data. MongoDB and Google Cloud Firestore are examples of document) Tj
T*
(databases.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Use case: Document databases are suitable for unstructured catalog data, like JSON files or) Tj
T*
(other complex structured hierarchical data. For example, in e-commerce applications, a product) Tj
T*
(has thousands of attributes, which is unfeasible to store in a relational database due to its) Tj
T*
(impact on the reading performance. Here comes the role of a document database, which can) Tj
T*
(efficiently store each attribute in a single file for easy management and faster reading speed.) Tj
T*
(Moreover, it’s also a good option for content management applications, such as blogs and video) Tj
T*
(platforms. An entity required for the application is stored as a single document in such) Tj
T*
(applications.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
