(# Concurrency in Collaborative Editing) Tj
T*
(## Introduction) Tj
T*
(We’ve discussed the design for a collaborative document editing service, but we haven’t) Tj
T*
(addressed how we’ll deal with concurrent changes in the document by different users. However,) Tj
T*
(before discussing concurrency issues, we need to understand the collaborative text editor.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## What is a document editor?) Tj
T*
(A document is a composition of characters in a specific order. Each character has a value and a) Tj
T*
(positional index. The character can be a letter, a number, an enter \(↵\), or a space. An index) Tj
T*
(represents the character’s position within the ordered list of characters.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The job of the text or document editor is to perform operations like insert\(\), delete\(\),) Tj
T*
(edit\(\), and more on the characters within the document. A depiction of a document and how the) Tj
T*
(editor will perform these operations is below.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([How a document editor performs different operations]\(./editor.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Concurrency issues) Tj
T*
(Collaboration on the same document by different users can lead to concurrency issues. Conflicts) Tj
T*
(may arise whenever multiple users edit the same portion of a document. Since users have a local) Tj
T*
(copy of the document, the final status of the document may be different at the server from what) Tj
T*
(the users see at their end. After the server pushes the updated version, users discover the) Tj
T*
(unexpected outcome.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Example 1) Tj
T*
(Let’s consider a scenario where two users want to add some characters at the same positional) Tj
T*
(index. Below, we’ve depicted how two users modifying the same sentence can lead to conflicting) Tj
T*
(results:) Tj
T*
([How two users modifying the same text can lead to concurrency issues]\(./concurrency.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
