(As shown above, two users are trying to modify the same sentence, “Educative by developers.”) Tj
T*
(Both users are performing insert\(\) at index 10. The two possibilities are as follows:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- The phrase “for developers” overwrites “platform.” This leads to an outcome of “for) Tj
T*
(developers.”) Tj
T*
(- The phrase “platform” overlaps “for developers.” This leads to an outcome of) Tj
T*
(“platformlopers.”) Tj
T*
(This example shows that operations applied in a different order don’t hold the commutative) Tj
T*
(property.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Example 2) Tj
T*
(Let’s look at another simple example where two users are trying to delete the same character) Tj
T*
(from a word. Let’s use the word “EEDUCATIVE.” Because the word has an extra “E,” both the users) Tj
T*
(would want to remove the extra character. Below, we see how an unexpected result can occur:) Tj
T*
() Tj
