(From the examples above, we understand that a solution to concurrency issues in collaborative) Tj
T*
(editing should respect two rules:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Commutativity: The order of applied operations shouldn’t affect the end result.) Tj
T*
(- Idempotency: Similar operations that have been repeated should apply only once.) Tj
T*
(Below, we identify two well-known techniques for conflict resolution.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Techniques for conflict resolution) Tj
T*
(Let’s discuss two leading technologies that are used for conflict resolution in collaborative) Tj
T*
(editing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Operational transformation) Tj
T*
(Operational transformation \(OT\) is a technique that’s widely used for conflict resolution in) Tj
T*
(collaborative editing. OT emerged in 1989 and has improved throughout the years. It’s a lock-) Tj
T*
(free and non-blocking approach for conflict resolution. If operations between collaborators) Tj
T*
(conflict, OT resolves conflicts and pushes the correct converged state to end users. As a) Tj
T*
(result, OT provides consistency for users.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(OT performs operations using the positional index method to resolve conflicts, such as the ones) Tj
T*
(we discussed above. OT resolves the problems above by holding commutativity and idempotency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Ensuring commutativity 1]\(./ot1.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Ensuring commutativity 2]\(./ot2.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Collaborative editors based on OT are consistent if they have the following two properties:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Causality preservation: If operation a happened before operation b, then operation a is) Tj
T*
(executed before operation b.) Tj
T*
(- Convergence: All document replicas at different clients will eventually be identical.) Tj
T*
(The properties above are a part of the CC consistency model, which is a model for consistency) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
