T*
(The research community has proposed various consistency models over the years. Some of them are) Tj
T*
(specific to collaborative editing, while others are specific to OT algorithms. The key) Tj
T*
(consistency models are the following:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- CC model: As we defined above, this includes causality preservation and convergence.) Tj
T*
(- CCI model: This includes causality preservation \(Same as CC model.\), convergence \(Same as CC) Tj
T*
(model.\), and intention preservation\(This property ensures that operations are executed as) Tj
T*
(intended by the users.\).) Tj
T*
(Other models include the CSM \(causality, single-operation effects, and multi-operation effects\)) Tj
T*
(model and the CA \(causality and admissibility\) model.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Various consistency models are suggested, and usually, the newer ones are supersets of the) Tj
T*
(earlier ones. Because there are so many proposed algorithms, discussing them is beyond the) Tj
T*
(scope of our lesson. Interested readers can find more details in) Tj
T*
(https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/289444.289469.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
