(Question 1) Tj
T*
(Why can’t we use locks to synchronize between users?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(Locks require us to segment documents into small sections where users could lock a portion and) Tj
T*
(edit it. This will help developers come up with an easy solution and avoid complexities like OT) Tj
T*
(and CRDTs. However, this also leads to poor user experience. For example, two users may want to) Tj
T*
(add characters to the same section of the document, but their operations may not necessarily) Tj
T*
(conflict.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A lock is a good choice for services like Google Sheets. This is because the document is) Tj
T*
(divided into equal sizes of small cells, and only one user can add or edit the contents of a) Tj
T*
(specific cell.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question 2) Tj
T*
(What happens if there are two users collaborating on a document and they have different) Tj
T*
(Internet speeds? Which technology, OT or CRDT, is better suited for conflict resolution in such) Tj
T*
(a case?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(With a varied Internet connection speed, the order of operations between users can lead to) Tj
T*
(problems. However, operations are order dependent in OT, whereas operations in CRDTs are order) Tj
T*
(independent. This is why CRDTs are a suitable solution to such a problem.) Tj
T*
