(                           - Horizontal sharding of RDBMS) Tj
T*
(                           - CDNs capable of handling a large number of requests for big files) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Scalability) Tj
T*
(Since we've used microservice architecture, we can easily scale each component individually in) Tj
T*
(case the number of requests on the operations queue exceeds its capacity. We can use multiple) Tj
T*
(operations queues. In that case, each operations queue will be responsible for a single) Tj
T*
(document. We can forward operations requested by different users that are associated with a) Tj
T*
(single document to a specific queue. The number of spawned queues will be equal to the number) Tj
T*
(of active documents. As a result, we’re able to achieve horizontal scalability.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Conclusion) Tj
T*
(In this chapter, we designed an online collaborative document editing service. In our design,) Tj
T*
(we provided features like collaborative editing, keeping version history for reverting to older) Tj
T*
