T*
(## Improve estimations using live data) Tj
T*
(This section describes how we can improve the ETA estimation accuracy using live data. If we) Tj
T*
(have a sequence of location data for different devices, we can find movement patterns and) Tj
T*
(perform analytics to predict various factors that may influence a user’s trip. Google Maps uses) Tj
T*
(a combination of GPS, Wi-Fi, and cell towers to track users’ locations. To collect this data,) Tj
T*
(our maps system servers need to have a persistent connection with all the devices that have) Tj
T*
(their location turned on. Below, we discuss the tools, techniques, and components involved in) Tj
T*
(the process of improving estimations using live data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- WebSocket is a communication protocol that allows users and servers to have a two-way,) Tj
T*
(interactive communication session. This helps in the real-time transfer of data between user) Tj
T*
(and server.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- The load balancer balances the connection load between different servers since there is a) Tj
T*
(limit on the number of WebSocket connections per server. It connects some devices to server 1,) Tj
T*
(some to server 2, and so on.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Performing analytics on the live location data to keep the map up-to-date and also improve ETA) Tj
T*
(estimations]\(./analysis.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- A pub-sub system collects the location data streams \(device, time, location\) from all) Tj
T*
(servers. The location data from pub-sub is read by a data analytics engine like Apache Spark.) Tj
T*
(The data analytics engine uses data science techniques—such as machine learning, clustering,) Tj
T*
(and so on—to measure and predict traffic on the roads, identify gatherings, hotspots, events,) Tj
T*
(find out new roads, and so on. These analytics help our system improve ETAs.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: The amount of traffic, road conditions, and hotspots directly affect average travel) Tj
T*
(speed, which ultimately affects users’ ETAs.) Tj
T*
