() Tj
T*
(- The map update service listens to the updates from the pub-sub topic for the analytics. It) Tj
T*
(updates the segment graphs if there is a new road identified or if there is a change in the) Tj
T*
(weight \(average speed \(traffic, road condition\)\) on the edges of the graph. Depending on the) Tj
T*
(location, we know which segment the update belongs to. We find the routing server on which that) Tj
T*
(segment is placed from the key-value store and update the graph on that server.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question) Tj
T*
(Many traffic conditions are transitory \(like stopping at a signal\), so updating the graph very) Tj
T*
(often wouldn’t scale well because it requires excessive processing. What could be the solution) Tj
T*
(to this problem?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(To detect transitory and normal conditions, we keep two copies of all relevant data \(weights\):) Tj
T*
(one for normal conditions and the other for transitory conditions. That way, we won’t have to) Tj
T*
(do excessive processing.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- The graph preprocessing service recalculates the new paths on the updated segment graph.) Tj
T*
(We’ve seen how the paths are updated continuously in the background based on the live data.) Tj
T*
(We’ve learned how the segments work, how a user finds the location between two points, and how) Tj
T*
(the ETA's accuracy is improved by utilizing the live location data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
