(## Design Google Maps/Evaluation of Google Maps' Design/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Evaluation of Google Maps' Design) Tj
T*
(Let’s see how the system we designed will handle millions of queries per second, ensuring a) Tj
T*
(fast response time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Availability) Tj
T*
(With a large road network graph hosted on a single server, we ran into these issues:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- We couldn’t process user queries, since it was impossible to load such a large graph into the) Tj
T*
(memory, making the system unavailable to the users.) Tj
T*
(- It wasn’t possible to make a persistent two-way connection \(for navigation\) between the) Tj
T*
(server and millions of users per second.) Tj
T*
(- It was also a single point of failure.) Tj
T*
(We solved the above problems by dividing the world into small segments. Each small segment) Tj
T*
(consists of a graph that can be easily loaded into a server’s memory. With segments, we) Tj
T*
(completed these objectives:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- We hosted each segment on a separate server, mitigating the issue of loading a large, global) Tj
T*
(graph.) Tj
T*
(- The load balancer divides the request load across different segment servers depending on the) Tj
T*
(user’s area of search. It mitigates the issue of putting the burden on a single server, which) Tj
T*
(was affecting the system’s availability.) Tj
T*
(- We didn’t discuss replication, but we can replicate each segment, which will help deal with a) Tj
T*
(segment server as a single point of failure and distribute the request load for a segment to) Tj
T*
(replicas.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: Google Maps uses lazy loading of data, putting less burden on the system, which improves) Tj
T*
(availability.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Lazy loading is postponing the loading or initialization of resources or objects until they are) Tj
T*
(needed. It reduces initial load time by reducing the amount of content to load, saves bandwidth) Tj
T*
(by delivering content to users when required, and preserves server and client resources by) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
