(destination. However, this approach wouldn’t scale well for billions of users sending millions) Tj
T*
(of queries per second. This is because running any path-finding algorithm on a graph with) Tj
T*
(billions of nodes running a million times per second is inefficient in terms of time and cost,) Tj
T*
(ultimately leading to a bad user experience. Therefore, our solution needs to find alternative) Tj
T*
(techniques to scale well.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Spanning]\(./spanning.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- ETA computation: In an ideal situation with empty roads, it’s straightforward to compute ETA) Tj
T*
(using the distance and the speed of the vehicle we want to ride on. However, we cannot ignore) Tj
T*
(factors like the amount of traffic on the roads and road conditions, which affect the ETA) Tj
T*
(directly. For example, a road under construction, collisions, and rush hours all might slow) Tj
T*
(down traffic. Quantifying the factors above to design our system is not trivial. Therefore,) Tj
T*
(we’ll, categorize the factors above in terms of traffic load to complete our design.) Tj
T*
() Tj
