(## What is Google Maps?) Tj
T*
(Let’s introduce the problem by assuming that we want to travel from one place to another. Here) Tj
T*
(are the possible things that we might want to know:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- What are the best possible paths that take us to our destination, depending on the vehicle) Tj
T*
(type we’re using?) Tj
T*
(- How long in miles is each path?) Tj
T*
(- How much time does each path take to get us to our destination?) Tj
T*
(A maps application \(like Google Maps or Apple Maps\) enables users to answer all of the above) Tj
T*
(questions easily. The following illustration shows the paths calculated by Google maps from) Tj
T*
(“Los Angeles, USA” to “New York City, USA.”) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Three paths suggested by Google maps for traveling from Los Angeles to New York]\(./map.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## When do we use a maps service?) Tj
T*
(Individuals and organizations rely on location data to navigate around the world. Maps help in) Tj
T*
(these cases:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Individuals can find the locations of and directions to new places quickly, instead of) Tj
T*
(wasting their time and the costs of travel, such as gas.) Tj
T*
(- Individuals use maps to see their estimated time of arrival \(ETA\) and the shortest path based) Tj
T*
(on current traffic data.) Tj
T*
(- Many modern applications rely heavily on maps, such as ride-hailing services, autonomous) Tj
T*
(vehicles, and hiking maps. For example:) Tj
T*
(  - Waymo’s self-driving car system uses Google Maps to navigate efficiently, quickly, and) Tj
T*
(safely.) Tj
T*
(  - Uber uses Google Maps as part of its application to assist drivers and provide customers) Tj
T*
(with a visual representation of their journey.) Tj
T*
(- Routing and logistics-based companies reduce the time it takes to make deliveries. By using a) Tj
T*
(map’s unique real-time and historical traffic data, it minimizes the overall cost of deliveries) Tj
T*
(by reducing gas usage and time spent stuck in traffic.) Tj
T*
(In 2022, more than five million businesses are using Google Maps. It provides an API for) Tj
T*
(enterprises to use a map system in their application.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## How will we design Google Maps?) Tj
T*
(We divide the design of Google Maps into five lessons:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Requirements: In this lesson, we’ll list the functional and non-functional requirements of a) Tj
T*
(Google Maps system. We will also identify the challenges involved in designing such a system.) Tj
T*
(Lastly, we’ll estimate the resources like servers and bandwidth needed to serve queries by) Tj
T*
(millions of users.) Tj
T*
(2. Design: This lesson consists of the high-level and API design of a system like Google maps.) Tj
T*
(We’ll describe the services and the workflow of the system.) Tj
T*
(3. Meeting the challenges: We will discuss how we overcome the challenges that we highlighted) Tj
T*
(in the requirements lesson.) Tj
T*
(4. Detailed design: Based on the solution to the challenges, we will improve our earlier design) Tj
T*
(and also elaborate on different aspects of it. We will describe the detailed design, including) Tj
T*
(storage schema.) Tj
T*
(5. Evaluation: This lesson explains how our designed Google Maps system fulfills all the) Tj
T*
(requirements.) Tj
T*
(Let’s start by understanding the requirements for designing a system like Google Maps.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Design Instagram/Design of Instagram/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Design of Instagram) Tj
T*
(## High-level design) Tj
T*
(Our system should allow us to upload, view, and search images and videos at a high level. To) Tj
T*
(upload images and videos, we need to store them, and upon fetching, we need to retrieve the) Tj
T*
(data from the storage. Moreover, the users should also be allowed to follow each other.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
