T*
(## API design) Tj
T*
(This section describes APIs invoked by the users to perform different tasks \(upload, like, and) Tj
T*
(view photos/videos\) on Instagram. We’ll implement REST APIs for these tasks. Let’s develop APIs) Tj
T*
(for each of the following features:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Post photos and videos) Tj
T*
(- Follow and unfollow users) Tj
T*
(- Like or dislike posts) Tj
T*
(- Search photos and videos) Tj
T*
(- Generate a news feed) Tj
T*
(All of the following calls will have a userID, that uniquely specifies the user performing the) Tj
T*
(action. We’ll only discuss new parameters in the calls.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Post photos or videos) Tj
T*
(The POST method is used to post photos/videos to the server from the user through the) Tj
T*
(/postMedia API. The /postMedia API is as follows:) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(postMedia\(userID, media_type, list_of_hashtags, caption\)) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Parameter             Description) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(media_type            It indicates the type of media \(photo or video\) in a post.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(list_of_hashtags      It represents all hashtags \(maximum limit 30 hashtags\) in a post.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(caption               It is a text \(maximum limit is 2,200 characters\) in a user’s post.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(### Follow and unfollow users) Tj
T*
(The /followUser API is used when a user follows other users on Instagram. The /followUser API) Tj
T*
(is as follows:) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(followUser\(userID, target_userID\)) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Parameter          Description) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(target_userID      It indicates the user to be followed.) Tj
T*
(````) Tj
