(## Storage schema) Tj
T*
(Let’s define our data model now:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Relational or non-relational database) Tj
T*
(It is essential to choose the right kind of database for our Instagram system, but which is the) Tj
T*
(right choice — SQL or NoSQL? Our data is inherently relational, and we need an order for the) Tj
T*
(data \(posts should appear in chronological order\) and no data loss even in case of failures) Tj
T*
(\(data durability\). Moreover, in our case, we would benefit from relational queries like) Tj
T*
(fetching the followers or images based on a user ID. Hence, SQL-based databases fulfill these) Tj
T*
(requirements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(So, we’ll opt for a relational database and store our relevant data in that database.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Define tables) Tj
T*
(On a basic level, we need the following tables:) Tj
T*
() Tj
