(## Ensure non-functional requirements) Tj
T*
(We evaluate the Instagram design with respect to its non-functional requirements:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Scalability: We can add more servers to application service layers to make the scalability) Tj
T*
(better and handle numerous requests from the clients. We can also increase the number of) Tj
T*
(databases to store the growing users’ data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Latency: The use of cache and CDNs have reduced the content fetching time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Availability: We have made the system available to the users by using the storage and) Tj
T*
(databases that are replicated across the globe.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Durability: We have persistent storage that maintains the backup of the data so any uploaded) Tj
T*
(content \(photos and videos\) never gets lost.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Consistency: We have used storage like blob stores and databases to keep our data consistent) Tj
T*
(globally.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Reliability: Our databases handle replication and redundancy, so our system stays reliable) Tj
T*
(and data is not lost. The load balancing layer routes requests around failed servers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
