(# System Design: Instagram) Tj
T*
(## What is Instagram?) Tj
T*
(Instagram is a free social networking application that allows users to post photos and short) Tj
T*
(videos. Users can add a caption for each post and utilize hashtags or location-based geotags to) Tj
T*
(index them and make them searchable within the application. A user’s Instagram posts display in) Tj
T*
(their followers’ feeds and can be seen by the general public if they are tagged with hashtags) Tj
T*
(or geotags. Alternatively, users can choose to make their profile private, which limits access) Tj
T*
(to those who have chosen to follow them.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The expansion in the number of users requires more resources \(servers, databases, and so on\)) Tj
T*
(over time. Knowing the users’ growth rate helps us predict the resources to scale our system) Tj
T*
(accordingly. The following illustration shows the Instagram user base in different countries as) Tj
T*
(of January 2022 \(source: Statista\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Countries with the most Instagram users]\(./countries.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## How will we design Instagram?) Tj
T*
(We have divided the design of Instagram into four lessons:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Requirements: This lesson will put forth the functional and non-functional requirements of) Tj
T*
(Instagram. It will also estimate the resources required to achieve these requirements.) Tj
T*
(2. Design: This lesson will explain the workflow and usage of each component, API design and) Tj
T*
(database schema.) Tj
T*
(3. Detailed design: In this lesson, we’ll explore the components of our Instagram design in) Tj
T*
(detail and discuss various approaches to generate timelines. Moreover, we’ll also evaluate our) Tj
T*
(proposed design.) Tj
T*
ET
