(## Detailed design) Tj
T*
(Let’s explore the design of the newsfeed system in detail.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(As discussed earlier, there are two parts of the newsfeed system; newsfeed publishing and) Tj
T*
(newsfeed generation. Therefore, we’ll discuss both parts, starting with the newsfeed generation) Tj
T*
(service.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### The newsfeed generation service) Tj
T*
(Newsfeed is generated by aggregated posts \(or feed items\) from the user’s friends, followers,) Tj
T*
(and other entities \(pages and groups\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In our proposed design, the newsfeed generation service is responsible for generating the) Tj
T*
(newsfeed. When a request from a user \(say Alice\) to retrieve a newsfeed is received at web) Tj
T*
(servers, the web server either:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Calls the newsfeed generation service to generate feeds because some users don’t often visit) Tj
T*
(the platform, so their feeds are generated on their request.) Tj
T*
(- It fetches the pre-generated newsfeed for active users who visit the platform frequently.) Tj
T*
(The following steps are performed in sequence to generate a newsfeed for Alice:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. The newsfeed generation service retrieves IDs of all users and entities that Alice follows) Tj
T*
(from the graph database.) Tj
T*
(2. When the IDs are retrieved from the graph database, the next step is to get their friends’) Tj
T*
(\(followers and entities\) information from the user cache, which is regularly updated whenever) Tj
T*
(the users database gets updated/modified.) Tj
T*
(3. In this step, the service retrieves the latest, most popular, and relevant posts for those) Tj
T*
(IDs from the post cache. These are the posts that we might be able to display on Alice’s) Tj
T*
(newsfeed.) Tj
T*
(4. The ranking service ranks posts based on their relevance to Alice. This represents Alice’s) Tj
T*
(current newsfeed.) Tj
T*
(5. The newsfeed is stored in the the newsfeed cache from which top N posts are published to) Tj
T*
(Alice’s timeline. \(The publishing process is discussed in detail in the following section\).) Tj
T*
(6. In the end, whenever Alice reaches the end of her timeline, the next top N posts are fetched) Tj
T*
(to her screen from the newsfeed cache.) Tj
T*
(The process is illustrated in the following figure:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Working of the newsfeed generation service]\(./newsfeed_generation.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question) Tj
T*
(The creation and storage of newsfeeds for each user in the cache requires an enormous amount of) Tj
T*
(memory \(step 5 in the above section\). Is there any way to reduce this memory consumption?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(A memory-efficient way would be to store just the mapping between users and their corresponding) Tj
T*
(posts in a table in the cache, that is., < Post_ID, User_ID>. During the feed publishing phase,) Tj
T*
(the system will retrieve posts from the post database and generate the newsfeed for a user who) Tj
T*
(follows another user with User_ID.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### The newsfeed publishing service) Tj
T*
ET
