() Tj
T*
(### The newsfeed ranking service) Tj
T*
(Often we see the relevant and important posts on the top of our newsfeed whenever we log in to) Tj
T*
(our social media accounts. This ranking involves multiple advanced ranking and recommendation) Tj
T*
(algorithms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In our design, the newsfeed ranking service consists of these algorithms working on various) Tj
T*
(features, such as, a user’s past history, likes, dislikes, comments, clicks, and many more.) Tj
T*
(These algorithms also perform the following functions:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Select “candidates” posts to show in a newsfeed.) Tj
T*
(- Eliminate posts including misinformation or clickbait from the candidate posts.) Tj
T*
(- Create a list of friends a user frequently interacts with.) Tj
T*
(- Choose topics on which a user spent more time.) Tj
T*
(The ranking system considers all the above points to predict relevant and important posts for a) Tj
T*
(user.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The ranked newsfeeds are stored in the cache servers]\(./ranked_newsfeed.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Posts ranking and newsfeed construction) Tj
T*
(The post database contains posts published by different users. Assume that there are 10 posts) Tj
T*
(in the database published by 5 different users. We aim to rank only 4 posts out of 10 for a) Tj
T*
(user \(say Bob\) who follows those five different users. We perform the following to rank each) Tj
T*
(post and create a newsfeed for Bob:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Various features such as likes, comments, shares, category, duration, etc and so on, are) Tj
T*
