(## Summary) Tj
T*
(In this chapter, we learned to design a newsfeed system at scale. Our design ranked enormous) Tj
T*
(user data to show carefully curated content to the user for better user experience and) Tj
T*
(engagement. Our newsfeed design is general enough that it can be used in many places such as) Tj
T*
(Twitter feeds, Facebook posts, YouTube and Instagram recommendations, News applications, and so) Tj
T*
(on.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Design Newsfeed System/Requirements of a Newsfeed System's Design/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Requirements of a Newsfeed System’s Design) Tj
T*
(## Requirements) Tj
T*
(To limit the scope of the problem, we’ll focus on the following functional and non-functional) Tj
T*
(requirements:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Functional requirements) Tj
T*
(- Newsfeed generation: The system will generate newsfeeds based on pages, groups, and followers) Tj
T*
(that a user follows. A user may have many friends and followers. Therefore, the system should) Tj
T*
(be capable of generating feeds from all friends and followers. The challenge here is that there) Tj
T*
(is potentially a huge amount of content. Our system needs to decide which content to pick for) Tj
T*
(the user and rank it further to decide which to show first.) Tj
T*
(- Newsfeed contents: The newsfeed may contain text, images, and videos.) Tj
T*
(- Newsfeed display: The system should affix new incoming posts to the newsfeed for all active) Tj
T*
(users based on some ranking mechanism. Once ranked, we show content to a user with higher-) Tj
T*
(ranked first.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Non-functional requirements) Tj
T*
(- Scalability: Our proposed system should be highly scalable to support the ever-increasing) Tj
T*
(number of users on any platform, such as Twitter, Facebook, and Instagram.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Fault tolerance: As the system should be handling a large amount of data; therefore,) Tj
T*
(partition tolerance \(system availability in the events of network failure between the system’s) Tj
T*
(components\) is necessary.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Availability: The service must be highly available to keep the users engaged with the) Tj
T*
(platform. The system can compromise strong consistency for availability and fault tolerance,) Tj
T*
(according to the PACELC theorem.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Low latency: The system should provide newsfeeds in real-time. Hence, the maximum latency) Tj
T*
(should not be greater than 2 seconds.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
