() Tj
T*
(# System Design: Newsfeed System) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## What is a newsfeed?) Tj
T*
(A newsfeed of any social media platform \(Twitter, Facebook, Instagram\) is a list of stories) Tj
T*
(generated by entities that a user follows. It contains text, images, videos, and other) Tj
T*
(activities such as likes, comments, shares, advertisements, and many more. This list is) Tj
T*
(continuously updated and presented to the relevant users on the user’s home page. Similarly, a) Tj
T*
(newsfeed system also displays the newsfeed to users from friends, followers, groups, and other) Tj
T*
(pages, including a user’s own posts.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(An entity could be a page, group, friends, and followers of a user.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A newsfeed is essential for social media platform users because it keeps them informed about) Tj
T*
(the latest industry developments, current affairs, and relevant information. It also provides) Tj
T*
(them additional reasons to return and connect with a platform on a regular basis. Billions of) Tj
T*
(users use such platforms. The challenging task is to provide a personalized newsfeed in real-) Tj
T*
(time while keeping the system scalable and highly available.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This chapter will discuss the high-level and detailed design of a newsfeed system for a social) Tj
T*
(platform like Facebook, Twitter, Instagram, etc.) Tj
T*
ET
