(## How will we design the newsfeed system?) Tj
T*
(We have divided the design of the newsfeed system into the following three lessons:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Requirements: In this lesson, we’ll identify the functional and non-functional requirements.) Tj
T*
(We’ll also estimate the resource requirements to provide a personalized newsfeed to billions of) Tj
T*
(users each day.) Tj
T*
(2. Design: We’ll discuss the high-level and detailed design of the newsfeed system in this) Tj
T*
(lesson. We’ll also describe the API design and database schema for our proposed design.) Tj
T*
(Moreover, this lesson will also help us to rank newsfeed to provide a better experience to) Tj
T*
(users.) Tj
T*
(3. Evaluation: In this lesson, we’ll evaluate the design of the newsfeed system based on the) Tj
T*
(non-functional requirements. We’ll also take a quiz to assess our understanding of the design) Tj
T*
(of the newsfeed system.) Tj
T*
(Let’s list down the requirements for designing our version of the newsfeed system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Design Quora/Evaluation of Quora’s Design/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Evaluation of Quora’s Design) Tj
T*
(## Fulfilling requirements) Tj
T*
(We have used various techniques to fulfill our functional requirements. However, we need to) Tj
T*
(determin if we have fulfilled the non-functional requirements. We’ll highlight some of the) Tj
T*
(mechanisms we have utilized to address the non-functional requirements:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Scalability: Our system is highly scalable for several reasons. The updated design uses) Tj
T*
(powerful and homogeneous service hosts. Quora uses powerful machines because service hosts use) Tj
T*
(an in-memory cache, some level of queueing, maintain manager, worker, and routing library. The) Tj
T*
(horizontal scaling of these service hosts is convenient because they are homogeneous.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Quora now uses Amazon EC2 instances with 32 cores, a shared 20 MB cache, and high network) Tj
T*
(throughput.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(On the database end, our design shards the MySQL databases vertically, which avoids issues in) Tj
T*
(scalability because of overloaded MySQL servers. To reduce complex join queries, tables) Tj
T*
(anticipating join operations are placed in the same shard or partition.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: As mentioned earlier, vertical sharding may not be enough because each shard can grow) Tj
T*
(large horizontally. For large MySQL tables, writing becomes a bottleneck. Therefore, our design) Tj
T*
(may have to adhere to horizontal sharding, a well-known practice in database scaling.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Consistency: Due to the variety of functionalities offered by Quora, different consistency) Tj
T*
(schemes may be selected for different types of data. For example, certain critical data like) Tj
T*
(questions and answers should be stored synchronously. In this case, performance can take a hit) Tj
T*
(because users don’t expect instantaneous responses to their questions. It means that a user may) Tj
T*
(get a reply in five minutes, one hour, one day, or no response at all, depending on the user’s) Tj
T*
(question and the availability of would-be respondents.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Other data like view counts may not necessarily be stored synchronously because it is not a) Tj
T*
(goal of the Quora service to ensure that all users see the same number of views as soon as the) Tj
T*
(question is posted. For such cases, eventual consistency is favored for improved performance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: In general, our design is equipped with strong techniques to reduce the user-perceived) Tj
T*
(latency as a whole.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
ET
