T*
(- Availability: Some of the main ideas to improve availability include isolation between) Tj
T*
(different components, keeping redundant instances, using CDN, using configuration services like) Tj
T*
(ZooKeeper, and load balancers to hide failures from users.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Decoupling services help to maintain, upgrade, and recover during failures of individual) Tj
T*
(service or hosts. If services are collocated on the same node or host, a failed node results in) Tj
T*
(the loss of multiple services at once.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Our design, however, lacks any disaster recovery management, which we’ll explore in the next) Tj
T*
(section.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Performance: This design has a strong performance because we have employed the right) Tj
T*
(technology for the right feature. For example, we have used several datastores for different) Tj
T*
(reasons. On top of that, we used different distributed caches depending upon the use case and) Tj
T*
(access frequency. Also, we employed Kafka to queue similar tasks and assign them to cron jobs) Tj
T*
(that otherwise take a long time if executed via API calls.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: Quora claims that using its custom queuing solution, it can handle roughly 15,000 tasks) Tj
T*
(per second.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Facts) Tj
T*
(Quora has developed a custom in-memory caching system called Pycache that can store tens of GBs) Tj
T*
(of cache in a local machine.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The Pycache API contains simple but effective functions like pycache.get\(key\), pycache.set\(key,) Tj
T*
(value\), pycache.delete\(key\), pycache.iteritems\(\), and pycache.update\(\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Both the set and delete functions have variants to set and delete multiple entries at once.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Quora has developed and open-sourced a tool called Asynq that simplifies batching of cache) Tj
T*
(requests to Memcached. So, developers can write code faster—and the latency of a round trip to) Tj
T*
(the caching service is reduced) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Meeting Non-functional Requirements) Tj
T*
(Requirements                Techniques) Tj
