() Tj
T*
(The approach is fairly straightforward. The data, application servers, and configurations are) Tj
T*
(backed up in the Amazon S3 storage service in the same zone. Zonal replication between S3) Tj
T*
(storage facilitates transfer to another zone. Later, the application and database servers can) Tj
T*
(be restored from the S3 storage in another zone.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The restoration strategy is simple and effective but it has a couple of drawbacks:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- We might lose some data that is not backed up since we take backups on a daily basis.) Tj
T*
(However, this issue can be mitigated if we do synchronous replication across regions.) Tj
T*
(- Restoration can take a long time \(a few hours\), and most databases do not serve queries while) Tj
T*
(data is being recovered.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: In general, Amazon provides service with high reliability and availability. For instance,) Tj
T*
(S3 service reports 99.999999999% durability and 99.9% availability over a year.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(## Conclusion) Tj
T*
(Throughout this design, we learned how Quora is able to scale its services as the number of) Tj
T*
(users increases. One interesting aspect of the design includes the vertical sharding of the) Tj
T*
(MySQL database. Apart from that, the Quora design discusses a variety of techniques to meet the) Tj
T*
(functional and non-functional requirements. However, our scope did not include the usage of) Tj
T*
(techniques like natural language processing \(NLP\) to remove spelling mistakes in user’s) Tj
T*
(questions or typeahead services during the search.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question) Tj
T*
(How can using different data stores for different types of data be beneficial in disaster) Tj
T*
(recovery?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(When we use different data stores, it means that we can recover various forms of data) Tj
T*
(simultaneously instead of one large blob of data. Since we recover data stores with variable) Tj
T*
(recovery times, the final recovery time equals the maximum recovery time among all data stores.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(However, using many databases also means that administrators need to know the details of) Tj
T*
(checkpointing or restoring them.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Design Quora/Final Design of Quora/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Final Design of Quora) Tj
T*
(## Limitations of the proposed design) Tj
T*
(The proposed design serves all the functional requirements. However, it has a number of serious) Tj
T*
(drawbacks that emerge as we scale. This means that we are unable to fulfill the non-functional) Tj
T*
(requirements. Let’s explore the main shortcomings below:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Limitations of web and application servers: To entertain the user’s request, payloads are) Tj
T*
(transferred between web and application servers, which increases latency because of network I/O) Tj
T*
(between these two types of servers. Even if we achieve parallel computation by separating the) Tj
T*
(web from application servers \(that is, the manager and worker processes\), the added latency due) Tj
T*
(to an additional network link erodes a user’s experience. Apart from data transfer, control) Tj
T*
(communication between the router library with manager and worker processes also imposes) Tj
T*
(additional performance penalties.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- In-memory queue failure: The internal architecture of application servers log tasks and) Tj
T*
(forward them to the in-memory queues, which serve them to the workers. These in-memory queues) Tj
T*
(of different priorities can be subject to failures. For instance, if a queue gets lost, all the) Tj
T*
(tasks in that queue are lost as well, and manual engineering is required to recover those) Tj
T*
(tasks. This greatly reduces the performance of the system. On the other hand, replicating these) Tj
T*
ET
