(## Detailed design of Quora) Tj
T*
(Let’s understand the improvements in our design:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Service hosts) Tj
T*
(We combine the web and application servers within a single powerful machine that can handle all) Tj
T*
(the processes at once. This technique eliminates the network I/O and the latency introduced due) Tj
T*
(to the network hops required between the manager, worker, and routing library processes. The) Tj
T*
(illustration below provides an abstract view of the updated web server architecture:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The updated design, where web and application servers are combined in the service) Tj
T*
(host]\(./servers.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Vertical sharding of MySQL) Tj
T*
(Tables in the MySQL server are converted to separate shards that we refer to as partitions. A) Tj
T*
(partition has a single primary server and multiple replica servers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The goal is to improve performance and reduce the load due to an increasing number of queries) Tj
T*
(on a single database table. To achieve that, we do vertical sharding in two ways:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. We split tables of a single database into multiple partitions. The concept is depicted in) Tj
T*
(Partitions 2 and 3, which embed Tables 4 and 3, respectively.) Tj
T*
(2. We combine multiple tables into a single partition, where join operations are anticipated.) Tj
T*
(The concept is depicted in Partition 1, which embeds Tables 1 and 2.) Tj
T*
(Therefore, we are able to co-locate related data and reduce traffic on hot data. The) Tj
T*
(illustration below depicts vertical sharding at Quora.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The architecture of vertical sharding at Quora]\(./partitions.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(After we complete the partitioning, we require two types of mappings or metadata to complete) Tj
T*
(our scaling process:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
