(1. Which partitions contain which tables and columns?) Tj
T*
(2. Which hosts are primary and replicas of a particular partition?) Tj
T*
(Both of these mappings are maintained by a service like ZooKeeper.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The sharded design above ensures scalability because we are able to locate related data in a) Tj
T*
(single partition, and therefore it eliminates the need for querying data from multiple shards.) Tj
T*
(Also, the number of read-replicas can be increased for hot shards, or further sharding may be) Tj
T*
(performed. For edge cases where joining may be needed, we can perform it at the application) Tj
T*
(level.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: Vertical sharding is of particular interest in Quora’s design because horizontal sharding) Tj
T*
(is more common in the database community. The main idea behind vertical sharding is to achieve) Tj
T*
(scalability by carefully dividing or re-locating tables and eliminating join operations across) Tj
T*
(different shards. Nevertheless, a vertically sharded partition or table can grow horizontally) Tj
T*
(to an extent where horizontal sharding will be necessary to retain acceptable performance.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### MyRocks) Tj
T*
(The new design embeds MyRocks as the key-value store instead of HBase. We use the MyRocks) Tj
T*
(version of RocksDB for two main reasons:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. MyRocks has a lower p99 latency instead of HBase. Quora claims to have reduced P99 latency) Tj
T*
(from 80 ms to 4 ms using MyRocks.) Tj
T*
(2. There are operational tools that can transfer data between MyRocks and MySQL.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: Quora serves the ML compute engine by extracting features from questions and answers) Tj
T*
(stored in MySQL. In this case, the operational tools come in handy to transfer data between) Tj
T*
(MyRocks and MySQL.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Kafka) Tj
T*
(Our updated design reduces the request load on service hosts by separating not-so-urgent tasks) Tj
T*
(from the regular API calls. For this purpose, we use Kafka, which can disseminate jobs among) Tj
T*
(various queues for tasks such as the view counter \(see Sharded Counters\), notification system,) Tj
T*
(analytics, and highlight topics to the user. Each of these jobs is executed through cron jobs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(cron jobs: It is also called “cron,” and is a command-line utility that is used to schedule) Tj
T*
(tasks on UNIX-like operating systems.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Technology usage) Tj
T*
(Services that scale quickly have little time to develop new features and handle an increasing) Tj
T*
(number of requests from users. Such services employ cloud infrastructure to handle spikes in) Tj
T*
(traffic. Also, the choice of programming language is important. Just like we mentioned that) Tj
T*
(YouTube chose Python for faster programming, we can apply the same logic to Quora. In fact,) Tj
T*
(Quora uses the Python Paste web framework.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(It is desirable to use a faster programming language like C++ to develop the feature extraction) Tj
T*
(service. For online recommendation services through a ML engine, feature extraction service) Tj
T*
(should be quick, to enable the ML engine to accomplish accurate recommendations. Not only that,) Tj
T*
(but reducing the latency burden on the ML engine allows it to provide a larger set of services.) Tj
T*
(We can employ the Thrift service to support interoperability between programming languages) Tj
T*
(within different components.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Feature extration service: Quora refers to their feature extraction service as Alchemy, a) Tj
T*
(scalable and high-performance tool.) Tj
T*
