T*
(Features like comments, upvotes, and downvotes require frequent page updates from the client) Tj
T*
(side. Polling is a technique where the client \(browser\) frequently requests the server for new) Tj
T*
(updates. The server may or may not have any updates but still responds to the client.) Tj
T*
(Therefore, the server may get uselessly overburdened. To resolve this issue, Quora uses a) Tj
T*
(technique called long polling, where if a client requests for an update, the server may not) Tj
T*
(respond for as long as 60 seconds if there are no updates. However, if there is an update, the) Tj
T*
(server will reply immediately and allow the client to make new requests.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
