(## Design Quora/Initial Design of Quora/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Initial Design of Quora) Tj
T*
(## Initial design) Tj
T*
(The initial design of Quora will be composed of the following building blocks and components:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Web and application servers: A typical Quora page is generated by various services. The web) Tj
T*
(and application servers maintain various processes to generate a webpage. The web servers have) Tj
T*
(manager processes and the application servers have worker processes for handling various) Tj
T*
(requests. The manager processes distribute work among the worker processes using a router) Tj
T*
(library. The router library is enqueued with tasks by the manager processes and dequeued by) Tj
T*
(worker processes. Each application server maintains several in-memory queues to handle) Tj
T*
(different user requests. The following illustration provides an abstract view of web and) Tj
T*
(application servers:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Web and application servers at Quora]\(./servers.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Data stores: Different types of data require storage in different data stores. We can use) Tj
T*
(critical data like questions, answers, comments, and upvotes/downvotes in a relational database) Tj
T*
(like MySQL because it offers a higher degree of consistency. NoSQL databases like HBase can be) Tj
T*
(used to store the number of views of a page, scores used to rank answers, and the extracted) Tj
T*
(features from data to be used for recommendations later on. Because recomputing features is an) Tj
T*
(expensive operation, HBase can be a good option to store and retrieve data at high bandwidth.) Tj
T*
(We require high read/write throughput because big data processing systems use high parallelism) Tj
T*
(to efficiently get the required statistics. Also, blob storage is required to store videos and) Tj
T*
(images posted in questions and answers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Quora was founded in 2009, whereas HBase was developed in 2008 by Apache. Because it is open-) Tj
T*
(source and modeled after Google’s BigTable, it is suitable for storing a large amount of small-) Tj
T*
(sized data. Furthermore, it has high read/write throughput. Therefore, it was a natural choice) Tj
T*
(for Quora to use in its inception.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Distributed cache: For performance improvement, two distributed cache systems are used:) Tj
T*
(Memcached and Redis. Memcached is primarily used to store frequently accessed critical data) Tj
T*
(that is otherwise stored in MySQL. On the other hand, Redis is mainly used to store an online) Tj
T*
(view counter of answers because it allows in-store increments. Therefore, two cache systems are) Tj
T*
(employed according to their use case. Apart from these two, CDNs serve frequently accessed) Tj
T*
(videos and images.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Compute servers: A set of compute servers are required to facilitate features like) Tj
T*
(recommendations and ranking based on a set of attributes. These features can be computed in) Tj
T*
(online or offline mode. The compute servers use machine learning \(ML\) technology to provide) Tj
T*
(effective recommendations. Naturally, these compute servers have a substantially high amount of) Tj
T*
(RAM and processing power.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
