T*
() Tj
T*
(Of course, other basic building blocks like load balancers, monitoring services, and rate) Tj
T*
(limiters will also be part of the design. A high-level design is provided below:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The high-level design of Quora]\(./hld.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Workflow) Tj
T*
(The design of Quora is complex because we have a large number of functional and non-functional) Tj
T*
(requirements. Therefore, we’ll explain the workflow on the basis of each feature:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Posting question, answers, comments: The web servers receive user requests through the load) Tj
T*
(balancer and direct them to the application servers. Meanwhile, the web servers generate part) Tj
T*
(of the web page and let the worker process in the application servers do the rest of the page) Tj
T*
(generation. The questions and answers data is stored in a MySQL database, whereas any videos) Tj
T*
(and images are stored in the blob storage. A similar approach is used to post comments and) Tj
T*
(upvote or downvote answers. Task prioritization is performed by employing different queues for) Tj
T*
(different tasks. We perform prioritization because certain tasks require immediate) Tj
T*
(attention—for example, fetching data from the database for a user request—while others are not) Tj
T*
(so urgent—for example, sending a weekly email digest. The worker processes will perform tasks) Tj
T*
(by fetching from these queues.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Question 1) Tj
T*
(When would a service like Quora require a notifications feature?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(Quora will need a notification service in the following scenarios:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A user posts a question on a topic subscribed by a would-be respondent.) Tj
T*
(A user posts an answer to a question asked by another user.) Tj
T*
(A post a user is interested in or wrote received new comments or upvotes/downvotes, and so on.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Question 2) Tj
T*
(How is it possible for Quora to send notifications to users through the above-described) Tj
T*
(mechanism?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Hide Answer) Tj
T*
(Since tasks are added to different priority queues, it is possible to maintain a queue for) Tj
T*
(notifications. While higher priority tasks are enqueued to high-priority queues, a notification) Tj
T*
(task will be added to a medium or lower priority queue. The illustration below visualizes the) Tj
T*
(described concept:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Notifications]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Answer ranking system: Answers to questions can be sorted based on date. Although it is) Tj
T*
(convenient to develop a ranking system on the basis of date \(using time stamps\), users prefer) Tj
T*
(to see the most appropriate answer at the top. Therefore, Quora uses ML to rank answers.) Tj
T*
(Different features are extracted over time and stored in the HBase for each type of question.) Tj
T*
(These features are forwarded to the ML engine to rank the most useful answer at the top. We) Tj
T*
(cannot use the number of upvotes as the only metric for ranking answers because a good number) Tj
T*
(of answers can be jokes—and such answers also get a lot of upvotes. It is good to implement the) Tj
T*
(ranking system offline because good answers get upvotes and views over time. Also, the offline) Tj
T*
(mode poses a lesser burden on the infrastructure. Implementing the ranking system offline and) Tj
T*
(the need for special ML hardware makes it suitable to use some public cloud elastic services.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
