(Question) Tj
T*
(Why is there a custom routing layer between the web and application servers instead of a load-) Tj
T*
(balancing layer?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Hide Answer) Tj
T*
(The primary reason is performance. A generic load-balancing layer will have little application) Tj
T*
(understandability and higher latency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(As stated, the manager processes generate the skeleton of the web page and leave the majority) Tj
T*
(of the work to worker processes. In that sense, one manager process can generate multiple) Tj
T*
(worker tasks. The custom router library is a queue between manager and worker, where any worker) Tj
T*
(process can consume a task generated by the manager process.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This design improves the overall performance and supports scalability.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(router library: Quora refers to it as “Fastrouter”–it is a custom C++ built queue server.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
