T*
() Tj
T*
(Requests Per Second \(RPS\)       69444) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We already established in the back-of-the-envelope calculations chapter that we’ll use the) Tj
T*
(following formula to estimate a pragmatic number of servers:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Number of daily active users/ RPS of a server= 300 x 10^6/8000=37500) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The estimated number of servers required for Quora]\(./servers.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Therefore, the total number of servers required to facilitate 300 million users generating an) Tj
T*
(average of 69,500 requests per second will be 37,500.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Storage estimation) Tj
T*
(Let’s keep in mind our assumption that 15% of questions have images and 5% have videos. So,) Tj
T*
(we’ll make the following assumptions to estimate the storage requirements for our design:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Each of the 300 million active users posts 1 question in a day, and each question has 2) Tj
T*
(responses on average, 10 upvotes, and 5 comments in total.) Tj
T*
(- The collective storage required for the textual content of one question equals 1 KB.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
