(## Building blocks we will use) Tj
T*
(We’ll use the following building blocks for the initial design of Quora:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Building blocks required for our design]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Load balancers will be used to divide the traffic load among the service hosts.) Tj
T*
(- Databases are essential for storing all sorts of data, such as user questions and answers,) Tj
T*
(comments, and likes and dislikes. Also, user data will be stored in the databases. We may use) Tj
T*
(different types of databases to store different data.) Tj
T*
(- A distributed caching system will be used to store frequently accessed data. We can also use) Tj
T*
(caching to store our view counters for different questions.) Tj
T*
(- The blob store will keep images and video files.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Design Quora/System Design Quora/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# System Design: Quora) Tj
T*
(## Introduction) Tj
T*
(With so much information available online, finding answers to questions can be daunting. That’s) Tj
T*
(why information sharing online has become so widespread.. Search engines help us dig for) Tj
T*
(information across the web. For example, Google’s search engine is intelligent enough to answer) Tj
T*
(questions by extracting information from web pages. While search engines have their advantages,) Tj
T*
(sometimes finding the information we want isn’t a straightforward process. Let’s look at the) Tj
T*
(illustration below to understand how seeking information through search engines is different in) Tj
T*
(comparison to people.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Comparing information seeking through search engines vs. humans]\(./infoseeking.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
