<< /Length 3971 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
12 TL
50 780 Td
(The illustration above depicts that information-seeking through other people can be more) Tj
T*
(instructive, even if it comes at the cost of additional time. Seeking information through) Tj
T*
(search engines can lead to dead ends because of content unavailability on a topic. Instead, we) Tj
T*
(can ask questions of others.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## What is Quora?) Tj
T*
(Quora is a social question-and-answer service that allows users to ask questions to other) Tj
T*
(users. Quora was created because of the issue that asking questions from search engines results) Tj
T*
(in fast answers but shallow information. Instead, we can ask the general public, which feels) Tj
T*
(more conversational and can result in deeper understanding, even if it’s slower. Quora enables) Tj
T*
(anyone to ask questions, and anyone can reply. Furthermore, there are domain experts that have) Tj
T*
(in-depth knowledge of a specific topic who occasionally share their expertise by answering) Tj
T*
(questions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The following plot shows global user search trends for the term “Quora” using Google:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Popularity of Quora according to Google by year]\(./popularity.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(More than 300 million monthly active users post thousands of questions daily related to more) Tj
T*
(than 400,000 topics on Quora.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In this chapter, we’ll design Quora and evaluate how it fulfills the functional and non-) Tj
T*
(functional requirements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## How will we design Quora?) Tj
T*
(We'll design Quora by dividing the design problem into the following four lessons.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Requirements: This lesson will focus on the functional and non-functional requirements for) Tj
