(server \(Tweet service\) receives the requests and performs multiple operations. It identifies) Tj
T*
(the attachments \(image, video\) in the Tweet and stores them in the Blobstore. Text in the) Tj
T*
(Tweets, user information, and all metadata are stored in the different databases \(Manhattan,) Tj
T*
(MySQL, Postgresql, Vertica\). Meanwhile, real-time processing, such as pulling Tweets, user) Tj
T*
(interactions data, and many other metrics from the real-time streams and client logs, is) Tj
T*
(achieved in the Apache Kafka.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Later, the data is moved to the cloud pub-sub through an event processor. Next, data is) Tj
T*
(transferred for deduping and aggregation to the BigQuery through Cloud Dataflow. Finally, data) Tj
T*
(is stored in the Google Cloud Bigtable, which is fully managed, easily scalable, and sorted) Tj
T*
(keys.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  - Timeline service: Assume the user sends a home timeline request using the) Tj
T*
(/viewHome_timeline API. In this case, the request is forwarded to the nearest CDN containing) Tj
T*
(static data. If the requested data is not found, it’s sent to the server providing timeline) Tj
T*
(services. This service fetches data from different databases or stores and returns the Top-k) Tj
T*
(Tweets. This service collects various interactions counts of Tweets from different sharded) Tj
T*
(counters to decide the Top-k Tweets. In a similar way, we will obtain the Top-k trends attached) Tj
T*
(in the response to the timeline request.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  - Search service: When users type any keyword\(s\) in the search bar on Twitter, the search) Tj
T*
(request is forwarded to the respective server using the /searchTweet API. It first looks into) Tj
T*
(the RAM in Apache Lucene to get real-time Tweets \(Tweets that have been published recently\).) Tj
T*
(Then, this server looks up in the index server and finds all Tweets that contain the requested) Tj
T*
(keyword\(s\). Next, it considers multiple factors, such as time, or location, to rank the) Tj
T*
(discovered Tweets. In the end, it returns the top Tweets.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- We can use the Zipkin tracing system that performs sampling on requests. Moreover, we can use) Tj
T*
(Zookeeper to maintain different data, including configuration information, distributed) Tj
T*
(synchronization, naming registry, and so on.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Design]\(./twitter_design.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Design Twitter/High-level Design of Twitter/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# High-level Design of Twitter) Tj
