(## Requirements) Tj
T*
(Let’s understand the functional and non-functional requirements below:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Functional requirements) Tj
T*
(The following are the functional requirements of Twitter:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Post Tweets: Registered users can post one or more Tweets on Twitter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Delete Tweets: Registered users can delete one or more of their Tweets on Twitter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Like or dislike Tweets: Registered users can like and dislike public and their own Tweets on) Tj
T*
(Twitter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Reply to Tweets: Registered users can reply to the public Tweets on Twitter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Search Tweets: Registered users can search Tweets by typing keywords, hashtags, or usernames) Tj
T*
(in the search bar on Twitter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- View user or home timeline: Registered users can view the user’s timeline, which contains) Tj
T*
(their own Tweets. They can also view the home’s timeline, which contains followers’ Tweets on) Tj
T*
(Twitter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Follow or unfollow the account: Registered users can follow or unfollow other users on) Tj
T*
(Twitter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Retweet a Tweet: Registered users can Retweet public Tweets of other users on Twitter.) Tj
T*
