(## Fulfill requirements) Tj
T*
(The non-functional requirements of the proposed typeahead suggestion system are low latency,) Tj
T*
(fault tolerance, and scalability.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Low latency: There are various levels at which we can minimize the system’s latency. We can) Tj
T*
(minimize the latency with the following options:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  - Reduce the depth of the tree, which reduces the overall traversal time.) Tj
T*
(  - Update the trie offline, which means that the time taken by the update operation isn’t on) Tj
T*
(the clients’ critical path.) Tj
T*
(  - Use geographically distributed application and database servers. This way, the service is) Tj
T*
(provided near the user, which also reduces any communication delays and aids in reducing) Tj
T*
(latency.) Tj
T*
(  - Use Redis and Cassandra cache clusters on top of NoSQL database clusters.) Tj
T*
(  - Appropriately partition tries, which leads to a proper distribution of the load and results) Tj
T*
(in better performance.) Tj
T*
(- Fault tolerance: Since the replication and partitioning of the trees are provided, the system) Tj
T*
(operates with high resilience. If one server fails, others are on standby to deliver the) Tj
T*
(services.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Scalability: Since our proposed system is flexible, more servers can be added or removed as) Tj
T*
(the load increases. For example, if the number of queries increases, the number of partitions) Tj
T*
(or shards of the trees is increased accordingly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
