(## Design Typeahead Suggestion/Requirements of the Typeahead Suggestion System’s) Tj
T*
(Design/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Requirements of the Typeahead Suggestion System’s Design) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Requirements) Tj
T*
(In this lesson, we look into the requirements and estimated resources that are necessary for) Tj
T*
(the design of the typeahead suggestion system. Our proposed design should meet the following) Tj
T*
(requirements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Functional requirements) Tj
T*
(The system should suggest top N \(let’s say top ten\) frequent and relevant terms to the user) Tj
T*
(based on the text a user types in the search box.) Tj
T*
(### Non-functional requirements) Tj
T*
(- Low latency: The system should show all the suggested queries in real time after a user) Tj
T*
(types. The latency shouldn’t exceed 200 ms. A study suggests that the average time between two) Tj
T*
(keystrokes is 160 milliseconds. So, our time-budget of suggestions should be greater than 160) Tj
T*
(ms to give a real-time response. This is because if a user is typing fast, they already know) Tj
T*
(what to search and might not need suggestions. At the same time, our system response should be) Tj
T*
(greater than 160 ms. However, it should not be too high because in that case, a suggestion) Tj
T*
(might be stale and less useful.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Fault tolerance: The system should be reliable enough to provide suggestions despite the) Tj
T*
(failure of one or more of its components.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Scalability: The system should support the ever-increasing number of users over time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Resource estimation) Tj
T*
(As was stated earlier, the typeahead feature is used to enhance the user experience while) Tj
T*
(typing a query. We need to design a system that works on a scale that’s similar to Google) Tj
T*
(Search. Google receives more than 3.5 billion searches every day. Designing such an enormous) Tj
T*
(system is a challenging task that requires different resources. Let’s estimate the storage and) Tj
T*
(bandwidth requirements for the proposed system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Storage estimation) Tj
T*
(Assuming that out of the 3.5 billion queries per day, two billion queries are unique and need) Tj
T*
(to be stored. Let’s also assume that each query consists of 15 characters on average, and each) Tj
T*
(character takes 2 Bytes of storage. According to this formulation, we would require the) Tj
T*
(following:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2 billion x ×15×2=60GB to store all the queries made in a day.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Storage required per year:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(60GB/day×365=21.9TB/year) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
