(```) Tj
T*
(## Design) Tj
T*
(Let’s look at the design of the payment platform in Uber and learn how different components) Tj
T*
(work together to complete the transactions:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The payment platform in Uber]\(./payment_platform.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The key components used in the payment service are as follows:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- API: The Uber API is used to access the payment service.) Tj
T*
(- Order store: This stores all the orders. Orders collect payments and contain information) Tj
T*
(regarding money flow between different riders and drivers.) Tj
T*
(- Account store: This stores all the accounts of riders and drivers.) Tj
T*
(- Risk engine: The risk engine analyzes different risks involved in collecting payment from a) Tj
T*
(particular rider. It checks the history of the rider—for example, the rating of the rider, if) Tj
T*
(the rider has sufficient funds in their rider account, any pending dues, if the rider cancels) Tj
T*
(the rides frequently, and so on.) Tj
T*
(- Payment profile service: This provides information on the payment mechanisms, such as credit) Tj
T*
(and debit cards.) Tj
T*
(- User profile service: This provides information regarding users’ payments.) Tj
T*
(- Payment authorization service: This offers payment authentication services.) Tj
T*
(- PSP gateways: This connects with payment service providers) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Workflow) Tj
T*
(The following steps show the workflow of the payment service:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. When a rider requests a ride, the Uber application uses the Uber API to request the risk) Tj
T*
(engine to check the risks involved.) Tj
T*
(3. The risk engine obtains user information from the user profile service and evaluates the) Tj
T*
(risk involved.) Tj
T*
(3. If the risks are high, the rider’s request isn’t entertained.) Tj
T*
(4. If the risks are low, the risk engine creates an authorization token and sends it to the) Tj
T*
(payment profile service \(for record-keeping\), which fetches that token and sends it to the) Tj
T*
(payment authorization service.) Tj
T*
(5. The payment authorization service sends that request to the PSP gateway, which contacts the) Tj
T*
(service provider for authorization.) Tj
T*
(6. The PSP gateway sends the authorization token back to the payment authorization service,) Tj
T*
(which sends the token back to the Uber application that the trip request is approved.) Tj
T*
(7. After the trip is completed, the Uber application uses the API to send the payment request) Tj
T*
(to the PSP gateway with authorization data.) Tj
T*
(8. The PSP gateway contacts the service provider and sends the status back to the Uber) Tj
T*
(application through the API.) Tj
T*
(The Uber payment service is constructed with a set of microservices grouped together as a) Tj
T*
(stream-processing architecture.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Apache Kafka) Tj
T*
(Kafka is an open-source stream-processing software platform. It’s the primary technology used) Tj
T*
(in payment services. Let’s see how Kafka helps to process an order:) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Stream processing is a computer programming paradigm that simplifies parallel software and) Tj
T*
(hardware by restricting the parallel computation that can be performed. Given a sequence of) Tj
T*
(data \(a stream\), a series of operations \(kernel functions\) is applied to each element in the) Tj
T*
(stream. Source: Wikipedia) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Payment service with Kafka]\(./payment_service.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The order creator gets a business event—for example, the trip is finished. The order creator) Tj
T*
(creates the money movement information and the metadata. This order creator publishes that) Tj
T*
(information to Kafka. Kafka processes that order and sends it to the order processor. The order) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
