T*
(RADAR recognizes the beginning of a fraud attempt and creates a rule to prevent it. The fraud) Tj
T*
(analyst is involved in the next step. They review the rule and approve or reject it if) Tj
T*
(required. They then send feedback \(approved or not approved\) to the protection system. The) Tj
T*
(feedback is also sent to the fraud detection system by the fraud analysts to improve detection.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Furthermore, the system examines the data in the following time dimensions:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- It examines the trip time when a trip has been completed. Multiple factors are involved in) Tj
T*
(real-time trip monitoring. For instance, the system can check whether or not the driver and) Tj
T*
(rider locations are the same. The system can also monitor the speed and analyze the real) Tj
T*
(traffic to check if the driver is intentionally driving slow or if there’s traffic congestion.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Payment settlement time refers to obtaining payment processing data. It might take days or) Tj
T*
(weeks to settle.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We’ve just discussed the basic details of how guarding against malicious activity at scale is) Tj
T*
(necessary for the success of a business. In the proposed model, the human experts are involved,) Tj
T*
(potentially decreasing the scalability of the system. Research is being carried out on how to) Tj
T*
(ensure that the decisions made by the AI system are fair and ethical.) Tj
T*
() Tj
