T*
(# Requirements of Uber’s Design) Tj
T*
(## Requirements) Tj
T*
(Let’s start with the requirements for designing a system like Uber.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Functional requirements) Tj
T*
(The functional requirements of our system are as follows:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Update driver location: The driver is a moving entity, so the driver’s location should be) Tj
T*
(automatically updated at regular intervals.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Find nearby drivers: The system should find and show the nearby available drivers to the) Tj
T*
(rider.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Request a ride: A rider should be able to request a ride, after which the nearest driver) Tj
T*
(should be notified about the rider’s requests.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Manage payments: At the start of the trip, the system must initiate the payment process and) Tj
T*
(manage the payments.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Show driver estimated time of arrival \(ETA\): The rider should be able to see the estimated) Tj
T*
(time of arrival of the driver.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Confirm pickup: Drivers should be able to confirm that they have picked up the rider.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Show trip updates: Once a driver and a rider accept a ride, they should be able to constantly) Tj
T*
(see trip updates like ETA and current location until the trip finishes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- End the trip: The driver marks the journey complete upon reaching the destination, and they) Tj
T*
(then become available for the next ride.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question) Tj
T*
(What if two drivers are at the same distance from the rider? How will we select the driver to) Tj
T*
(whom we’ll send the request?) Tj
T*
