T*
(### Non-functional requirements) Tj
T*
(The non-functional requirements of our system are as follows:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Availability: The system should be highly available. The downtime of even a fraction of a) Tj
T*
(second can result in a trip failure, in the driver being unable to locate the rider, or in the) Tj
T*
(rider being unable to contact the driver.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Scalability: The system should be scalable to handle an ever-increasing number of drivers and) Tj
T*
(riders with time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Reliability: The system should provide fast and error-free services. Ride requests and) Tj
T*
(location updates should happen smoothly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Consistency: The system must be strongly consistent. The drivers and riders in an area should) Tj
T*
(have a consistent view of the system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Fraud detection: The system should have the ability to detect any fraudulent activity related) Tj
T*
(to payment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Resource estimation) Tj
T*
(Now, let’s estimate the resources for our design. Let’s assume it has around 500 million riders) Tj
T*
(and about five million drivers. We’ll assume the following numbers for our estimates:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- We have 20 million daily active riders and three million daily active drivers.) Tj
T*
(- We have 20 million daily trips.) Tj
T*
(- All active drivers send a notification of their current location every four seconds.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Storage estimation) Tj
T*
(Let’s estimate the storage required for our system:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Rider’s metadata) Tj
T*
(Let’s assume we need around 1,000 Bytes to store each rider’s information, including ID, name,) Tj
T*
(email, and so on, when the rider registers in our application. To store the 500 million riders,) Tj
T*
(we require 500 GB of storage:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(500×10^ 6×1000=500 GB) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Additionally, if we have around 500,000 new riders registered daily, we’ll need a further 500) Tj
T*
(MB to store them.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Driver’s metadata) Tj
T*
(Let’s assume we need around 1,000 Bytes to store each driver’s information, including ID, name,) Tj
T*
(email, vehicle type, and so on, when the driver registers in our application. To store the five) Tj
T*
(million drivers, we require 5 GB of storage:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5×10^6×1000=5 GB) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Additionally, if we have around 100,00 new drivers registered daily, we’ll need around 100 MB) Tj
T*
(to store them.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Driver location metadata) Tj
T*
(Let’s assume we need around 36 Bytes to store the driver’s location updates. If we have five) Tj
T*
(million drivers, we need around 180 MB of storage just for the drivers’ locations.) Tj
T*
ET
