(Why is WebSocket preferred over HTTP\(S\) protocol for client-server communication?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(HTTP\(S\) doesn’t keep the connection open for the servers to send frequent data to a client.) Tj
T*
(With HTTP\(S\) protocol, a client constantly requests updates from the server, commonly called) Tj
T*
(polling, which is resource intensive and causes latency. WebSocket maintains a persistent) Tj
T*
(connection between the client and a server. This protocol transfers data to the client) Tj
T*
