T*
(At registration time, a WhatsApp client generates a number of public-private key pairs that) Tj
T*
(include keys pairs for identity, a signed prekey, and a batch of one-time prekeys. These keys) Tj
T*
(are used for different purposes. The public keys are stored in the database associated with the) Tj
T*
(user service along with the user’s identifier. Whenever a sender wants to establish a) Tj
T*
(connection with the receiver, it also requests the server for the keys associated with a) Tj
T*
(receiver’s ID. Private keys are only stored on the client’s end devices.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(One-to-one communication) Tj
T*
(To communicate securely, WhatsApp clients, on both sender and receiver sides, establish a) Tj
T*
(pairwise encrypted session with each other. The session is created using the following steps:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The sender requests the public identity key, signed prekey, and a single public one-time prekey) Tj
T*
(of the receiver’s device. The one-time prekey is used only once.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The WhatsApp server returns the requested public keys of the receiver.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The sender generates an ephemeral Curve25519 key pair.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The sender creates a master secret key using its own identity key, the ephemeral key pair, and) Tj
T*
(the receiver’s public keys.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The sender uses the HMAC-based key-derivation function \(HKDF\) to create two other keys known as) Tj
T*
(a root key and chain key from the master secret key. The sender starts sending messages to the) Tj
T*
(receiver after establishing the pairwise encrypted session. The receiver creates the same) Tj
T*
(session based on the information present in the header of the first receiving message.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(After establishing a session, an 80-byte Message Key is generated based on the root and chain) Tj
T*
(Keys. The Message Key is used for encryption and authentication of messages.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Group communication) Tj
T*
(The communication in a WhatsApp group is handled by the same process discussed in the previous) Tj
T*
(section on one-to-one communication. A sender key, used by the signaling messaging protocol, is) Tj
T*
(generated and shared with each member’s device of the group using the pairwise encrypted) Tj
T*
