(## Fulfill the requirements) Tj
T*
(Our non-functional requirements for the proposed WhatsApp design are low latency, consistency,) Tj
T*
(availability, and security. Let’s discuss how we have achieved these requirements in our) Tj
T*
(system:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Low latency: We can minimize the latency of the system at various levels:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  - We can do this through geographically distributed WebSocket servers and the cache) Tj
T*
(associated with them.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  - We can use Redis cache clusters on top of MySQL database clusters.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  - We can use CDNs for frequently sharing documents and media content.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Consistency: The system also provides high consistency in messages with the help of a FIFO) Tj
T*
(messaging queue with strict ordering. However, the ordering of messages would require the) Tj
T*
(Sequencer to provide ID with appropriate causality inference mechanisms to each message. For) Tj
T*
(offline users, the Mnesia database stores messages in a queue. The messages are sent later in a) Tj
T*
(sequence after the user goes online.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
