(## Trade-offs) Tj
T*
(We’ve seen that our proposed WhatsApp system fulfills the functional and non-functional) Tj
T*
(requirements. However, two major trade-offs exist in the proposed WhatsApp design:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- There’s a trade-off between consistency and availability.) Tj
T*
(- There’s a trade-off between latency and security.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### The trade-off between consistency and availability) Tj
T*
(According to the CAP theorem, in the event of a network failure or partition, the system can) Tj
T*
(provide either consistency or availability. So, in the case of our WhatsApp design, we have to) Tj
T*
(choose either consistency or availability. In WhatsApp, the order of messages sent or received) Tj
T*
(by a user is essential. Therefore, we should prioritize consistency rather than availability.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### The trade-off between latency and security) Tj
T*
(Low latency is an essential factor in system design that provides a real-time experience to) Tj
T*
ET
