(## Design WhatsApp/High-level Design of WhatsApp/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# High-level Design of WhatsApp) Tj
T*
(## High-level design) Tj
T*
(At an abstract level, the high-level design consists of a chat server responsible for) Tj
T*
(communication between the sender and the receiver. When a user wants to send a message to) Tj
T*
(another user, both connect to the chat server. Both users send their messages to the chat) Tj
T*
(server. The chat server then sends the message to the other intended user and also stores the) Tj
T*
(message in the database.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The high-level design of WhatsApp messenger]\(./design.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The following steps describe the communication between both clients:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. User A and user B create a communication channel with the chat server.) Tj
T*
(2. User A sends a message to the chat server.) Tj
T*
(3. Upon receiving the message, the chat server acknowledges back to user A.) Tj
T*
(4. The chat server sends the message to user B and stores the message in the database if the) Tj
T*
(receiver’s status is offline.) Tj
T*
(5. User B sends an acknowledgment to the chat server.) Tj
T*
(6. The chat server notifies user A that the message has been successfully delivered.) Tj
T*
(7. When user B reads the message, the application notifies the chat server.) Tj
