(## Requirements) Tj
T*
(Our design of the WhatsApp messenger should meet the following requirements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Functional requirements) Tj
T*
(- Conversation: The system should support one-on-one and group conversations between users.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Acknowledgment: The system should support message delivery acknowledgment, such as sent,) Tj
T*
(delivered, and read.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Sharing: The system should support sharing of media files, such as images, videos, and audio.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Chat storage: The system must support the persistent storage of chat messages when a user is) Tj
T*
(offline until the successful delivery of messages.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- ush notifications: The system should be able to notify offline users of new messages once) Tj
T*
(their status becomes online.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Non-functional requirements) Tj
T*
(- Low latency: Users should be able to receive messages with low latency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Consistency: Messages should be delivered in the order they were sent. Moreover, users must) Tj
T*
(see the same chat history on all of their devices.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Availability: The system should be highly available. However, the availability can be) Tj
T*
(compromised in the interest of consistency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Security: The system must be secure via end-to-end encryption. The end-to-end encryption) Tj
T*
(ensures that only the two communicating parties can see the content of messages. Nobody in) Tj
T*
(between, not even WhatsApp, should have access.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The non-functional requirements of the WhatsApp system]\(./nfr.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Resource estimation) Tj
T*
(WhatsApp is the most used messaging application across the globe. According to WhatsApp, it) Tj
T*
(supports more than two billion users around the world who share more than 100 billion messages) Tj
T*
(each day. We need to estimate the storage capacity, bandwidth, and number of servers to support) Tj
T*
(such an enormous number of users and messages.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Storage estimation) Tj
T*
(As there are more than 100 billion messages shared per day over WhatsApp, let’s estimate the) Tj
T*
(storage capacity based on this figure. Assume that each message takes 100 Bytes on average.) Tj
T*
(Moreover, the WhatsApp servers keep the messages only for 30 days. So, if the user doesn’t get) Tj
T*
(connected to the server within these days, the messages will be permanently deleted from the) Tj
T*
(server.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(100 billion/day∗100 Bytes=10 TB/day) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For 30 days, the storage capacity would become the following:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(30∗10 TB/day=300 TB/month) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Besides chat messages, we also have media files, which take more than 100 Bytes per message.) Tj
T*
(Moreover, we also have to store users’ information and messages’ metadata—for example, time) Tj
T*
(stamp, ID, and so on. Along the way, we also need encryption and decryption for secure) Tj
T*
(communication. Therefore, we would also need to store encryption keys and relevant metadata.) Tj
T*
(So, to be precise, we need more than 300 TB per month, but for the sake of simplicity, let’s) Tj
T*
(stick to the number 300 TB per month.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The total storage required by WhatsApp in a month]\(./storage.jpg\)) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
