(## Design WhatsApp/System Design WhatsApp/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# System Design: WhatsApp) Tj
T*
(## WhatsApp) Tj
T*
(In today’s technological world, WhatsApp is an important messaging application that connects) Tj
T*
(billions of people around the globe. Many users start their day by reading or sending WhatsApp) Tj
T*
(messages to their friends and family. According to July 2021 estimates, WhatsApp has two) Tj
T*
(billion active users worldwide. Further, an average WhatsApp user spends approximately 19.4) Tj
T*
(hours per month on the application.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In December 2020, the WhatsApp CEO tweeted that WhatsApp users share more than 100 billion) Tj
T*
(messages per day, an increase of approximately 54% since 2018. The increase in messages sent) Tj
T*
(globally per day is depicted in the following chart:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Design problem) Tj
T*
(As system designers, we should be aware of the growth rate of users. There are many interesting) Tj
T*
(questions about WhatsApp:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- How is this application designed?) Tj
T*
(- How does it work?) Tj
T*
(- What are the different types of components involved in it?) Tj
T*
(- How does WhatsApp enable billions of users to communicate with each other?) Tj
T*
(- How does WhatsApp keep all that data secure?) Tj
T*
(In this chapter, we’ll focus on the high-level and detailed design of the WhatsApp application) Tj
T*
(to answer the above questions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## How will we design WhatsApp?) Tj
T*
(We’ve divided the design of WhatsApp messenger into the following five lessons:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Requirements: In this lesson, we’ll identify functional and non-functional requirements.) Tj
T*
(We’ll also discuss resource estimations required for better and smooth operations of the) Tj
T*
(proposed design of WhatsApp.) Tj
T*
(2. High-level Design: We’ll focus on the high-level design of our WhatsApp version. We’ll also) Tj
T*
(discuss essential APIs for our WhatsApp design.) Tj
T*
(3. Detailed Design: In this lesson, we’ll describe the design of our WhatsApp messenger in) Tj
T*
(detail. Initially, we’ll explain the design of each microservice, including connection with) Tj
T*
(servers, send and receive messages and media content, and group messages. In the end, the) Tj
T*
(design of each microservice is combined into the detailed design of WhatsApp.) Tj
T*
(4. Evaluation: This lesson will explain how our version of WhatsApp fulfills non-functional) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
