(## Design Youtube/Design of YouTube/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Design of YouTube) Tj
T*
(## High-level design) Tj
T*
(The high-level design shows how we’ll interconnect the various components we identified in the) Tj
T*
(previous lesson. We have started developing a solution to support the functional and non-) Tj
T*
(functional requirements with this design.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The high-level design of YouTube]\(./sys.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The workflow for the abstract design is provided below:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. The user uploads a video to the server.) Tj
T*
(2. The server stores the metadata and the accompanying user data to the database and, at the) Tj
T*
(same time, hands over the video to the encoder for encoding \(see 2.1 and 2.2 in the) Tj
T*
(illustration above\).) Tj
T*
(3. The encoder, along with the transcoder, compresses the video and transforms it into multiple) Tj
T*
(resolutions \(like 2160p, 1440p, 1080p, and so on\). The videos are stored on blob storage) Tj
T*
(\(similar to GFS or S3\).) Tj
T*
(4. Some popular videos may be forwarded to the CDN, which acts as a cache.) Tj
T*
(5. The CDN, because of its vicinity to the user, lets the user stream the video with low) Tj
T*
(latency. However, CDN is not the only infrastructure for serving videos to the end user, which) Tj
T*
(we will see in the detailed design.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question) Tj
T*
(Why don’t we upload the video directly to the encoder instead of to the server? Doesn’t the) Tj
T*
(current strategy introduce an additional delay?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(There are several reasons why it’s a good idea to introduce a server in between the encoder and) Tj
T*
(the client:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- The client could be malicious and could abuse the encoder.) Tj
T*
(- If the uploaded video is a duplicate, the server could filter it out.) Tj
T*
(- Encoders will be available on a private IP address within YouTube’s network and not available) Tj
T*
(for public access.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## API design) Tj
T*
(Let’s understand the design of APIs in terms of the functionalities we’re providing. We’ll) Tj
T*
(design APIs to translate our feature set into technical specifications. In this case, REST APIs) Tj
T*
(can be used for simplicity and speed purposes. Our API design section will help us understand) Tj
T*
(how the client will request services from the back-end application of YouTube. Let’s develop) Tj
T*
(APIs for each of the following features:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Upload videos) Tj
T*
(- Stream videos) Tj
T*
(- Search videos) Tj
T*
(- View thumbnails) Tj
T*
(- Like or dislike videos) Tj
T*
(- Comment on videos) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([API design overview]\(./api.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Upload video) Tj
T*
