([Storage schema]\(./db.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: Much of the underlying details regarding database tables that can be mapped to services) Tj
T*
(provided by YouTube have been omitted for simplicity. For example, one video can have different) Tj
T*
(qualities and that is not mentioned in the “Video” table.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Detailed design) Tj
T*
(Now, let’s get back to our high-level design and see if we can further explore parts of the) Tj
T*
(design. In particular, the following areas require more discussion:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Component integration: We’ll cover some interconnections between the servers and storage) Tj
T*
(components to better understand how the system will work.) Tj
T*
(- Thumbnails: It’s important for users to see some parts of the video through thumbnails.) Tj
T*
(Therefore, we’ll add thumbnail generation and storage to the detailed design.) Tj
T*
(- Database structure: Our estimation showed that we require massive storage space. We also) Tj
T*
(require storing varying types of data, such as videos, video metadata, and thumbnails, each of) Tj
T*
(which demands specialized data storage for performance reasons. Understanding the database) Tj
T*
(details will enable us to design a system with the least possible lag.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Let’s take a look at the diagram below. We’ll explain our design in two steps, where the first) Tj
T*
(looks at what the newly added components are, and the second considers how they coordinate to) Tj
T*
(build the YouTube system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Detailed design components) Tj
T*
(Since we highlighted the requirements of smooth streaming, server-level details, and thumbnail) Tj
T*
(features, the following design will meet our expectations. Let’s explain the purpose of each) Tj
T*
(added component here:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Load balancers: To divide a large number of user requests among the web servers, we require) Tj
T*
(load balancers.) Tj
T*
(- Web servers: Web servers take in user requests and respond to them. These can be considered) Tj
T*
(the interface to our API servers that entertain user requests.) Tj
T*
ET
