391 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Resources << /Font << /F1 3 0 R >> >> /Contents 390 0 R >>
endobj
392 0 obj
<< /Length 4418 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
12 TL
50 780 Td
(- Application server: The application and business logic resides in application servers. They) Tj
T*
(prepare the data needed by the web servers to handle the end users’ queries.) Tj
T*
(- User and metadata storage: Since we have a large number of users and videos, the storage) Tj
T*
(required to hold the metadata of videos and the content related to users must be stored in) Tj
T*
(different storage clusters. This is because a large amount of not-so-related data should be) Tj
T*
(decoupled for scalability purposes.) Tj
T*
(- Bigtable: For each video, we’ll require multiple thumbnails. Bigtable is a good choice for) Tj
T*
(storing thumbnails because of its high throughput and scalability for storing key-value data.) Tj
T*
(Bigtable is optimal for storing a large number of data items each below 10 MB. Therefore, it is) Tj
T*
(the ideal choice for YouTube’s thumbnails.) Tj
T*
(- Upload storage: The upload storage is temporary storage that can store user-uploaded videos.) Tj
T*
(- Encoders: Each uploaded video requires compression and transcoding into various formats.) Tj
T*
(Thumbnail generation service is also obtained from the encoders.) Tj
T*
(- CDN and colocation sites: CDNs and colocation sites store popular and moderately popular) Tj
T*
(content that is closer to the user for easy access. Colocation centers are used where it’s not) Tj
T*
(possible to invest in a data center facility due to business reasons.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Bigtable: Chang, Fay, et al. “Bigtable: A distributed storage system for structured data.” ACM) Tj
T*
(Transactions on Computer Systems \(TOCS\) 26.2 \(2008\): 1-26.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Detailed design of YouTube’s components]\(./c.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Design flow and technology usage) Tj
T*
(Now that we understand the purpose of every component, let’s discuss the flow and technology) Tj
T*
(used in different components in the following steps:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. The user can upload a video by connecting to the web servers. The web server can run Apache) Tj
T*
(or Lighttpd. Lighttpd is preferable because it can serve static pages and videos due to its) Tj
T*
(fast speed.) Tj
T*
(2. Requests from the web servers are passed onto application servers that can contact various) Tj
T*
(data stores to read or write user, videos, or videos’ metadata. There are separate web and) Tj
T*
(application servers because we want to decouple clients’ services from the application and) Tj
T*
(business logic. Different programming languages can be used on this layer to perform different) Tj
T*
(tasks efficiently. For example, the C programming language can be used for encryption.) Tj
T*
(Moreover, this gives us an additional layer of caching, where the most requested objects are) Tj
T*
(stored on the application server while the most frequently requested pages will be stored on) Tj
T*
(the web servers.) Tj
T*
(3. Multiple storage units are used. Let’s go through each of these:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    I. Upload storage is used to store user-uploaded videos before they are temporarily) Tj
T*
(encoded.) Tj
T*
(    II. User account data is stored in a separate database, whereas videos metadata is stored) Tj
T*
(separately. The idea is to separate the more frequently and less frequently accessed storage) Tj
T*
(clusters from each other for optimal access time. We can use MySQL if there are a limited) Tj
T*
(number of concurrent reads and writes. However, as the number of users—and therefore the number) Tj
T*
(of concurrent reads and writes—grows, we can move towards NoSQL types of data management) Tj
T*
(systems.) Tj
T*
(   III. Since Bigtable is based on Google File System \(GFS\), it is designed to store a large) Tj
T*
(number of small files with low retrieval latency. It is a reasonable choice for storing) Tj
T*
(thumbnails.) Tj
T*
(4. The encoders generate thumbnails and also store additional metadata related to videos in the) Tj
T*
(metadata database. It will also provide popular and moderately popular content to CDNs and) Tj
T*
(colocation servers, respectively.) Tj
T*
(5. The user can finally stream videos from any available site.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(A colocation server is placed in a colocation/carrier site that is equipped with storage and) Tj
T*
(networking resources. These resources can be rented to customers based on their needs.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
