(- Datastores) Tj
T*
(- Placing load balancers among each of the layers above) Tj
T*
(- Implementing distributed caches) Tj
T*
(Any infrastructure mentioned above requires some modifications and adaptation to the) Tj
T*
(application-level logic. For example, if we continue to increase our data in MySQL servers, it) Tj
T*
(can become a choke point. To effectively use a sharded database, we might have to make changes) Tj
T*
(to our database client to achieve a good level of performance and maintain the ACID \(atomicity,) Tj
T*
(consistency, isolation, durability\) properties. However, even if we continue to change to the) Tj
T*
(database client as we scale, its complexity may reach a point where it is no longer manageable.) Tj
T*
(Also note that we haven’t incorporated a disaster recovery mechanism into our design yet.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(To resolve the problems above, YouTube has developed a solution called Vitess.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Vitess system for scalability]\(./vitess.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The key idea in Vitess is to put an abstraction on top of all the database layers, giving the) Tj
T*
(database client the illusion that it is talking to a single database server. The single) Tj
T*
(database in this case is the Vitess system. Therefore, all the database-client complexity is) Tj
T*
(migrated to and handled by Vitess. This maintains the ACID properties because the internal) Tj
T*
(database in use is MySQL. However, we can enable scaling through partitioning. Consequently,) Tj
T*
(we’ll get a MySQL structured database that gives the performance of a NoSQL storage system. At) Tj
T*
(the same time, we won’t have to live with a rich database client \(application logic\). The) Tj
T*
(following illustration highlights how Vitess is able to achieve both scalability and structure.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Vitess on the scalability versus structure spectrum]\(./spectrum.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(One could imagine using techniques like data denormalization instead of the Vitess system.) Tj
T*
(However, data denormalization won’t work because it comes at the cost of reduced writing) Tj
T*
(performance. Even if our work is read-intensive, as the system scales, writing performance will) Tj
T*
(degrade to an unbearable limit.) Tj
T*
(## Web server) Tj
T*
(A web server is an extremely important component and, with scale, a custom web server can be a) Tj
T*
(viable solution. This is because most commercial or open-source solutions are general purpose) Tj
T*
(and are developed with a wide range of users in mind. Therefore, a custom solution for such a) Tj
T*
(successful service is desirable.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Let’s try an interesting exercise to see which server YouTube currently uses. Click on the) Tj
T*
