(## Design Youtube/Requirements of YouTube's Design/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Requirements of YouTube's Design) Tj
T*
(## Requirements) Tj
T*
(Let’s start with the requirements for designing a system like YouTube.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Functional requirements) Tj
T*
(We require that our system is able to perform the following functions:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Stream videos) Tj
T*
(2. Upload videos) Tj
T*
(3. Search videos according to titles) Tj
T*
(4. Like and dislike videos) Tj
T*
(5. Add comments to videos) Tj
T*
(6. View thumbnails) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Representation of the functional and non-functional requirements]\(./youtube.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Non-functional requirements) Tj
T*
(It’s important that our system also meets the following requirements:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- High availability: The system should be highly available. High availability requires a good) Tj
T*
(percentage of uptime. Generally, an uptime of 99% and above is considered good.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
