(# The Reality Is More Complicated) Tj
T*
(## Introduction) Tj
T*
(Now that we’ve understood the design well, let’s see how YouTube can optimize the usage of) Tj
T*
(storage and network demands while maintaining good quality of experience \(QoE\) for the end) Tj
T*
(user.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(QoE is the measure of a customer’s satisfaction with the experience of a particular service.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(When talking about providing effective service to end users, the following three steps are) Tj
T*
(important:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Encode: The raw videos uploaded to YouTube have significant storage requirements. It’s) Tj
T*
(possible to use various encoding schemes to reduce the size of these raw video files. Apart) Tj
T*
(from compression, the choice of encoding scheme will also depend on the types of end devices) Tj
T*
(used to stream the video content. Since multiple devices could be used to stream the same) Tj
T*
(video, we may have to encode the same video using different encoding schemes resulting in one) Tj
T*
(raw video file being converted into multiple files each encoded differently. This strategy will) Tj
T*
(result in a good user-perceived experience because of two reasons: users will save bandwidth) Tj
T*
(because the video file will be encoded and compressed to some limit, and the encoded video file) Tj
T*
(will be appropriate for the client for a smooth playback experience.) Tj
T*
(- Deploy: For low latency, content must be intelligently deployed so that it is closer to a) Tj
T*
(large number of end users. Not only will this reduce latency, but it will also put less burden) Tj
T*
(on the networks as well as YouTube’s core servers.) Tj
T*
(- Deliver: Delivering to the client requires knowledge about the client or device used for) Tj
T*
(playing the video. This knowledge will help in adapting to the client and network conditions.) Tj
T*
(Therefore, we’ll enable ourselves to serve content efficiently.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Let’s understand each phase in detail now.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Encode) Tj
T*
(Until now, we’ve considered encoding one video with different encoding schemes. However, if we) Tj
T*
(encode videos on a per-shot basis, we’ll divide the video into smaller time frames and encode) Tj
T*
(them individually. We can divide videos into shorter time frames and refer to them as segments.) Tj
T*
(Each segment will be encoded using multiple encoding schemes to generate different files called) Tj
T*
(chunks. The choice of encoding scheme for a segment will be based on the detail within the) Tj
T*
(segment to get optimized quality with lesser storage requirements. Eventually, each shot will) Tj
T*
(be encoded into multiple chunk sizes depending on the segment’s content and encoding scheme) Tj
T*
(used. As we divide the raw video into segments, we’ll see its advantages during the deployment) Tj
T*
(and delivery phase.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
