(## Deploy) Tj
T*
(As discussed in our design and evaluation sections, we have to bring the content closer to the) Tj
T*
(user. This has three main advantages:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Users will be able to stream videos quickly.) Tj
T*
(2. There will be a reduced burden on the origin servers.) Tj
T*
(3. Internet service providers \(ISPs\) will have spare bandwidth.) Tj
T*
(So, instead of streaming from our data centers directly, we can deploy chunks of popular videos) Tj
T*
(in CDNs and point of presence \(PoPs\) of ISPs. In places where there is no collaboration) Tj
T*
(possible with the ISPs, our content can be placed in internet exchange point \(IXPs\). We can put) Tj
T*
(content in IXPs that will not only be closer to users, but can also be helpful in filling the) Tj
T*
(cache of ISP PoPs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(PoP is a point where two or more large networks combine to enable communication between their) Tj
T*
(clients) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
