T*
() Tj
T*
(We should keep in mind that the caching at the ISP or IXP is performed only for the popular) Tj
T*
(content or moderately popular content because of limited storage capacity. Since our per-shot) Tj
T*
(encoding scheme saves storage space, we’ll be able to serve out more content using the cache) Tj
T*
(infrastructure closer to end users.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Additionally, we can have two types of storage at the origin servers:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Flash servers: These servers hold popular and moderately popular content. They are optimized) Tj
T*
(for low-latency delivery.) Tj
T*
(2. Storage servers: This type holds a large portion of videos that are not popular. These) Tj
T*
(servers are optimized to hold large storage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
