<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Resources << /Font << /F1 3 0 R >> >> /Contents 446 0 R >>
endobj
448 0 obj
<< /Length 2797 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
12 TL
50 780 Td
() Tj
T*
(  - Key-value stores: We’ll need to fetch the places in a segment efficiently. For that, we) Tj
T*
(store the list of places against a segment ID in a key-value store to minimize searching time.) Tj
T*
(We also save the QuadTree information in the key-value store, by storing the QuadTree data) Tj
T*
(against a unique ID.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Load balancer: A load balancer distributes users’ incoming requests to all the servers) Tj
T*
(uniformly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Yelp design]\(./design.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Workflow) Tj
T*
(The user puts in a search request. We find all the relevant places in the given radius, while) Tj
T*
(considering the user’s location \(latitude, longitude\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We explain the detailed workflow of our system in terms of the required functionalities below:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Searching a place: The load balancers route read requests to the read servers upon receiving) Tj
T*
(them. The read servers direct them to the QuadTree servers to find all the places that fall) Tj
T*
(within the given radius. The QuadTree servers then send the results to the aggregators to) Tj
T*
(refine them and send them to the user.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Adding a place or feedback: The load balancers route the write requests to the write servers) Tj
T*
(upon receiving them. Depending on the provided content, meaning the place information or) Tj
T*
(review, the write servers add an entry in the relational database and put all the related) Tj
T*
(images in the blob storage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Making segments: The segment’s producer splits the world map taken from the third-party map) Tj
T*
(service into smaller segments. The places inside each segment are stored in a key-value store.) Tj
T*
(Even though this is a one-time job, this process is repeated periodically for newer segments) Tj
T*
(and places. Since the probability of new places being added is low, we update our segments) Tj
T*
(every month.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We’ve discussed the design of Yelp, its API design, and the relevant storage schema. In the) Tj
T*
(next lesson, we’ll talk about the design considerations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
