BT
/F1 10 Tf
12 TL
50 780 Td
(cache solution. We require a simple, horizontally scalable cache system with minimal data) Tj
T*
(structure requirements. Moreover, we’ll have a data-center-specific caching layer to handle) Tj
T*
(native requests. Having a global caching layer will result in higher latency.) Tj
T*
(- Rate limiter: Limiting each user’s quota is preferable for adding a security layer to our) Tj
T*
(system. We can achieve this by uniquely identifying users through their unique api_dev_key and) Tj
T*
(applying one of the discussed rate-limiting algorithms \(see Rate Limiter from Building Blocks\).) Tj
T*
(Keeping in view the simplicity of our system and the requirements, the fixed window counter) Tj
T*
(algorithm would serve the purpose, as we can assign a set number of shortening and redirection) Tj
T*
(operations per api_dev_key for a specific timeframe.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question 1) Tj
T*
(How will we maintain a unique mapping if redirection requests can go to different data centers) Tj
T*
(that are geographically apart? Does our design assume that our DB is consistent geographically?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(We initially assumed that our data center was globally consistent. Let’s look at the problem) Tj
T*
(differently and consider the opposite case: we need to filter the redirection requests based on) Tj
T*
(data centers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Solution: An simple way of achieving this functionality is to introduce a unique character in) Tj
T*
(the short URL. This special character will act as an indicator for the exact data center.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Example: Let’s assume that the short URL that needs redirection is service.com/x/short123/,) Tj
T*
(where x indicates the data center containing this record.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In this solution, if the short URL goes to the wrong data center, it can be redirected to the) Tj
T*
(correct one. However, if a specific data center is not reachable for a specific short URL \(and) Tj
T*
(that URL is not yet cached\), the redirection will fail.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question 2) Tj
T*
(How will the data-center-specific caching handle an unseen redirection request?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(Since we’ve assumed the data-center-specific caching solution for our system, a case needs) Tj
T*
(highlighting: handling unseen redirection requests by our system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Scenario: The scenario entails receiving an unknown redirection request at a data center. Since) Tj
T*
(the local cache wouldn’t have that entry, it would fetch that record from the globally) Tj
T*
(consistent database and place this entry into the local cache for future use.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question 3) Tj
T*
(What is the probability of collision when we ask the short URL generator for a new short URL?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
