(## The scope of the short URL generator) Tj
T*
(The short URL generator is the backbone of our URL shortening service. The output of this short) Tj
T*
(URL generator depends on the design-imposed limitations, as given below:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- The generated short URL should contain alphanumeric characters.) Tj
T*
(- None of the characters should look alike.) Tj
T*
(- The minimum default length of the generated short URL should be six characters.) Tj
T*
(These limitations define the scope of our short URL generator. We can define the scope, as) Tj
T*
(shown below:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Starting range: Our sequencer can generate a 64-bit binary number that ranges from 1 to) Tj
T*
(\(2^{64}-1\). To meet the requirement for the minimum length of a short URL, we can select the) Tj
T*
(sequencer IDs to start from at least 10 digits, i.e., 1 Billion.) Tj
T*
(- Ending point: The maximum number of digits in sequencer IDs that map into the short URL) Tj
T*
(generator's output depends on the maximum utilization of 64 bits, that is, the largest base-10) Tj
T*
(number in 64-bits. We can estimate the total number of digits in any base by calculating these) Tj
T*
(two points:) Tj
T*
(1. The numbers of bits to represent one digit in a base-n. This is given by log_2{n}) Tj
T*
(2. Number of digits = Total bits available/Number of bits to represent one digit) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Let's see the calculations above for both the base-10 and base-58 mathematically:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  - Base-10:) Tj
T*
(    - The number of bits needed to represent one decimal digit = log_2{10} = 3.13) Tj
T*
(  - The total number of decimal digits in 64-bit numeric ID = 64 / 3.13= 20) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Base-58:) Tj
T*
(The number of bits needed to represent one decimal digit = log_2{58}=5.85) Tj
T*
(The total number of base-58 digits in a 64-bit numeric ID =64 / 5.85=11) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Maximum digits: The calculations above show that the maximum digits in the sequencer generated) Tj
T*
(ID will be 20 and consequently, the maximum number of characters in the encoded short URL will) Tj
T*
(be 11.  ) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
