(## Requirements for URL Shortening Design) Tj
T*
(Let’s look at the functional and non-functional requirements for the service we’ll be) Tj
T*
(designing:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Functional requirements) Tj
T*
(- Short URL generation: Our service should be able to generate a unique shorter alias of the) Tj
T*
(given URL.) Tj
T*
(- Redirection: Given a short link, our system should be able to redirect the user to the) Tj
T*
(original URL.) Tj
T*
(- Custom short links: Users should be able to generate custom short links for their URLs using) Tj
T*
(our system.) Tj
T*
(- Deletion: Users should be able to delete a short link generated by our system, given the) Tj
T*
(rights.) Tj
T*
(- Update: Users should be able to update the long URL associated with the short link, given the) Tj
T*
(proper rights.) Tj
T*
(- Expiry time: There must be a default expiration time for the short links, but users should be) Tj
T*
(able to set the expiration time based on their requirements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question) Tj
T*
(As a design choice, we don’t reuse the expired short URLs. Since we don’t reuse them, why do we) Tj
T*
(need to delete them from our system?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(So far, we’ve kept the default expiration time to five years. If we relax that limitation and) Tj
T*
(start saving the records forever, our datastore’s search index will grow without bound, and) Tj
T*
(querying time from it can add noticeable latency.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Non-functional requirements) Tj
T*
(- Availability: Our system should be highly available, because even a fraction of the second) Tj
T*
(downtime would result in URL redirection failures. Since our system’s domain is in URLs, we) Tj
T*
(don’t have the leverage of downtime, and our design must have fault-tolerance conditions) Tj
T*
(instilled in it.) Tj
T*
(- Scalability: Our system should be horizontally scalable with increasing demand.) Tj
T*
(- Readability: The short links generated by our system should be easily readable,) Tj
T*
(distinguishable, and typeable.) Tj
T*
(- Latency: The system should perform at low latency to provide the user with a smooth) Tj
T*
(experience.) Tj
T*
(- Unpredictability: From a security standpoint, the short links generated by our system should) Tj
T*
(be highly unpredictable. This ensures that the next-in-line short URL is not serially produced,) Tj
T*
(eliminating the possibility of someone guessing all the short URLs that our system has ever) Tj
T*
(produced or will produce.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question) Tj
T*
(Why is producing unpredictable short URLs mandatory for our system?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Hide Answer) Tj
T*
(The following two problems highlight the necessity of producing non-serial, unpredictable short) Tj
T*
(URLs:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Attackers can have access to the system-level information of the short URLs’ total count,) Tj
T*
(giving them a defined range to plan out their attacks. This type of internal information) Tj
T*
