(## Design a URL Shortening Service TinyURL/System Design TinyURL/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# System Design: TinyURL) Tj
T*
(## Introduction) Tj
T*
(URL shortening is a service that produces short aliases for long URLs, commonly referred to as) Tj
T*
(short links. Upon clicking, these short links direct to the original URLs. The following) Tj
T*
(illustration depicts how the process works:) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Uniform Resource Locator \(URL\), is an address that uniquely identifies a resource on the web.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
([How URL shortening service works]\(./url.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Advantages) Tj
T*
(The key advantages of a URL shortening service are:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Shortened URLs are convenient to use: they optimize link usage across different forms of) Tj
T*
(devices due to their enhanced accessibility and non-breakability.) Tj
T*
(- They are visually professional, engaging and facilitate a higher degree of sharing) Tj
T*
(possibilities.) Tj
T*
(- They are less error-prone while typing.) Tj
T*
(- They require smaller storage space at the user’s end.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
