(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Distributed Cache/Evaluation of a Distributed Cache's Design/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Evaluation of a Distributed Cache's Design) Tj
T*
(## High performance) Tj
T*
(Here are some design choices we made that will contribute to overall good performance:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- We used consistent hashing. Finding a key under this algorithm requires a time complexity of) Tj
T*
(O\(log\(N\)\), where N represents the number of cache shards.) Tj
T*
(- Inside a cache server, keys are located using hash tables that require constant time on) Tj
T*
(average.) Tj
T*
(- The LRU eviction approach uses a constant time to access and update cache entries in a doubly) Tj
T*
(linked list.) Tj
T*
(- The communication between cache clients and servers is done through TCP and UDP protocols,) Tj
T*
(which is also very fast.) Tj
T*
(- Since we added more replicas, these can reduce the performance penalties that we have to face) Tj
T*
(if there’s a high request load on a single machine.) Tj
T*
(- An important feature of the design is adding, retrieving, and serving data from the RAM.) Tj
T*
(Therefore, the latency to perform these operations is quite low.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: A critical parameter for high performance is the selection of the eviction algorithm) Tj
T*
(because the number of cache hits and misses depends on it. The higher the cache hit rate, the) Tj
T*
(better the performance.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(To get an idea of how important the eviction algorithm is, let’s assume the following:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Cache hit service time \(99.9th percentile\): 5 ms) Tj
T*
(- Cach miss service time \(99.9th percentile\): 30 ms \(this includes time to get the data from) Tj
T*
(the database and set the cache\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Let’s assume we have a 10% cache miss rate using the most frequently used \(MFU\) algorithm,) Tj
T*
(whereas we have a 5% cache miss rate using the LRU algorithm. Then, we use the following) Tj
T*
(formula:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(EAT = Ratio_{hit} x Time_{hit} + Ratio_{miss} x Time_{miss}) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Here, this means the following:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(EAT: Effective access time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Ratio_{hit}: The percentage of times a cache hit will occur.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Ratio_{miss}: The percentage of times a cache miss will occur.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Time_{hit}: Time required to serve a cache hit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Time_{miss}: Time required to serve a cache miss.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For MFU, we see the following:) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(EAT = 0.90 x 5 milliseconds + 0.10 x 30 milliseconds = 0.0045 + 0.003 = 0.0075 = 7.5) Tj
T*
(milliseconds) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(For LRU, we see the following:) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(EAT = 0.95 x 5 milliseconds + 0.05 x 30 milliseconds =  0.00475 + 0.0015 = 0.00625 = 6.25) Tj
T*
(milliseconds.) Tj
T*
ET
