(### Functional) Tj
T*
(The following are the functional requirements:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Insert data: The user of a distributed cache system must be able to insert an entry to the) Tj
T*
(cache.) Tj
T*
(- Retrieve data: The user should be able to retrieve data corresponding to a specific key.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Functional and non-functional requirements of a distributed cache]\(./req.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Non-functional requirements) Tj
T*
(We’ll consider the following non-functional requirements:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- High performance: The primary reason for the cache is to enable fast retrieval of data.) Tj
T*
(Therefore, both the insert and retrieve operations must be fast.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Scalability: The cache system should scale horizontally with no bottlenecks on an increasing) Tj
T*
(number of requests.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- High availability: The unavailability of the cache will put an extra burden on the database) Tj
T*
(servers, which can also go down at peak load intervals. We also require our system to survive) Tj
T*
(occasional failures of components and network, as well as power outages.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Consistency: Data stored on the cache servers should be consistent. For example, different) Tj
T*
(cache clients retrieving the same data from different cache servers \(primary or secondary\)) Tj
T*
(should be up to date.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Affordability: Ideally, the caching system should be designed from commodity hardware instead) Tj
T*
(of an expensive supporting component within the design of a system.) Tj
T*
(## API design) Tj
T*
(The API design for this problem is sufficiently easy since there are only two basic operations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Insertion) Tj
T*
(The API call to perform insertion should look like this:) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(insert\(key, value\)) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Parameter      Description) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(key            This is a unique identifier.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(value          This is the data stored against a unique key.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(This function returns an acknowledgment or an error depicting the problem at the server end.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Retrieval) Tj
T*
(The API call to retrieve data from the cache should look like this:) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(retrieve\(key\)) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Parameter    Description) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(key          This returns the data stored against the key.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(This call returns an object to the caller.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
