(## Initial design) Tj
T*
(In a distributed system, clients across the globe generate events by requesting services from) Tj
T*
(different serving nodes. The nodes generate logs while handling each of the requests. These) Tj
T*
(logs are accumulated on the respective nodes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In addition to the building blocks, let’s list the major components of our system:) Tj
T*
(- Log accumulator: An agent that collects logs from each node and dumps them into storage. So,) Tj
T*
(if we want to know about a particular event, we don’t need to visit each node, and we can fetch) Tj
T*
(them from our storage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Storage: The logs need to be stored somewhere after accumulation. We’ll choose blob storage) Tj
T*
(to save our logs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Log indexer: The growing number of log files affects the searching ability. The log indexer) Tj
T*
(will use the distributed search to search efficiently.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Visualizer: The visualizer is used to provide a unified view of all the logs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
