(cause of the failure or breach. It decreases the meantime to repair a system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why don’t we simply print out our statements to understand the application flow? It’s possible) Tj
T*
(but not ideal. Simple print statements have no way of tracking the severity of the message. The) Tj
T*
(output of print functions usually goes to the terminal, while our need could be to persist such) Tj
T*
(data on a local or remote store. Moreover, we can have millions of print statements, so it’s) Tj
T*
(better to structure and store them properly.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Mean time to repair \(MTTR\) is a basic measure of the maintainability of repairable items. It) Tj
T*
(represents the average time required to repair a failed component or device. \(Source:) Tj
T*
(Wikipedia\)) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
