() Tj
T*
(Concurrent activity by a service running on many nodes might need causality information to) Tj
T*
(stitch together a correct flow of events properly. We must be careful while dealing with) Tj
T*
(causality in a distributed system. We use a logging service to appropriately manage the) Tj
T*
(diagnostic and exploratory data of our distributed software.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Logging allows us to understand our code, locate unforeseen errors, fix the identified errors,) Tj
T*
(and visualize the application’s performance. This way, we are aware of how production works,) Tj
T*
(and we know how processes are running in the system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Log analysis helps us with the following scenarios:) Tj
T*
(- To troubleshoot applications, nodes, or network issues.) Tj
T*
(- To adhere to internal security policies, external regulations, and compliance.) Tj
T*
(- To recognize and respond to data breaches and other security problems.) Tj
T*
(- To comprehend users’ actions for input to a recommender system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## How will we design a distributed logging system?) Tj
T*
(1. Introduction: We’ll discuss how logging works at a distributed level. We’ll also show how we) Tj
T*
(can restrict the huge size of a log file, and structure them. This lesson will guide us about) Tj
T*
(the requirements we should consider while logging information about a system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Design: In this lesson, we’ll define the requirements, API design, and detailed design of) Tj
T*
(our distributed logging system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Distributed Messaging Queue/Considerations of a Distributed Messaging Queue’s) Tj
T*
(Design/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Considerations of a Distributed Messaging Queue’s Design) Tj
T*
(Before embarking on our journey to design a distributed messaging queue, let’s discuss some) Tj
T*
(major factors that could significantly affect the design. These include the order of messages,) Tj
T*
(the effect of the ordering on performance, and the management of concurrent access to the) Tj
T*
(queue. We discuss each of these factors in detail below.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Ordering of messages) Tj
T*
(A messaging queue is used to receive messages from producers. These messages are consumed by) Tj
T*
(the consumers at their own pace. Some operations are critical in that they require strict) Tj
T*
(ordering of the execution of the tasks, driven by the messages in the queue. For example, while) Tj
T*
(chatting over a messenger application with a friend, the messages should be delivered in order;) Tj
T*
(otherwise, such communication can be confusing, to say the least. Similarly, emails received by) Tj
T*
(a user from different users may not require strict ordering. Therefore, in some cases, the) Tj
T*
(strict order of incoming messages in the queue is essential, while many use cases can tolerate) Tj
T*
(some reordering.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Let’s discuss the following two categories of messages ordering in a queue:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
