T*
(## Effect on performance) Tj
T*
(Primarily, a queue is designed for first-in, first-out \(FIFO\) operations;. First-in, first-out) Tj
T*
(operations suggest that the first message that enters a queue is always handed out first.) Tj
T*
(However, it isn’t easy to maintain this strict order in distributed systems. Since message A) Tj
T*
(was produced before message B, it’s still uncertain that message A will be consumed before) Tj
T*
(message B. Using monotonically increasing message identifiers or causality-bearing identifiers) Tj
T*
(provide high throughput while putting messages in a queue. Though the need for the online) Tj
T*
(sorting to provide a strict order takes some time before messages are ready for extraction. To) Tj
T*
(minimize latency caused by the online sorting, we use a time-window approach.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
