(### Managing concurrency) Tj
T*
(Concurrent queue access needs proper management. Concurrency can take place at the following) Tj
T*
(stages:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- When multiple messages arrive at the same time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- When multiple consumers request concurrently for a message.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The first solution is to use the locking mechanism. When a process or thread requests a) Tj
T*
(message, it should acquire a lock for placing or consuming messages from the queue. However, as) Tj
T*
(was discussed earlier, this approach has several drawbacks. It’s neither scalable nor) Tj
T*
(performant.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Another solution is to serialize the requests using the system’s buffer at both ends of the) Tj
T*
(queue so that incoming messages are placed in an order and consumer processes also receive) Tj
T*
(messages in their arrival sequence. This is a more viable solution because it can help us avoid) Tj
T*
(the occurrence of race conditions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Applications might use multiple queues with dedicated producers and consumers to keep the) Tj
T*
(ordering cost per queue under check, although this comes at the cost of more complicated) Tj
T*
(application logic.) Tj
T*
() Tj
