([High-level architecture of distributed messaging queue]\(./design.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The essential components of our design are described in detail below.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(#### Load balancer) Tj
T*
(The load balancer layer receives requests from producers and consumers, which are forwarded to) Tj
T*
(one of the front-end servers. This layer consists of numerous load balancers. Therefore,) Tj
T*
(requests are accepted with minimal latency and offer high availability.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(#### Front-end service) Tj
T*
(The front-end service comprises stateless machines distributed across data centers. The) Tj
T*
(frontend provides the following services:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Request validation: This ensures the validity of a request and checks if it contains all the) Tj
T*
(necessary information.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Authentication and authorization: This service checks if the requester is a valid user and if) Tj
T*
(these services are authorized for use to a requester.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Caching: In the front-end cache, metadata information is stored related to the frequently) Tj
T*
(used queues. Along with this, user-related data is also cached here to reduce request time to) Tj
T*
(authentication and authorization services.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Request dispatching: The frondend is also responsible for calling two other services, the) Tj
T*
(backend and the metadata store. Differentiating calls to both of these services is one of the) Tj
T*
(responsibilities of the frontend.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Request deduplication: The frontend also tracks information related to all the requests,) Tj
T*
(therefore, it also prevents identical requests from being put in a queue. Deciding what to do) Tj
T*
(about duplicates might be as easy as searching a hash key in a store. If something is found in) Tj
T*
(the store, this implies a duplicate and the message can be rejected.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(A question might arise here: how to identify that two \(or more\) requests are duplicates. There) Tj
T*
(are several ways to identify duplicate messages; however, the most reliable one is to compute) Tj
T*
(the hash \(preferably SHA256\) of the message content \(not the message attributes\). This way, if) Tj
T*
(incoming messages have the same content, the service will detect duplication based on their) Tj
T*
(hash.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
