T*
(in the lesson on database partitioning. Each shard is stored on a different host in the) Tj
T*
(cluster. Moreover, each shard is also replicated on different hosts to enhance availability. In) Tj
T*
(this cluster-organization approach, the front-end server has a mapping table between shards and) Tj
T*
(the hosts. Therefore, the front-end server is responsible for redirecting requests to the host) Tj
T*
(where the data is stored.) Tj
