() Tj
T*
(The same process is applied to receive message requests from the consumer. Similar to the first) Tj
T*
(approach, the randomly selected host is responsible for message delivery and cleanup upon a) Tj
T*
(successful processing of the message.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Furthermore, another component called an external cluster manager is introduced, which is) Tj
T*
(accountable for maintaining the mapping between queues and clusters, as shown in the following) Tj
T*
(figure. The external cluster manager is also responsible for queue management and cluster) Tj
T*
(assignment to a particular queue.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The following figure illustrates the cluster of independent hosts. There are two clusters, A) Tj
T*
(and B, which consist of several nodes. The external cluster manager has the mapping table) Tj
T*
(between queues and their corresponding cluster. Whenever a frontend receives a request for a) Tj
T*
(queue, it determines the corresponding cluster for the queue and forwards the request to the) Tj
T*
(cluster where the queue resides. The nodes within that cluster are responsible for storing and) Tj
T*
(sending messages accordingly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([A cluster of independent hosts that consist of distributed queues]\(./cluster.jpg\)) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question) Tj
T*
(What kind of anomalies can arise while replicating messages on other hosts?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(There are two ways to replicate messages in a queue residing on multiple hosts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Synchrounous replication) Tj
T*
(2. Asynchrounous replication) Tj
T*
(In synchronous replication, the primary host is responsible for replicating the message in all) Tj
T*
(the relevant queues on other hosts. After acknowledgment from secondary hosts, the primary host) Tj
T*
(then notifies the client regarding the reception of messages. In this approach, messages remain) Tj
T*
(consistent in all queues replicas; however, it costs extra delay in communication and causes) Tj
T*
(partial to no availability while an election is in progress to promote a secondary as a) Tj
T*
(primary.) Tj
T*
ET
