(## Distributed Messaging Queue/Requirements of a Distributed Messaging Queue’s Design/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Requirements of a Distributed Messaging Queue’s Design) Tj
T*
(## Requirements) Tj
T*
(In a distributed messaging queue, data resides on several machines. Our aim is to design a) Tj
T*
(distributed messaging queue that has the following functional and non-functional requirements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Functional requirements) Tj
T*
(- Listed below are the actions that a client should be able to perform:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Queue creation: The client should be able to create a queue and set some parameters—for) Tj
T*
(example, queue name, queue size, and maximum message size.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Send message: Producer entities should be able to send messages to a queue that’s intended) Tj
T*
(for them.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Receive message: Consumer entities should be able to receive messages from their respective) Tj
T*
(queues.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Delete message: The consumer processes should be able to delete a message from the queue) Tj
T*
(after a successful processing of the message.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Queue deletion: Clients should be able to delete a specific queue.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
