(A messaging queue has many use cases, both in single-server and distributed environments. For) Tj
T*
(example, it can be used for interprocess communication within one operating system. It also) Tj
T*
(enables communication between processes in a distributed environment. Some of the use cases of) Tj
T*
(a messaging queue are discussed below.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Sending many emails: Emails are used for numerous purposes, such as sharing information,) Tj
T*
(account verification, resetting passwords, marketing campaigns, and more. All of these emails) Tj
T*
(written for different purposes don’t need immediate processing and, therefore, they don’t) Tj
T*
(disturb the system’s core functionality. A messaging queue can help coordinate a large number) Tj
T*
(of emails between different senders and receivers in such cases.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
