T*
(sending and receiving emails.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Data post-processing: Many multimedia applications need to process content for different) Tj
T*
(viewer needs, such as for consumption on a mobile phone and a smart television. Oftentimes,) Tj
T*
(applications upload the content into a store and use a messaging queue for post-processing of) Tj
T*
(content offline. Doing this substantially reduces client-perceived latency and enables the) Tj
T*
(service to schedule the offline work at some appropriate time—probably late at night when the) Tj
T*
(compute capacity is less busy.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Recommender systems: Some platforms use recommender systems to provide preferred content or) Tj
T*
(information to a user. The recommender system takes the user’s historical data, processes it,) Tj
T*
(and predicts relevant content or information. Since this is a time-consuming task, a messaging) Tj
T*
(queue can be incorporated between the recommender system and requesting processes to increase) Tj
T*
(and quicken performance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
