T*
(monitoring?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(In logging, the application servers log the information into the file. The information can be) Tj
T*
(CPU usage, application-related information, and other relevant properties that we deem) Tj
T*
(necessary to backtrace or debug a file when a problem is encountered. We can populate our) Tj
T*
(metrics based on the values logged in the logs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Logs and metrics both help in monitoring a service. But this isn’t always true since processing) Tj
T*
(the log information takes time. In real time, we need to act swiftly for early detection of) Tj
T*
(issues. So, logging is also one of the inputs of metrics. Logging is just a mechanism to) Tj
T*
