(### Persist the data) Tj
T*
(Figuring out how to store the metrics from the servers that are being monitored is important. A) Tj
T*
(centralized in-memory metrics repository may be all that’s needed. However, for a large data) Tj
T*
(center with millions of things to monitor, there will be an enormous amount of data to store,) Tj
T*
(and a time-series database can help in this regard.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Time-series databases help maintain durability, which is an important factor. Without a) Tj
T*
(historical view of events in a monitoring system, it isn’t very useful. Samples having a value) Tj
T*
(of time stamp are stored in chronological sequence. So, a whole metric’s timeline can be shown) Tj
T*
(in the form of a time series.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Time series data is continuous, and a time-series database \(TSDB\) allows storing data) Tj
T*
(associated with timestamps. Using TSDB is an efficient method of storing and retrieving massive) Tj
T*
(amounts of timestamped data.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Application metrics) Tj
T*
(We may need to add code or APIs to expose metrics we care about for other components, notably) Tj
T*
(our own applications. We embed logging or monitoring code in our applications, called code) Tj
T*
(instrumentation, to collect information of interest.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Looking at metrics as a whole can shed light on how our systems are performing and how healthy) Tj
T*
(they are. Monitoring systems employ these inputs to generate a comprehensive view of our) Tj
T*
(environment, automate responses to changes like commissioning more EC2 instances if the) Tj
T*
(applications’ traffic increases, and warn humans when necessary. Metrics are system) Tj
T*
(measurements that allow analyzing historical trends, correlations, and changes in the) Tj
T*
(performance, consumption, or error rates.) Tj
T*
(## Alerting) Tj
T*
(Alerting is the part of a monitoring system that responds to changes in metric values and takes) Tj
T*
(action. There are two components to an alert definition: a metrics-based condition or) Tj
T*
(threshold, and an action to take when the values fall outside of the permitted range.) Tj
T*
() Tj
