T*
(## Monitoring) Tj
T*
(The modern economy depends on the continual operation of IT infrastructure. Such infrastructure) Tj
T*
(contains hardware, distributed services, and network resources. These components are) Tj
T*
(interlinked in such infrastructure, making it challenging to keep everything functioning) Tj
T*
(smoothly and without application downtime.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(It’s challenging to know what’s happening at the hardware or application level when our) Tj
T*
(infrastructure is distributed across multiple locations and includes many servers. Components) Tj
T*
(can run into failures, response latency overshoot, overloaded or unreachable hardware, and) Tj
T*
(containers running out of resources, among others. Multiple services are running in such an) Tj
T*
(infrastructure, and anything can go awry.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(When one of the services goes down, it can be the reason for other services to crash, and as a) Tj
T*
(result, the application is unavailable to users. If we don’t know what went wrong early, it) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
