T*
(## Availability) Tj
T*
(We utilized distributed storage to store these items:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Documents crawled by the indexer.) Tj
T*
(- Inverted indexes generated by the indexing nodes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Data is replicated across multiple regions in distributed storage, making cross-region) Tj
T*
(deployment for indexing and search easier. The group of indexing and search nodes merely needs) Tj
T*
(to be replicated in different availability zones. Therefore, we deploy the cluster of indexing) Tj
T*
(and search nodes in different availability zones. So, if a failure occurs in one place, we can) Tj
T*
(process the requests from another cluster. Multiple groups of indexing and search nodes help to) Tj
T*
(achieve high indexing and search availability. Moreover, in each cluster, if a node dies,) Tj
T*
(another can take its place.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The indexing is performed offline, not on the user’s critical path. We don’t need to replicate) Tj
T*
(the indexing operations synchronously. It is unnecessary to respond to the user search queries) Tj
T*
(with the latest data that has just been added to the index. So, we don’t have to wait for the) Tj
T*
(replication of the new index to respond to the search queries. This makes the search available) Tj
T*
(to the users.) Tj
