(## Indexing on a centralized system) Tj
T*
(In a centralized search system, all the search system components run on a single node, which is) Tj
T*
(computationally quite capable. The architecture of a centralized search system is shown in the) Tj
T*
(following illustration:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The architecture of a centralized search system]\(./arch.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- The indexing process takes the documents as input and converts them into an inverted index,) Tj
T*
(which is stored in the form of a binary file.) Tj
T*
(- The query processing or search process interprets the binary file that contains the inverted) Tj
T*
(index. It also computes the intersection of the inverted lists for a given query to return the) Tj
T*
(search results against the query.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(These are the problems that come with the architecture of a centralized search system:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- SPOF \(single point of failure\)) Tj
T*
(- Server overload) Tj
T*
(- Large size of the index) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SPOF: A centralized system is a single point of failure. If it’s dead, no search operation can) Tj
T*
(be performed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Server overload: If numerous users perform queries and the queries are complicated, it stresses) Tj
T*
(the server \(node\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Large size of the index: The size of the inverted index increases with the number of documents,) Tj
T*
(placing resource demands on a single server. The bigger the computer system, the higher the) Tj
T*
(cost and complexity of managing it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: With a distributed system, low-cost computer systems are utilized, which is cost) Tj
T*
(effective overall.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(An inverted index needs to be loaded into the main memory when adding a document or running a) Tj
T*
(search query. A large portion of the inverted index must fit into the RAM of the machine for) Tj
T*
(efficiency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(According to Google analytics in 2022, there are hundreds of billions of web pages, the total) Tj
T*
(size of which is around 100 petabytes. If we make a search system for the worldwide web, the) Tj
T*
(inverted index size will also be in petabytes. This means we have to load petabytes of data) Tj
T*
(into the RAM. It’s impractical and inefficient to increase the resources of a single machine) Tj
T*
(for indexing a billion pages instead of shifting to a distributed system and utilizing the) Tj
T*
ET
