(## Requirements) Tj
T*
(Let’s understand the functional and non-functional requirements of a distributed search system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Functional requirements) Tj
T*
(The following is a functional requirement of a distributed search system:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Search: Users should get relevant content based on their search queries.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The functional requirement of a distributed search system]\(./fr.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Non-functional requirements) Tj
T*
(Here are the non-functional requirements of a distributed search system:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Availability: The system should be highly available to the users.) Tj
T*
(- Scalability: The system should have the ability to scale with the increasing amount of data.) Tj
T*
(In other words, it should be able to index a large amount of data.) Tj
T*
(- Fast search on big data: The user should get the results quickly, no matter how much content) Tj
T*
(they are searching.) Tj
T*
(- Reduced cost: The overall cost of building a search system should be less.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The non-functional requirement of a distributed search system]\(./nfr.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Resource estimation) Tj
T*
(Let’s estimate the total number of servers, storage, and bandwidth that is required by the) Tj
T*
(distributed search system. We’ll calculate these numbers using an example of a YouTube search.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Number of servers estimation) Tj
T*
(To estimate the number of servers, we need to know how many daily active users per day are) Tj
T*
(using the search feature on YouTube and how many requests per second our single server can) Tj
T*
(handle. We assume the following numbers:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- The number of daily active users who use the search feature is three million.) Tj
T*
(- The number of requests a single server can handle is 1,000.) Tj
T*
(The number of servers required is calculated using this formula:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Number of active users/queries handled per server =3K servers) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If three million users are searching concurrently, three million search requests are being) Tj
T*
(generated at one time. A single server handles 1,000 requests at a time. Dividing three million) Tj
T*
(by 1,000 gives us 3,000 servers.) Tj
T*
ET
