(## Distributed Search/Scaling Search and Indexing/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Scaling Search and Indexing) Tj
T*
(Although the proposed design in the previous lesson seems reasonable, still, there are a couple) Tj
T*
(of serious drawbacks. We’ll discuss these drawbacks below:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Colocated indexing and searching: We’ve created a system that colocates indexing and) Tj
T*
(searching on the same node. Although it seems like efficient usage of resources, it has its) Tj
T*
(downsides as well. Searching and indexing are both resource-intensive operations. Both) Tj
T*
(operations impact the performance of each other. Also, this colocated design doesn’t scale) Tj
T*
(efficiently with varying indexing and search operations over time. Colocating both these) Tj
T*
ET
