(- Batching and prioritization: After we store the tasks in the RDB, the tasks are grouped into) Tj
T*
(batches. Prioritization is based on the attributes of the tasks, such as delay tolerance or the) Tj
T*
(tasks with short execution cap, and so on. The top K priority tasks are pushed into the) Tj
T*
(distributed queue, where K limits the number of elements we can push into the queue. The value) Tj
T*
(of K depends on many factors, such as currently available resources, the client or task) Tj
T*
(priority, and subscription level.) Tj
T*
(- Distributed queue: It consists of a queue and a queue manager. The queue manager adds,) Tj
T*
(updates, or deletes tasks in the queue. It keeps track of the types of queues we use. It is) Tj
T*
(also responsible for keeping the task in the queue until it executes successfully. In case a) Tj
T*
(task execution fails, that task is made visible in the queue again. The queue manager knows) Tj
T*
(which queue to run during the peak time and which queue to run during the off-peak time.) Tj
T*
(- Queue manager: The queue manager deletes a task from the queue if it executes successfully.) Tj
T*
(It also makes the task visible if its previous execution failed. It retries for the allowed) Tj
T*
(number of attempts for a task in case of a failed execution.) Tj
T*
(- Resource manager: The resource manager knows which of the resources are free. It pulls the) Tj
T*
(tasks from the distributed queue and assigns them resources. The resource manager keeps track) Tj
T*
(of the execution of each task and sends back their statuses to the queue manager. If a task) Tj
T*
(goes beyond its promised or required resource use, that task will be terminated, and the status) Tj
T*
(is sent back to the task submitter, which will notify the client about the termination of the) Tj
T*
(task through an error message.) Tj
T*
(- Monitoring service: It is responsible for checking the health of the resource manager and the) Tj
T*
(resources. If some resource fails, it alerts the administrators to repair the resource or add) Tj
T*
(new resources if required. If resources are not being used, it alerts the administrators to) Tj
T*
(remove them or power them off.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
