(```) Tj
T*
(DNS resolver: Resolvers initiate the querying sequence and forward requests to the other DNS) Tj
T*
(name servers. Typically, DNS resolvers lie within the premise of the user’s network. However,) Tj
T*
(DNS resolvers can also cater to users’ DNS queries through caching techniques, as we will see) Tj
T*
(shortly. These servers can also be called local or default servers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Root-level name servers: These servers receive requests from local servers. Root name servers) Tj
T*
(maintain name servers based on top-level domain names, such as .com, .edu, .us, and so on. For) Tj
T*
(instance, when a user requests the IP address of educative.io, root-level name servers will) Tj
T*
(return a list of top-level domain \(TLD\) servers that hold the IP addresses of the .io domain.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Top-level domain \(TLD\) name servers: These servers hold the IP addresses of authoritative name) Tj
T*
(servers. The querying party will get a list of IP addresses that belong to the authoritative) Tj
T*
(servers of the organization.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Authoritative name servers: These are the organization’s DNS name servers that provide the IP) Tj
T*
(addresses of the web or application servers.) Tj
