BT
/F1 10 Tf
12 TL
50 780 Td
(DNS uses various protocols to update and transfer information among replicated servers in a) Tj
T*
(hierarchy. DNS compromises on strong consistency to achieve high performance because data is) Tj
T*
(read frequently from DNS databases as compared to writing. However, DNS provides eventual) Tj
T*
(consistency and updates records on replicated servers lazily. Typically, it can take from a few) Tj
T*
(seconds up to three days to update records on the DNS servers across the Internet. The time it) Tj
T*
(takes to propagate information among different DNS clusters depends on the DNS infrastructure,) Tj
T*
(the size of the update, and which part of the DNS tree is being updated.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Consistency can suffer because of caching too. Since authoritative servers are located within) Tj
T*
(the organization, it may be possible that certain resource records are updated on the) Tj
T*
(authoritative servers in case of server failures at the organization. Therefore, cached records) Tj
T*
(at the default/local and ISP servers may be outdated. To mitigate this issue, each cached) Tj
T*
(record comes with an expiration time called time-to-live \(TTL\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(TTL refers to the amount of time a record can be cached by the querying party. TTL values are) Tj
T*
(reported in the units of seconds.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question) Tj
T*
(To maintain high availability, should the TTL value be large or small?) Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(To maintain high availability, the TTL value should be small. This is because if any server or) Tj
T*
(cluster fails, the organization can update the resource records right away. Users will) Tj
T*
(experience non-availability only for the time the TTL isn’t expired. However, if the TTL is) Tj
T*
(large, the organization will update its resource records, whereas users will keep pinging the) Tj
T*
(outdated server that would have crashed long ago. Companies that long for high availability) Tj
T*
(maintain a TTL value as low as 120 seconds. Therefore, even in case of a failure, the maximum) Tj
T*
(downtime is a few minutes.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
