(Question) Tj
T*
(If we need DNS to tell us which IP to reach a website or service, how will we know the DNS) Tj
T*
(resolver’s IP address? \(It seems like a chicken-and-egg problem!\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(End users’ operating systems have configuration files \(/etc/resolv.conf in Linux\) with the DNS) Tj
T*
(resolvers’ IP addresses, which in turn obtain all information for them. \(Often, DHCP provides) Tj
T*
(the default DNS resolver IP address along with other configurations.\) The end-systems request) Tj
T*
(DNS resolves for any DNS queries. DNS resolvers have special software installed to resolve) Tj
T*
(queries through the DNS infrastructure. The root server’s IP addresses are within the special) Tj
T*
(software. Typically, the Berkeley Internet Name Domain \(BIND\) software is used on DNS) Tj
T*
(resolvers. The InterNIC maintains the updated list of 13 root servers.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
