(## Domain Name System/Introduction to Domain Name System \(DNS\)/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Introduction to Domain Name System \(DNS\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## The origins of DNS) Tj
T*
(Let’s consider the example of a mobile phone where a unique number is associated with each) Tj
T*
(user. To make calls to friends, we can initially try to memorize some of the phone numbers.) Tj
T*
(However, as the number of contacts grows, we’ll have to use a phone book to keep track of all) Tj
T*
(our contacts. This way, whenever we need to make a call, we’ll refer to the phone book and dial) Tj
T*
(the number we need.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Similarly, computers are uniquely identified by IP addresses—for example, 104.18.2.119 is an IP) Tj
T*
(address. We use IP addresses to visit a website hosted on a machine. Since humans cannot easily) Tj
T*
(remember IP addresses to visit domain names \(an example domain name being educative.io\), we) Tj
T*
(need a phone book-like repository that can maintain all mappings of domain names to IP) Tj
T*
(addresses. In this chapter, we’ll see how DNS serves as the Internet’s phone book.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The origins of DNS]\(./dns_brief.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## What is DNS?) Tj
T*
(The domain name system \(DNS\) is the Internet’s naming service that maps human-friendly domain) Tj
T*
(names to machine-readable IP addresses. The service of DNS is transparent to users. When a user) Tj
T*
(enters a domain name in the browser, the browser has to translate the domain name to IP address) Tj
T*
(by asking the DNS infrastructure. Once the desired IP address is obtained, the user’s request) Tj
T*
(is forwarded to the destination web server.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The slides below show the high-level flow of the working of DNS:) Tj
T*
([What is DNS]\(./dns_flow\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The entire operation is performed very quickly. Therefore, the end user experiences minimum) Tj
T*
(delay. We’ll also see how browsers save some of the frequently used mappings for later use in) Tj
T*
(the next lesson.) Tj
T*
(## Important details) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Let’s highlight some of the important details about DNS, some of which we’ll cover in the next) Tj
T*
(lesson:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(**Name servers**: It’s important to understand that the DNS isn’t a single server. It’s a) Tj
T*
(complete infrastructure with numerous servers. DNS servers that respond to users’ queries are) Tj
T*
