(## Add scalability) Tj
T*
(Let’s start with one of the core design requirements: scalability. We store key-value data in) Tj
T*
(storage nodes. With a change in demand, we might need to add or remove storage nodes. It means) Tj
T*
(we need to partition data over the nodes in the system to distribute the load across all nodes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For example, let’s consider that we have four nodes, and we want 25% of the requests to go to) Tj
T*
(each node to balance the load equally. The traditional way to solve this is through the modulus) Tj
T*
(operator. When a request comes in, we assign a request ID, calculate its hash, and find the) Tj
T*
(remainder by taking the modulus with the number of nodes available. The remainder value is the) Tj
T*
(node number, and we send the request to that node to process it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
