T*
() Tj
T*
(Let’s take an example. Suppose we have three hash functions. For each node, we calculate three) Tj
T*
(hashes and place them into the ring. For the request, we use only one hash function. Wherever) Tj
T*
(the request lands onto the ring, it’s processed by the next node found while moving in the) Tj
T*
(clockwise direction. Each server has three positions, so the load of requests is more uniform.) Tj
T*
(Moreover, if a node has more hardware capacity than others, we can add more virtual nodes by) Tj
T*
(using additional hash functions. This way, it’ll have more positions in the ring and serve more) Tj
T*
(requests.) Tj
