/F1 10 Tf
12 TL
50 780 Td
(Question 4) Tj
T*
(The image above shows a higher number of tier-3 load balancers than that of tier-2. What do you) Tj
T*
(think is the reason for such a representation?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(Tier 3 performs application-specific analysis and substantially more sophisticated) Tj
T*
(computations. Therefore, handling the same number of queries as tier 2 requires a higher number) Tj
T*
(of machines. Furthermore, tier-3 LBs maintain the state of a large number of application) Tj
T*
(servers, which may not be possible using the same number of LBs as tier 2.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Implementation of load balancers) Tj
T*
(Different kinds of load balancers can be implemented depending on the number of incoming) Tj
T*
(requests, organization, and application-specific requirements:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Hardware load balancers) Tj
T*
(Load balancers were introduced in the 1990s as hardware devices. Hardware load balancers work) Tj
T*
(as stand-alone devices and are quite expensive. Nonetheless, they have their performance) Tj
T*
(benefits and are able to handle a lot of concurrent users. Configuration of hardware-based) Tj
T*
(solutions is problematic because it requires additional human resources. Therefore, they aren’t) Tj
T*
(the go-to solutions even for large enterprises that can afford them. Availability can be an) Tj
T*
(issue with hardware load balancers because additional hardware will be required to failover to) Tj
T*
(in case of failures. Finally, hardware LBs can have higher maintenance/operational costs and) Tj
T*
(compatibility issues making them less flexible. Not to mention that hardware LBs have vendor) Tj
T*
(locks as well.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Software load balancers) Tj
T*
(Software load balancers are becoming increasingly popular because of their flexibility,) Tj
T*
(programmability, and cost-effectiveness. That’s all possible because they’re implemented on) Tj
T*
(commodity hardware. Software LBs scale well as requirements grow. Availability won’t be an) Tj
T*
(issue with software LBs because small additional costs are required to implement shadow load) Tj
T*
(balancers on commodity hardware. Additionally, software LBs can provide predictive analysis) Tj
T*
(that can help prepare for future traffic patterns.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Cloud load balancers) Tj
T*
(With the advent of the field of cloud computing, Load Balancers as a Service \(LBaaS\) has been) Tj
T*
(introduced. This is where cloud owners provide load balancing services. Users pay according to) Tj
T*
(their usage or the service-level agreement \(SLA\) with the cloud provider. Cloud-based LBs may) Tj
T*
(not necessarily replace a local on-premise load balancing facility, but they can perform global) Tj
T*
(traffic management between different zones. Primary advantages of such load balancers include) Tj
T*
(ease of use, management, metered cost, flexibility in terms of usage, auditing, and monitoring) Tj
T*
(services to improve business decisions. An example of how cloud-based LBs can provide GSLB is) Tj
T*
(given below:) Tj
T*
([GSLB is obtained through LBaaS, and the regions contain data centers that are the property of) Tj
T*
(application providers]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: Another interesting implementation of load balancers comes in the form of client-side) Tj
T*
(load balancing. Client-side load balancing is suited where there are numerous services, each) Tj
T*
(with many instances \(such as load balancing in Twitter\). Our focus, however, is on traditional) Tj
T*
(load balancers because most three-tier applications employ these in their design.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
([GSLB is obtained through LBaaS, and the regions contain data centers that are the property of) Tj
T*
(application providers]\(./gslb.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Conclusion) Tj
T*
(LBs have come a long way to become a service offered in the cloud, starting since their) Tj
T*
(inception in the form of hardware. They’re a key component of any enterprise-level service.) Tj
T*
(Horizontal scalability of hosting servers will always require a good load balancing layer) Tj
T*
(capable of providing load balancing, session maintenance, TLS offloading, service discovery,) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
