(# Introduction to Load Balancers) Tj
T*
(## What is load balancing?) Tj
T*
(Millions of requests could arrive per second in a typical data center. To serve these requests,) Tj
T*
(thousands \(or a hundred thousand\) servers work together to share the load of incoming requests.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: Here, it’s important that we consider how the incoming requests will be divided among all) Tj
T*
(the available servers.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(A load balancer \(LB\) is the answer to the question. The job of the load balancer is to fairly) Tj
T*
(divide all clients’ requests among the pool of available servers. Load balancers perform this) Tj
T*
(job to avoid overloading or crashing servers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The load balancing layer is the first point of contact within a data center after the firewall.) Tj
T*
(A load balancer may not be required if a service entertains a few hundred or even a few) Tj
T*
(thousand requests per second. However, for increasing client requests, load balancers provide) Tj
T*
(the following capabilities:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Scalability: By adding servers, the capacity of the application/service can be increased) Tj
T*
(seamlessly. Load balancers make such upscaling or downscaling transparent to the end users.) Tj
T*
(- Availability: Even if some servers go down or suffer a fault, the system still remains) Tj
T*
(available. One of the jobs of the load balancers is to hide faults and failures of servers.) Tj
T*
(- Performance: Load balancers can forward requests to servers with a lesser load so the user) Tj
T*
(can get a quicker response time. This not only improves performance but also improves resource) Tj
T*
(utilization.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Here’s an abstract depiction of how load balancers work:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Simplified working of a load balancer]\(./lbsymplified.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Placing load balancers) Tj
T*
(Generally, LBs sit between clients and servers. Requests go through to servers and back to) Tj
T*
(clients via the load balancing layer. However, that isn’t the only point where load balancers) Tj
T*
(are used.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Let’s consider the three well-known groups of servers. That is the web, the application, and) Tj
T*
(the database servers. To divide the traffic load among the available servers, load balancers) Tj
T*
(can be used between the server instances of these three services in the following way:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
