(## Services offered by load balancers) Tj
T*
(LBs not only enable services to be scalable, available, and highly performant, they offer some) Tj
T*
(key services like the following:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Health checking: LBs use the heartbeat protocol to monitor the health and, therefore,) Tj
T*
(reliability of end-servers. Another advantage of health checking is the improved user) Tj
T*
(experience.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- TLS termination: LBs reduce the burden on end-servers by handling TLS termination with the) Tj
T*
(client.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Predictive analytics: LBs can predict traffic patterns through analytics performed over) Tj
T*
(traffic passing through them or using statistics of traffic obtained over time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Reduced human intervention: Because of LB automation, reduced system administration efforts) Tj
T*
(are required in handling failures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Service discovery: An advantage of LBs is that the clients’ requests are forwarded to) Tj
T*
(appropriate hosting servers by inquiring about the service registry.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Security: LBs may also improve security by mitigating attacks like denial-of-service \(DoS\) at) Tj
T*
(different layers of the OSI model \(layers 3, 4, and 7\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(As a whole, load balancers provide flexibility, reliability, redundancy, and efficiency to the) Tj
T*
(overall design of the system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(The heartbeat protocol is a way of identifying failures in distributed systems. Using this) Tj
T*
(protocol, every node in a cluster periodically reports its health to a monitoring service.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
