T*
(Question) Tj
T*
(What if load balancers fail? Are they not a single point of failure \(SPOF\)?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(Load balancers are usually deployed in pairs as a means of disaster recovery. If one load) Tj
T*
(balancer fails, and there’s nothing to failover to, the overall service will go down.) Tj
T*
(Generally, to maintain high availability, enterprises use clusters of load balancers that use) Tj
T*
(heartbeat communication to check the health of load balancers at all times. On failure of) Tj
T*
(primary LB, the backup can take over. But, if the entire cluster fails, manual rerouting can) Tj
T*
(also be performed in case of emergencies.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
