T*
() Tj
T*
(## Monitor Client-side Errors/Design of a Client-side Monitoring System/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Design of a Client-side Monitoring System) Tj
T*
(A service has no visibility of the errors that don’t occur at its infrastructure. Still, such) Tj
T*
(failures are equally frustrating for the customers, and they might have to ask their friends,) Tj
T*
(“Is the service X down for you as well?” or head to sites like Downdetector to see if anyone) Tj
T*
(else is reporting the same issues. They might report the problem via a Tweet or some other) Tj
T*
(communication channel. However, all such cases have a slow feedback loop. As a service) Tj
T*
(provider, we want to detect such problems as quickly as possible to take remedial measures.) Tj
T*
(Let’s design such a system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Initial design) Tj
T*
(To ensure that the client’s requests reach the server, we’ll act as clients and perform) Tj
T*
(reachability and health checks. We’ll need various vantage points across the globe. We can run) Tj
T*
(a service, let’s call it prober, that periodically sends requests to the service to check) Tj
T*
(availability. This way, we can monitor reachability to our service from many different places.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Prober checking availability of website]\(./probe.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Issues with probers) Tj
T*
(We can have the following issues with probers:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Incomplete coverage: We might not have good coverage across all autonomous systems. There are) Tj
T*
(100,000 unique autonomous systems on the Internet as of March 2021. It’s not cost-effective or) Tj
T*
(even possible to put those many probes across the globe. Country or ISP-specific regulations) Tj
T*
(and the need for periodic maintenance are additional hurdles to implementing such a scheme.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
