() Tj
T*
(## Protect user privacy) Tj
T*
(The human user who uses the client-side software should be in full control to precisely know) Tj
T*
(what data is collected and sent with each request. The user should also be able to reactivate) Tj
T*
(the feature any time they wish. If we use our client-side application \(and not a browser) Tj
T*
(application\), we have a lot of flexibility in what diagnostic could be included in the report.) Tj
T*
(For a browser-based client, we can avoid the following information:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- We can avoid including traceroute hops to see a client to the service path. Users can be) Tj
T*
(susceptible to their geographic location. It might be akin to collecting location information.) Tj
T*
(- We can avoid including which DNS resolver is being used. Again, details of DNS can leak some) Tj
T*
(information about the location.) Tj
T*
(- We can avoid including round-trip-time \(RTT\) and packet loss information.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: As a guiding rule, we should try to collect as little information as possible, and it) Tj
T*
(must only be used for the specific purpose a user gave consent for.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Ideally, for a web-based client, we should only collect the information that’s logged in the) Tj
T*
(weblog when any request has been successful.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We shouldn’t use any active probing except to test the service’s standard functionality and) Tj
T*
(report such probes’ results. So, traceroute and RTT or packet loss information is excluded.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Any intermediary \(like ISPs or middleboxes\) can’t change, add, or remove the error reporting) Tj
T*
(mechanism due to encryption. Similarly, designated collectors are the only place where such) Tj
T*
(data can go.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Conclusion) Tj
T*
(In a distributed system, it’s difficult to detect and respond to errors on the client side. So,) Tj
T*
(it’s necessary to monitor such events to provide a good user experience.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We can handle errors using an independent agent that sends service reports about any failures) Tj
T*
(to a collector. Such collectors should be independent of the primary service in terms of) Tj
T*
(infrastructure and deployment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Monitor Client-side Errors/Focus on Client-side Errors in a Monitoring System/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Focus on Client-side Errors in a Monitoring System) Tj
T*
(## Client-side errors) Tj
T*
(In a distributed system, clients often access the service via an HTTP request. We can monitor) Tj
T*
(our web and application servers’ logs if a request fails to process. If multiple requests fail,) Tj
T*
(we can observe a spike in internal errors \(error 500\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
