(# Detailed Design of a Monitoring System) Tj
T*
(We’ll discuss the core components of our monitoring system, identify the shortcomings of our) Tj
T*
(design, and improve the design to fulfill our requirements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Storage) Tj
T*
(We’ll use time-series databases to save the data locally on the server where our monitoring) Tj
T*
(service is running. Then, we’ll integrate it with a separate storage node. We’ll use blob) Tj
T*
(storage to store our metrics.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We need to store metrics and know which action to perform if a metric has reached a particular) Tj
T*
(value. For example, if CPU usage exceeds 90%, we generate an alert to the end user so the alert) Tj
T*
(receiver can do take the necessary steps, such as allocate more resources to scale. For this) Tj
T*
(purpose, we need another storage area that will contain the rules and actions. Let’s call it a) Tj
T*
(rules databse. Upon any violation of the rules, we can take appropriate action.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Here, we have identified two more components in our design—that is, a rules and action database) Tj
T*
