(Question 1) Tj
T*
(What happens if a local or global monitoring system is down?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(We can store the data locally and wait for the system to be up and running again. But there’s a) Tj
T*
(limit for the local data storage. So, either we delete previous data or we don’t store new) Tj
T*
(data. To make a decision, relevant policies need to be created.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question 2) Tj
T*
(How can a monitoring system reliably work if it uses the same infrastructure in a data center) Tj
T*
(that it was supposed to monitor? Consider this given that a failure of a network in a data) Tj
T*
(center can knock out the monitoring components.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(The actual deployment of a monitoring system needs special care. We might have an internal,) Tj
T*
(monitoring-specific network to isolate it from the common network. We should use a separate) Tj
T*
(instance of blob stores and other services.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(It also helps to have external components to the monitoring, where external might mean an) Tj
T*
(independent service provider’s infrastructure. However, designing such a system is complex and) Tj
T*
(is more expensive.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Humans need to consume enormous amounts of data, and even after different kinds of data) Tj
T*
(summarizations, the data can still be huge. Next, we’ll tackle how to present enormous data to) Tj
T*
(human administrators.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Monitor Server-side Errors/Visualize Data in a Monitoring System/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Visualize Data in a Monitoring System) Tj
T*
(Large data centers have millions of servers, and visualizing the health data for all of them is) Tj
T*
(challenging. An important aspect of monitoring a fleet of servers is to know which ones are) Tj
T*
(alive and which ones are offline. A modern data center can house many thousands of servers in a) Tj
T*
(building. We can use a heat map to display information about thousands of servers compactly in) Tj
T*
(a data center.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A heat map is a data visualization technique that shows the magnitude of a phenomenon in two) Tj
T*
(dimensions by using colors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Using heat maps to troubleshoot) Tj
T*
(We’ll identify if a server is down by using heat maps. Each rack of servers is named and is) Tj
T*
(sorted by data center, then cluster, then row, so problems common at any of these levels are) Tj
T*
(readily apparent.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A heat map depicting the operational state of a large number of components is an effective) Tj
T*
(method. The health of each component is indicated by the color of each cell in a big matrix.) Tj
T*
(Nodes with green cells operate within permitted parameters, while nodes with red cells are) Tj
T*
(nonresponsive on multiple tries.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Below, we have a heat map displaying the server’s state.) Tj
T*
() Tj
