T*
() Tj
T*
([The consumers can read anywhere from the file. Producers add to the end of file]\(./2.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The broker solved the problems that our first design had. We avoided a large number of queues) Tj
T*
(by partitioning the topic. We introduced parallelism using partitions that avoided bottlenecks) Tj
T*
(while consuming the message.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Cluster manager) Tj
T*
(We’ll have multiple brokers in our cluster. The cluster manager will perform the following) Tj
T*
(tasks:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Broker and topics registry: This stores the list of topics for each broker.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Manage replication: The cluster manager manages replication by using the leader-follower) Tj
T*
(approach. One of the brokers is the leader. If it fails, the manager decides who the next) Tj
T*
(leader is. In case the follower fails, it adds a new broker and makes sure to turn it into an) Tj
T*
(updated follower. It updates the metadata accordingly. We’ll keep three replicas of each) Tj
T*
(partition on different brokers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Replication at the partitioning level]\(./replication.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Consumer manager) Tj
T*
(The consumer manager will manage the consumers. It has the following responsibilities:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Verify the consumer: The manager will fetch the data from the database and verify if the) Tj
T*
(consumer is allowed to read a certain message. For example, if the consumer has subscribed to) Tj
T*
(Topic A \(but not to Topic B\), then it should not be allowed to read from Topic B. The consumer) Tj
T*
(manager verifies the consumer’s request.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Retention time management: The manager will also verify if the consumer is allowed to read) Tj
T*
(the specific message or not. If, according to its retention time, the message should be) Tj
T*
(inaccessible to the consumer, then it will not allow the consumer to read the message.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Message receiving options management: There are two methods for consumers to get data. The) Tj
T*
(first is that our system pushes the data to its consumers. This method may result in) Tj
T*
(overloading the consumers with continuous messages. Another approach is for consumers to) Tj
T*
(request the system to read data from a specific topic. The drawback is that a few consumers) Tj
T*
(might want to know about a message as soon as it is published, but we do not support this) Tj
T*
(function.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Therefore, we’ll support both techniques. Each consumer will inform the broker that it wants) Tj
T*
(the data to be pushed automatically or it needs the data to read itself. We can avoid) Tj
T*
(overloading the consumer and also provide liberty to the consumer. We’ll save this information) Tj
T*
(in the relational database along with other consumer details.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Allow multiple reads: The consumer manager stores the offset information of each consumer.) Tj
T*
(We’ll use a key-value to store offset information against each consumer. It allows fast) Tj
T*
(fetching and increases the availability of the consumers. If Consumer 1 has read from offset 0) Tj
T*
(and has sent the acknowledgment, we’ll store it. So, when the consumer wants to read again, we) Tj
T*
(can provide the next offset to the reader for reading the message.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Finalized design) Tj
T*
(The finalized design of our pub-sub system is shown below.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
