T*
(There are numerous use cases of a pub-sub. Due to decoupling between producers and consumers,) Tj
T*
(the system can scale dynamically, and the failures are well-contained. Additionally, due to) Tj
T*
(proper accounting of data consumption, the pub-sub is a system of choice for a large-scale) Tj
T*
(system that produces enormous data. We can determine precisely which data is needed and not) Tj
T*
(needed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Pub-sub/Introduction to Pub-sub/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Introduction to Pub-sub) Tj
T*
(Pub-sub messaging offers asynchronous communication. Let’s explore the use cases where it is) Tj
T*
(beneficial to have a pub-sub system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Use cases of pub-sub) Tj
T*
(A few use cases of pub-sub are listed below:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Improved performance: The pub-sub system enables push-based distribution, alleviating the) Tj
T*
(need for message recipients to check for new information and changes regularly. It encourages) Tj
T*
(faster response times and lowers the delivery latency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Handling ingestion: The pub-sub helps in handling log ingestion. The user-interaction data) Tj
T*
(can help us figure out useful analyses about the behavior of users. We can ingest a large) Tj
T*
(amount of data to the pub-sub system, so much so that it can deliver the data to any analytical) Tj
T*
(system to understand the behavior patterns of users. Moreover, we can also log the details of) Tj
T*
(the event that’s happening while completing a request from the user. Large services like Meta) Tj
T*
(use a pub-sub system called Scribe to know exactly who needs what data, and remove or archive) Tj
T*
(processed or unwanted data. Doing this is necessary to manage an enormous amount of data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Real-time monitoring: Raw or processed messages of an application or system can be provided) Tj
T*
(to multiple applications to monitor a system in real time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Replicating data: The pub-sub system can be used to distribute changes. For example, in a) Tj
T*
(leader-follower protocol, the leader sends the changes to its followers via a pub-sub system.) Tj
T*
(It allows followers to update their data asynchronously. The distributed caches can also) Tj
T*
(refresh themselves by receiving the modifications asynchronously. Along the same lines,) Tj
T*
(applications like WhatsApp that allow multiple views of the same conversation—for example, on a) Tj
T*
(mobile phone and a computer’s browser—can elegantly work using a pub-sub, where multiple views) Tj
T*
(can act either as a publisher or a subscriber.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Log ingestion refers to importing logs into a database for immediate use, such as monitoring.) Tj
T*
(Huge applications like Facebook produce massive amounts of data and logs. Real-time fetching) Tj
T*
(and processing of logs allow us to run analysis and take quick actions in case of failures.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Motivation and use cases of the pub-sub system]\(./real-time.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question 1) Tj
T*
(What are the similarities and differences between a pub-sub system and queues?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(The pub-sub system and queues are similar because they deliver information that’s produced by) Tj
T*
(the producer to the consumer. The difference is that only one consumer consumes a message in) Tj
T*
(the queue, while there can be multiple consumers of the same message in a pub-sub system.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question 2) Tj
T*
