(How are producers and consumers decoupled from one another in a pub-sub system?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(Producers don’t know who’ll end up reading their information. They just send it to the system,) Tj
T*
(and it is read by the consumer. Producers are not affected by slow consumers, the count of) Tj
T*
(consumers, or the failure of consumers. We can scale them independently.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(## Requirements) Tj
T*
(We aim to design a pub-sub system that has the following requirements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Functional requirements) Tj
T*
(Let’s specify the functional requirements of a pub-sub system:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Create a topic: The producer should be able to create a topic.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Write messages: Producers should be able to write messages to the topic.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Subscription: Consumers should be able to subscribe to the topic to receive messages.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Read messages: The consumer should be able to read messages from the topic.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Specify retention time: The consumers should be able to specify the retention time after) Tj
T*
(which the message should be deleted from the system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(A topic is a collection of related events or messages. The producers can create a topic and) Tj
T*
(write the message into a topic. Consumers can subscribe to a topic and read from that topic.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Delete messages: A message should be deleted from the topic or system after a certain) Tj
T*
(retention period as defined by the user of the system.) Tj
T*
(### Non-functional requirements) Tj
T*
(We consider the following non-functional requirements when designing a pub-sub system:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Scalable: The system should scale with an increasing number of topics and increasing writing) Tj
T*
(\(by producers\) and reading \(by consumers\) load.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Available: The system should be highly available, so that producers can add their data and) Tj
T*
(consumers can read data from it anytime.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Durability: The system should be durable. Messages accepted from producers must not be lost) Tj
T*
(and should be delivered to the intended subscribers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Fault tolerance: Our system should be able to operate in the event of failures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Concurrent: The system should handle concurrency issues where reading and writing are) Tj
T*
(performed simultaneously.) Tj
T*
(## API Design) Tj
