(## Building blocks we will use) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The design of pub-sub utilizes many building blocks that have been discussed in the initial) Tj
T*
(chapters. We’ll consider the following lessons on building blocks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The building blocks we’ll use]\(./bb.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Database: We’ll use databases to store information like subscription details.) Tj
T*
(- Distributed messaging queue: We’ll use use a messaging queue to store messages sent by the) Tj
T*
(producer.) Tj
T*
(- Key-value: We’ll use a key-value store to hold information about consumers.) Tj
T*
(In the next lesson, we’ll focus on designing a pub-sub system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Pub-sub/System Design The Pub-sub Abstraction/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# System Design: The Pub-sub Abstraction) Tj
T*
(## What is a pub-sub system?) Tj
T*
(Publish-subscribe messaging, often known as pub-sub messaging, is an asynchronous service-to-) Tj
T*
(service communication method that’s popular in serverless and microservices architectures.) Tj
T*
(Messages can be sent asynchronously to different subsystems of a system using the pub-sub) Tj
T*
(system. All the services subscribed to the pub-sub model receive the message that’s pushed into) Tj
T*
(the system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For example, when Cristiano Ronaldo, a famous athlete, posts on Instagram or shares a tweet,) Tj
T*
(all of his followers are updated. Here, Cristiano Ronaldo is the publisher, his post or tweet) Tj
T*
(is the message, and all of his followers are subscribers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The pub-sub system]\(./Pub-sub-sys.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Motivation) Tj
T*
(The hardware infrastructure of distributed systems consists of millions of machines. Using a) Tj
T*
(pub-sub system to communicate asynchronously increases scalability. Producers and consumers are) Tj
T*
(disconnected and operate independently, thereby allowing us to scale and develop them) Tj
T*
(separately. The decoupling between components, producers and consumers, allows greater) Tj
T*
(scalability because adding or removing any component doesn’t affect the other components.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## How do we design a pub-sub system?) Tj
T*
(We have divided the pub-sub system design into the following lessons:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Introduction: In this lesson, we learn about the use cases of the pub-sub system, define its) Tj
T*
(requirements, and design the API for it.) Tj
T*
(2. Design: In this lesson, we discuss two designs of the pub-sub system, one with messaging) Tj
T*
(queues and the other with a broker.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Grokking-Modern-System-Design-Interview) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Content here is extracted from the same-named course by Educative.io for previews only. To) Tj
T*
(achieve better study efficiency and study complete course contents, please buy membership of) Tj
T*
(Educative.io.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([the course]\(./system_design_course.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Rate Limiter/Design of a Rate Limiter/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
