(## Rate Limiter/System Design The Rate Limiter/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# System Design: The Rate Limiter) Tj
T*
(## What is a rate limiter?) Tj
T*
(A rate limiter, as the name suggests, puts a limit on the number of requests a service) Tj
T*
(fulfills. It throttles requests that cross the predefined limit. For example, a client using a) Tj
T*
(particular service’s API that is configured to allow 500 requests per minute would block) Tj
T*
(further incoming requests for the client if the number of requests the client makes exceeds) Tj
T*
(that limit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Why do we need a rate limiter?) Tj
T*
(A rate limiter is generally used as a defensive layer for services to avoid their excessive) Tj
T*
(usage, whether intended or unintended. It also protects services against abusive behaviors that) Tj
T*
(target the application layer, such as denial-of-service \(DOS\) attacks and brute-force password) Tj
T*
(attempts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Below, we have a list of scenarios where rate limiters can be used to make the service more) Tj
T*
(reliable.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Preventing resource starvation: Some denial of service incidents are caused by errors in) Tj
T*
(software or configurations in the system, which causes resource starvation. Such attacks are) Tj
T*
(referred to as friendly-fire denial of service. One of the common use cases of rate limiters is) Tj
T*
(to avoid resource starvation caused by such denial of service attacks, whether intentional or) Tj
T*
(unintentional.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Managing policies and quotas: There is also a need for rate limiters to provide a fair and) Tj
T*
(reasonable use of resources’ capacity when they are shared among many users. The policy refers) Tj
T*
(to applying limits on the time duration or quantity allocated \(quota\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Controlling data flow: Rate limiters could also be used in systems where there is a need to) Tj
T*
(process a large amount of data. Rate limiters control the flow of data to distribute the work) Tj
T*
(evenly among different machines, avoiding the burden on a single machine.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Avoiding excess costs: Rate limiting can also be used to control the cost of operations. For) Tj
T*
(example, organizations can use rate limiting to prevent experiments from running out of control) Tj
T*
(and avoid large bills. Some cloud service providers also use this concept by providing freemium) Tj
T*
(services to certain limits, which can be increased on request by charging from users.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Throttling the number of requests to API servers via a rate limiter]\(./sys.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## How will we design a rate limiter?) Tj
T*
(In the following lessons, we will learn about the following:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Requirements: This is where we discuss the functional and non-functional requirements of the) Tj
T*
(rate limiter. We also describe the types of throttling and locations where a rate limiter can) Tj
T*
(be placed to perform its functions efficiently.) Tj
T*
(2. High-level design: In this section, we look at the high-level design to provide an overview) Tj
T*
(of a rate limiter.) Tj
T*
(3. Detailed design: In this section, we discuss the detailed design of a rate limiter and) Tj
T*
(explain various building blocks involved in the detailed design.) Tj
T*
(4. Rate limiter algorithms: In this lesson, we explain different algorithms that play a vital) Tj
T*
(role in the operations of a rate limiter.) Tj
T*
(5. Quiz: To assess your understanding of rate limiters, we’ve provided a quiz at the end of) Tj
T*
(this chapter.) Tj
T*
(In the next lesson, let’s start by understanding the requirements and design of a rate limiter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
