(## Sharded Counters/System Design The Sharded Counters/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# System Design: The Sharded Counters) Tj
T*
(## Problem statement) Tj
T*
(Real-time applications like Facebook, Twitter, and YouTube have high user traffic. Users) Tj
T*
(interact with the applications and perform multiple operations \(view, like, comment, and so on\)) Tj
T*
(depending on the application’s structure. For instance, an image is posted on a Facebook page) Tj
T*
(that has millions of followers, and the post’s likes rapidly increase after each millisecond.) Tj
T*
(Here, it might be easy to count the likes for this single image, but what will we do when) Tj
T*
(thousands of such images or videos are uploaded simultaneously by many celebrities, each with) Tj
T*
(millions of followers. This problem is known as the heavy hitters problem.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The above scenario shows how a simple counting operation becomes challenging to manage with) Tj
T*
(precision and performance. The following figure shows YouTube’s videos that were viewed by) Tj
T*
(millions of users in a 24-hour span in August 2021:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([YouTube videos' views in 24 hours]\(./views.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(On average, six thousand tweets are sent on Twitter within one second, which equals 360,000) Tj
T*
(tweets per minute and about 500 million tweets per day. A challenging task is to handle) Tj
T*
(billions of likes on these 500 million tweets per day. The following table shows the most liked) Tj
T*
(tweets in one day as of 2022:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Most liked tweets in a single day]\(./likes.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(How will we handle millions of write requests coming against the likes on thousands of tweets) Tj
T*
(per minute? The challenge is that writing takes more time than reading, and concurrent activity) Tj
T*
(makes this problem harder. As the number of concurrent writes increases for some counter \(which) Tj
T*
(might be a variable residing in a node’s memory\), the lock contention increases non-linearly.) Tj
T*
(After some point, we might spend most of the time acquiring the lock so that we could safely) Tj
T*
(update the counter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
