(## Spectacular Failures/AWS Kinesis Outage Affecting Many Organizations/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# AWS Kinesis Outage Affecting Many Organizations) Tj
T*
(Amazon Kinesis allows us to aggregate, process, and analyze real-time streaming data to get) Tj
T*
(timely insights and react quickly to the information it provides. It continuously captures) Tj
T*
(gigabytes of data from hundreds of thousands of sources per second. The Kinesis service’s) Tj
T*
(frontend handles authentication, throttling, and distributes workloads to its back-end) Tj
T*
(“workhorse” cluster via database sharding. On November 25, 2020, the Amazon Kinesis service was) Tj
T*
(disrupted in the US-East-1 \(Northern Virginia\) region, affecting thousands of other third-party) Tj
T*
(services. The failure was significant enough to take out a large portion of Internet services.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Sequence of events) Tj
T*
(- According to Amazon, the event was triggered by adding a small capacity to the AWS front-end) Tj
T*
(fleet of servers, scheduled from 2:44 a.m. PST to 3:47 a.m. PST.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- The addition of the new capacity caused all the servers in the fleet to exceed the maximum) Tj
T*
(number of threads that are allowed by an operating system configuration.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Due to exceeding the limit on threads, cache construction was failing to complete, and front-) Tj
T*
(end servers were ending with useless shard maps that left them unable to route requests to) Tj
T*
(back-end clusters.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Other primary Amazon services also stopped working, including Amazon Cognito and CloudWatch.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  - Kinesis Data Streams is used by Amazon Cognito to gather and analyze API usage patterns.) Tj
T*
(Because of the long-running issue with Kinesis Data Streams, a hidden error in the buffering) Tj
T*
(code—which is required for Cognito services—caused the Cognito web servers to start blocking on) Tj
T*
(the backlogged Kinesis Data Stream buffers. As a result, Cognito customers witnessed an) Tj
T*
(increase in API failures and latencies for Cognito user pools and identity pools, making it) Tj
T*
(impossible for external users to authenticate or receive temporary AWS credentials.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  - CloudWatch uses Kinesis Data Streams to process metrics and log data. The PutMetricData and) Tj
T*
(PutLogEvents APIs in CloudWatch encountered higher error rates and latencies, and alerts were) Tj
T*
(set to INSUFFICIENT DATA. The great majority of metrics were unable to be processed due to) Tj
T*
(higher error rates and latencies. When CloudWatch was experiencing these greater issues,) Tj
T*
(internal and external clients couldn’t persist all metric data to the CloudWatch service.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Sequence of events]\(./seq.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Due to the problems with CloudWatch metrics, two services were also impacted. First,) Tj
T*
(AutoScaling policies that rely on CloudWatch measurements suffered delays. Second, Lambda) Tj
T*
(experienced the effect. Currently, posting metric data to CloudWatch is required as a part of) Tj
T*
(Lambda function invocation. If CloudWatch is unavailable, Lambda metric agents are meant to) Tj
T*
(buffer metric data locally for a period of time. The metric data buffering became so large that) Tj
T*
(it generated memory congestion on the underlying service hosts utilized for Lambda function) Tj
T*
(invocations, leading to higher error rates.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Increased API failures and event processing delays plagued CloudWatch Events and EventBridge.) Tj
T*
(EventBridge is used by Elastic Container Service \(ECS\) and Elastic Kubernetes Service \(EKS\) to) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
