(drive internal processes for managing client clusters and jobs. This has an impact on new) Tj
T*
(cluster provisioning, existing cluster scaling, and task deprovisioning.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Apart from the service issues, Amazon also experienced delays in communicating service status) Tj
T*
(to their customers. Amazon uses two dashboards for communication with their customers, Service) Tj
T*
(Health Dashboard and Personal Health Dashboard. The Service Health Dashboard informs all) Tj
T*
(customers of events, such as the current one. It was down because of its dependency on Cognito,) Tj
T*
(which was impacted by this event.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Apart from the disruption in the Amazon services, this also had a ripple effect on thousands) Tj
T*
(of third-party online services, applications, and websites. This includes Adobe Spark, Acorns,) Tj
T*
(Coinbase, Washington Post, and hundreds of such services.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Analysis) Tj
T*
(- Complexity of enhancing scalability: We’ve been stressing the need for horizontal scalability) Tj
T*
(in all of our design problems. This outage event shows that in practice, adding more capacity) Tj
T*
(to a serving cluster so that we don’t deny any client requests can be challenging and can have) Tj
T*
(unintended side effects.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- The need for a trained team: Training the production team to deal with such unforeseen) Tj
T*
(situations is a challenging task, but it’s worth it and can result in expedited recovery. In) Tj
T*
(addition, randomly restarting the front-end servers and suspecting that the memory pressure) Tj
T*
(causes the problem alludes to the challenges of reaching the root causes under the stress of) Tj
T*
(time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Reading from authoritative servers during bootstrap: During the bootstrap process, it’s a) Tj
T*
(good idea to take data from the authoritative metadata store rather than from the front-end) Tj
T*
(servers to reduce the impact of such failures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Identification of faults in initial stages: There’s a need for automated processes to) Tj
T*
(identify the causes of failure within the initial stages of its occurrence.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Proper testing mechanisms can reduce the severity of the fault: The new capacity that’s) Tj
T*
(causing the servers in the fleet to exceed the maximum number of threads is a potential bug) Tj
T*
(that should have been fixed earlier than before restarting the servers. This reflects the) Tj
T*
(inability to properly test the system. There should be a kind of simulator to test all cases) Tj
T*
(before deploying additional capacity into the fleet.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Finding potential bugs before planned events: The issue with Kinesis Data Streams triggered a) Tj
T*
(latent bug in the buffering code that caused the Cognito web servers to begin to block on the) Tj
T*
(backlogged Kinesis Data Stream buffers. The potential bugs should be identified and fixed) Tj
T*
(before critical planned events, such as adding capacity or software and hardware maintenance.) Tj
T*
(Adopting automated processes for resource allocation: The Cognito team sought to reduce the) Tj
T*
(effect of the Kinesis faults in the early phases of the event by providing extra capacity and) Tj
T*
(therefore boosting their ability to buffer calls to Kinesis. Instead of manually assigning) Tj
T*
(capacity, there should be an automated system to increase or reallocate capacity in such) Tj
T*
(events.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Lessons learned) Tj
T*
(- Testing: Proper testing and identifying the potential bugs are essential. In this case, the) Tj
T*
(number of threads exceeding a maximum limit defined by the operating system seems to be a) Tj
T*
(possible bug.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Ready operations team: A bug bringing an overall system to a halt is the single point of) Tj
T*
(failure, which is possible in a complex system. The production team should be trained and ready) Tj
T*
(for such events.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Reducing number of servers: To get significant headroom in the thread count used as the total) Tj
T*
ET
