(## Spectacular Failures/AWS Wide Spread Outage/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# AWS Wide Spread Outage) Tj
T*
(## Introduction) Tj
T*
(Several Amazon services and other services that depend on AWS were disrupted by an outage) Tj
T*
(incident that spanned more than eight hours on Tuesday, December 7, 2021, at approximately 7:35) Tj
T*
(a.m. PST. The incident impacted everything from home consumer products to numerous commercial) Tj
T*
(services.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This hours-long outage made headlines in the popular media, such as this one from the Financial) Tj
T*
(Times: “From angry Adele fans to broken robot vacuums: AWS outage ripples through the US.” The) Tj
T*
(outage affected millions of users worldwide, including individuals who were using the AWS) Tj
T*
(online stores and other businesses that relied heavily on AWS for providing their services.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The disruption caused by AWS emphasized the need for a decentralized Internet where services) Tj
T*
(don’t rely on a small number of giant companies. According to Gartner, 80% of the cloud market) Tj
T*
(is handled by just five companies. Amazon, with a 41% share of the cloud computing market, is) Tj
T*
(the largest.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Outages like the one above remind us of famous Lamport’s quip: “A distributed system is one in) Tj
T*
(which the failure of a computer you didn’t even know existed can render your own computer) Tj
T*
(unusable.”) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Sequence of events) Tj
T*
ET
