(- An automated action to expand the capacity of one of the AWS services near the main AWS) Tj
T*
(network elicited unusual behavior from a significant number of customers within the internal) Tj
T*
(network.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- As a result, there was a significant increase in connection activity, which swamped the) Tj
T*
(networking equipment that connected the internal network to the main AWS network.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Communication between these networks got delayed. These delays enhanced latency and failures) Tj
T*
(for services interacting between these networks, leading to a rise in retries and ping) Tj
T*
(requests.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- As a result, the devices connecting the two networks experienced constant overload and) Tj
T*
(performance difficulties.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- This overload instantly affected the availability of real-time monitoring data for AWS) Tj
T*
(internal operations teams, hampering their ability to identify and remedy the cause of the) Tj
T*
(congestion.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Operators relied on logs to figure out what was going on and initially observed heightened) Tj
T*
(internal DNS failures.) Tj
T*
(The following slides show the series of events that led to the outage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Sequence of Events]\(./arch\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Analysis) Tj
T*
(- Hampered AWS services: The networking difficulties affected a variety of AWS services,) Tj
T*
(impacting customers that utilized these service capabilities. Since the primary AWS network) Tj
T*
(remained unaffected, certain client applications that don’t depend on these capabilities) Tj
T*
(suffered relatively minor consequences as a result of this occurrence. AWS users, such as) Tj
T*
(Amazon RDS, EMR, and Workspaces, were unable to generate new resources due to the inability of) Tj
T*
(the system to launch new EC2 instances.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Impaired control plane: Apart from the AWS services, the AWS control planes that are used for) Tj
T*
(establishing and managing AWS resources were also impacted. These control planes take advantage) Tj
T*
(of internal network-hosted services. For example, EC2 instances weren’t affected by this event,) Tj
T*
(but EC2 APIs suffered from increased latency and error rates.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Slow restoration: Since DNS is the basis for all communication across the web, operators) Tj
T*
(focused on moving the internal DNS traffic away from congested areas of the network in order to) Tj
T*
(improve availability. However, since monitoring services were unavailable, operators had to) Tj
T*
(identify and disable major sources of traffic manually. This further improved the availability) Tj
T*
(of services.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Elastic Load Balancers \(ELB\): Current Elastic Load Balancers were unaffected by the incident.) Tj
T*
(However, the rising API error rates and latencies for the ELB APIs resulted in longer) Tj
T*
(provisioning times for new load balancers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Lessons learned) Tj
T*
(- Independent communication system: While the intention of having an internal network that’s) Tj
T*
(separate from the main network is the right idea, they weren’t truly independent. A sequence of) Tj
T*
(events highlighted their dependency. Finding such dependencies is crucial to truly benefit from) Tj
T*
(independent networks for internal service use and external client use.) Tj
T*
(Contingency plan: Although AWS takes measures to prepare its infrastructure for sudden surges) Tj
T*
(in customer requests or power usage, the organization still found itself in a difficult) Tj
T*
(situation due to the unusual severity of the failure. Investing in greater risk-based) Tj
T*
(contingency planning benefits organizations during times of crisis.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Ready operations team: A bug bringing an overall system to a halt is a single point of) Tj
T*
(failure, which is possible in a complex system. The production team should be trained and ready) Tj
T*
(for such events.) Tj
T*
ET
