T*
(# Introduction to Distributed System Failures) Tj
T*
(## Introduction) Tj
T*
(Once in a while, we encounter the failure of a service that’s a household name, and individuals) Tj
T*
(and businesses react to them. As system designers, we might wonder how carefully designed) Tj
T*
(services that have been perfected over years by experienced teams can also fail.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This chapter discusses some of the major failures of well-known services and the measures that) Tj
T*
(can be taken to mitigate such failures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The following two factors contribute to failures:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Diverse users: Most services have a vibrant user community, and as their needs evolve, so do) Tj
T*
(the software products. If a software doesn’t update in the way it provides new features and) Tj
T*
(services, it will become stable over time. However, it might not have the features customers) Tj
T*
