/F1 10 Tf
12 TL
50 780 Td
(pages against a domain in the URL frontier is a strong indicator of a crawler trap. So,) Tj
T*
(limiting the crawl at such a domain will be of utmost importance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The identification process of web crawler traps]\(./id.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Solution) Tj
T*
(Our design lacks details on the responsible crawling mechanism to avoid crawler traps for the) Tj
T*
(identifications described above.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Crawling is a resource and time-consuming task, and it’s of extreme importance to efficiently) Tj
T*
(avoid crawler traps in order to achieve timely and helpful crawling. Once the crawler starts) Tj
T*
(communicating with the server for downloading the web page content, there are multiple factors) Tj
T*
(that it needs to take into consideration, mainly at the HTML-fetcher level. Let’s go over these) Tj
T*
(factors individually.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. The crawler must implement an application-layer logic to counter the crawler traps. This) Tj
T*
(logic might be based on the observed number of web pages exceeding a specified threshold.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The crawler must be intelligent enough to limit its crawling at a specific domain after a) Tj
T*
(finite amount of time or web page visits. A crawler should smartly exit a web page and store) Tj
T*
(that URL as a no-go area for future traversals to ensure performance effectiveness.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. When initiating communication with the web server, the crawler needs to fetch a file named) Tj
T*
(robots.txt. This file contains the dos and don’ts for a crawler listed by the web masters.) Tj
T*
(Adhering to this document is an integral part of the crawling process. It also allows the) Tj
T*
(crawler to access certain domain-specified web pages prioritized for crawling, without limiting) Tj
T*
(its access to specific web pages.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Another essential component of this document is the revisit frequency instructions for the) Tj
T*
(crawler. A popular website might demand a frequent revisit, contrary to a website that rarely) Tj
T*
(updates its content. This standard of websites communicating with the web crawlers is called) Tj
T*
(the Robots Exclusion Protocol. This protocol prevents the crawlers from unnecessarily spending) Tj
T*
(crawling resources on uncrawlable web pages.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The robots exclusion protocol]\(./robots.txt.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(The robots.txt file doesn’t protect crawlers from malicious or intended crawler traps. The) Tj
T*
(other explained mechanisms must handle those traps.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Since each domain has a limited incoming and outgoing bandwidth allocation, the crawler) Tj
T*
(needs to be polite enough to limit its crawling at a specific domain. Instead of having a) Tj
T*
(static crawl speed for every domain, a better approach is to adjust the crawl speed based on a) Tj
T*
(domain’s Time to First Byte \(TTFB\) value. The higher the TTFB value, the slower the server. And) Tj
T*
(so, crawling that domain too fast might lead to more time-out requests and incomplete crawling.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(These modifications in the design will ensure a crawler capable of avoiding crawler traps and) Tj
T*
(hence optimizing resources’ usage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
