T*
(- Service host: This component acts as the brain of the crawler and is composed of worker) Tj
T*
(instances. For simplicity, we will refer to this whole component or a single worker as a) Tj
T*
(crawler. There are three main tasks that this service host/crawler performs:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  1. It handles the multi-worker architecture of the crawling operation. Based on the) Tj
T*
(availability, each worker communicates with the URL frontier to dequeue the next available URL) Tj
T*
(for crawling.) Tj
T*
(  2. Each worker is responsible for acquiring the DNS resolutions of the incoming URLs from the) Tj
T*
(DNS resolver.) Tj
T*
(  3. Each worker acts as a gateway between the scheduler and the HTML fetcher by sending the) Tj
T*
(necessary DNS resolution information to the HTML fetcher for communication initiation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Service host interaction with other components]\(./service_hosts.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Extractor: Once the HTML fetcher gets the web page, the next step is to extract two things) Tj
T*
(from the webpage: URLs and the content. The extractor sends the extracted URLs directly and the) Tj
T*
(content with the document input stream \(DIS\) to the duplicate eliminator. DIS is a cache that’s) Tj
T*
(used to store the extracted document, so that other components can access and process it. Over) Tj
T*
(here, we can use Redis as our cache choice because of its advanced data structure) Tj
T*
(functionality.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Once it’s verified that the duplicates are absent in the data stores, the extractor sends the) Tj
T*
(URLs to the task scheduler that contains the URL frontier and stores the content in blob) Tj
T*
(storage for indexing purposes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Duplicate eliminator: Since the web is all interconnected, the probability of two different) Tj
T*
(URLs referring to the same web page or different URLs referring to various web pages having the) Tj
T*
(same content is evident. The crawler needs a component to perform a dedup test to eliminate the) Tj
T*
(risk of exploiting resources by storing and processing the same content twice. The duplicate) Tj
T*
(eliminator calculates the checksum value of each extracted URL and compares it against the URLs) Tj
T*
(checksum data store. If found, it discards the extracted URL. Otherwise, it adds a new entry to) Tj
T*
(the database with the calculated checksum value.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Dedup testing in action]\(./dedup.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The duplicate eliminator repeats the same process with the extracted content and adds the new) Tj
T*
(webpage’s checksum value in the document checksum data store for future matchings.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Our proposed design for the duplicate eliminator can be made robust against these two issues:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. By using URL redirection, the new URL can pass through the URL dedup test. But, the second) Tj
T*
(stage of the document dedup wouldn’t allow content duplication in the blob storage.) Tj
T*
(2. By changing just one Byte in a document, the checksum of the modified document is going to) Tj
T*
(come out different than the original one.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Blob store: Since a web crawler is the backbone of a search engine, storing and indexing the) Tj
T*
(fetched content and relevant metadata is immensely important. The design needs to have a) Tj
T*
(distributed storage, such as a blob store, because we need to store large volumes of) Tj
T*
(unstructured data.) Tj
