(### Workflow) Tj
T*
(1. Assignment to a worker: The crawler \(service host\) initiates the process by loading a URL) Tj
T*
(from the URL frontier’s priority queue and assigns it to the available worker.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. DNS resolution: The worker sends the incoming URL for DNS resolution. Before resolving the) Tj
T*
(URL, the DNS resolver checks the cache and returns the requested IP address if it’s found.) Tj
T*
(Otherwise, it determines the IP address, sends it back to the worker instance of the crawler,) Tj
T*
(and stores the result in the cache.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(The implementation of the URL frontier—dequeuing the URLs from a FIFO priority queue and) Tj
T*
(enqueuing all the extracted URLs back into the queue rather than crawling them one after) Tj
T*
(another—ensures that we are crawling the web in a breadth-first search \(BFS\) rather than a) Tj
T*
(depth-first-search \(DFS\) manner.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Question) Tj
T*
(Can we use DFS instead of BFS?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Answer) Tj
T*
(We can use DFS when we want to utilize a website’s persistent connection to traverse all the) Tj
T*
(web pages on that specific domain. This saves time as it helps us avoid reconnecting with the) Tj
T*
(same website repeatedly in case the session expires.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(3. Communication initiation by the HTML fetcher: The worker forwards the URL and the associated) Tj
T*
(IP address to the HTML fetcher, which initiates the communication between the crawler and the) Tj
T*
(host server.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Content extraction: Once the worker establishes the communication, it extracts the URLs and) Tj
T*
(the HTML document from the web page and places the document in a cache for other components to) Tj
T*
(process it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Dedup testing: The worker sends the extracted URLs and the document for dedup testing to the) Tj
T*
(duplicate eliminator. The duplicate eliminator calculates and compares the checksum of both the) Tj
T*
(URL and the document with the checksum values that have already been stored.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The duplicate eliminator discards the incoming request in case of a match. If there’s no match,) Tj
T*
(it places the newly-calculated checksum values in the respective data stores and gives the go-) Tj
T*
(ahead to the extractor to store the content.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Content storing: The extractor sends the newly-discovered URLs to the scheduler, which) Tj
T*
(stores them in the database and sets the values for the priority and recrawl frequency) Tj
T*
(variables.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The extractor also writes the required portions of the newly discovered document—currently in) Tj
T*
(the DIS—into the database.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. Recrawling: Once a cycle is complete, the crawler goes back to the first point and repeats) Tj
T*
(the same process until the URL frontier queue is empty.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Note: Because of multiple instances of each service and microservices architecture, our design) Tj
T*
(can make use of client-side load balancing \(see Client-side Load Balancer for Twitter\).) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
