T*
(a suitable frequency. Let’s define this frequency of revisits as two weeks. The crawler) Tj
T*
(revisits all the standard priority URLs every two weeks. Once the crawler visits a URL, it re-) Tj
T*
(appends the same URL into the URL frontier with a default next visit time that’s equal to two) Tj
T*
(weeks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The default revisit-time is application-dependent rather than system-dependent, so we change) Tj
T*
(this variable to cater to our needs. It’s a compelling case of assigning the priority) Tj
T*
(comparator to URLs. Our system can predict the content change on a website using predictive) Tj
T*
(analysis of the previous content changes. This way we can confidently assign the priority and) Tj
T*
(revisit-time to each URL. For example, our analysis might show frequent changes on news) Tj
T*
(websites and our crawler might suggest revisiting them on a high priority after every five) Tj
T*
(minutes.) Tj
