(## Building blocks we will use) Tj
T*
(Here is the list of the main building blocks we’ll use in our design:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Building blocks in high-level design]\(./bb.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Scheduler is used to schedule crawling events on the URLs that are stored in its database.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- DNS is needed to get the IP address resolution of the web pages.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Cache is utilized in storing fetched documents for quick access by all the processing) Tj
T*
(modules.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Blob store’s main application is to store the crawled content.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- The HTML fetcher establishes a network communication connection between the crawler and the) Tj
T*
(web hosts.) Tj
T*
(- The service host manages the crawling operation among the workers.) Tj
T*
(- The extractor extracts the embedded URLs and the document from the web page.) Tj
T*
(- The duplicate eliminator performs dedup testing on the incoming URLs and the documents.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In the next lesson, we’ll focus on the high-level and detailed design of a web crawler.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([The components in a high-level design]\(./components.jpg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Besides these basic building blocks, our design includes some additional components as well:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## System Design Web Crawler/System Design Web Crawler/README.md) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# System Design: Web Crawler) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Introduction) Tj
T*
(A web crawler is an Internet bot that systematically scours the world wide web \(WWW\) for) Tj
T*
(content, starting its operation from a pool of seed URLs. This process of acquiring content) Tj
T*
(from the WWW is called crawling. It further saves the crawled content in the data stores. The) Tj
T*
(process of efficiently saving data for subsequent use is called storing.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(To go or move swiftly about, over, or through in search of something.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Stored URLs that serve as a starting point for a crawler.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(This is the first step that’s performed by search engines; the stored data is used for indexing) Tj
T*
(and ranking purposes. This specific design problem is limited to web crawlers and doesn’t) Tj
T*
(include explanations of the later stages of indexing and ranking in the search engines.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([An overview of the web crawler system]\(./overview.jpg\)) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
