stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
12 TL
50 780 Td
() Tj
T*
(### Additional benefits) Tj
T*
(The additional utilities of a web crawler are as follows:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Web pages testing: We use web crawlers to check the validity of the links and structures of) Tj
T*
(web pages.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Web page monitoring: We use web crawlers to monitor the content or structure updates on web) Tj
T*
(pages.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Site mirroring: Web crawlers are an effective way to mirror popular websites.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Copyright infringement check: Web crawlers fetch content and check for copyright infringement) Tj
T*
(issues.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In this chapter, we’ll design a web crawler and evaluate how it fulfills the functional and) Tj
T*
(non-functional requirements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The output of the crawling process is the data that’s the input for the subsequent processing) Tj
T*
(phases—data cleaning, indexing, page relevance using algorithms like page ranks, and analytics.) Tj
T*
(To learn about some of these subsequent stages, refer to our chapter on distributed search.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(Mirroring is like making a dynamic carbon copy of a website. Mirroring refers to network) Tj
T*
(services available by any protocol, such as HTTP or FTP. The URLs of these sites differ from) Tj
T*
(the original sites, but the content is similar or almost identical.) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(## How will we design a Web crawler?) Tj
T*
(This chapter consists of four lessons that encompass the overall design of the web crawler) Tj
T*
(system:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Requirements: This lesson enlists the functional and non-functional requirements of the) Tj
T*
(system and estimates calculations for various system parameters.) Tj
T*
(2. Design: This lesson analyzes a bottom-up approach for a web-crawling service. We get a) Tj
T*
(detailed overview of all the individual components leading to a combined operational mechanism) Tj
T*
(to meet the requirements.) Tj
T*
(3. Improvements: This lesson provides all the design improvements required to counter) Tj
T*
(shortcomings, especially the crawler traps. These crawler traps include links with query) Tj
T*
(parameters, internal links redirection, links holding infinite calendar pages, links for) Tj
T*
(dynamic content generation, and links containing cyclic directories.) Tj
T*
(4. Evaluation: This lesson provides an in-depth evaluation of our design choices to check if) Tj
T*
(they meet all the standards and requirements we expect from our design.) Tj
T*
(Let’s begin with defining the requirements of a web crawler.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
